{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0])' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.yaml && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\", \"title\"=>\"Share RV32 multiply datapath\", \"category\"=>\"micro_opt\", \"motivation\"=>\"The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\\nevaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Replace the unconditional signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and\\nsigned-unsigned product expressions with one shared 33x33 unsigned modular\\nmultiplier. Select the operands' sign extension from the decoded multiply\\noperation, then select bits [31:0] for MUL or [63:32] for MULH, MULHU, and\\nMULHSU. The low 64 bits of the 33-bit two's-complement product preserve all\\nRV32M result definitions, while removing two large parallel multiplier\\ncones. Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expressions unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>5, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\"=>\"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\"}]}\nid: hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\ntitle: \"Share RV32 multiply datapath\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\n  evaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\n  high-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\n  below its 135 MHz Fmax target.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the unconditional signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and\n  signed-unsigned product expressions with one shared 33x33 unsigned modular\n  multiplier. Select the operands' sign extension from the decoded multiply\n  operation, then select bits [31:0] for MUL or [63:32] for MULH, MULHU, and\n  MULHSU. The low 64 bits of the 33-bit two's-complement product preserve all\n  RV32M result definitions, while removing two large parallel multiplier\n  cones. Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expressions unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
