ruction can consume only one result. This is a\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the unconditional signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and\\nsigned-unsigned product expressions with one shared 33x33 unsigned modular\\nmultiplier. Select the operands' sign extension from the decoded multiply\\noperation, then select bits [31:0] for MUL or [63:32] for MULH, MULHU, and\\nMULHSU. The low 64 bits of the 33-bit two's-complement product preserve all\\nRV32M result definitions, while removing two large parallel multiplier\\ncones. Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expressions unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 306.38, \"delta_pct\": 8.33, \"vs_baseline\": 8.33, \"fmax_mhz\": 137.61, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9816, \"ff\": 1867, \"seeds\": [136.3, 149.12, 137.61], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"err