ranches are taken repeatedly and pay the\\ntwo-younger-instruction redirect cost on nearly every iteration.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage core resolves every conditional branch in EX and normally\\ncontinues fetching PC+4. CoreMark spends substantial time in counted loops,\\nso its backward conditional branches are taken repeatedly and pay the\\ntwo-younger-instruction redirect cost on nearly every iteration.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a combinational backward-taken, forward-not-taken (BTFNT) predictor in\\nIF. For a valid BRANCH encoding with a negative B immediate, fetch will\\nselect the statically computed target instead of PC+4 and carry the\\npredicted next PC with the instruction. EX will compare that prediction with\\nits resolved next PC, redirect and squash only on disagreement. This removes\\nthe recurring loop-back recovery bubbles without adding a RAM-based BTB or a\\npredictor-table timing path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize negative-offset conditional branches, form the B-immediate target, and advance the fetch PC to that predicted target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry predicted-taken and predicted-next-PC metadata through the pipeline bundles to branch resolution.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch IF predictor metadata alongside decoded instruction state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved branch direction and target against prediction, issuing a redirect only for a misprediction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the misprediction signal to flush only wrong-path work while preserving correctly predicted control-flow throughput.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire prediction metadata and misprediction recovery between fetch, execute, and hazard control.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for backward-taken prediction, forward/not-taken fall-through, and final loop-exit recovery.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize negative-offset conditional branches, form the B-immediate target, and advance the fetch PC to that predicted target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry predicted-taken and predicted-next-PC metadata through the pipeline bundles to branch resolution.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch IF predictor metadata alongside decoded instruction state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved branch direction and target against prediction, issuing a redirect only for a misprediction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the misprediction signal to flush only wrong-path work while preserving correctly predicted control-flow throughput.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire prediction metadata and misprediction recovery between fetch, execute, and hazard control.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for backward-taken prediction, forward/not-taken fall-through, and final loop-exit recovery.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 252.17, \"delta_pct\": -10.84, \"vs_baseline\": -10.84, \"fmax_mhz\": 108.67, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4309463, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9601, \"ff\": 1897, \"seeds\": [108.67, 115.59, 101.69], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:58:34.960871Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, -10.84%): A combinational BTFNT predictor that derives the PC update from imem_data puts instruction fetch, branch decode, immediate extraction, and target addition on the IF-to-PC feedback path, so it must be pipelined or decoupled when its Fmax loss exceeds CoreMark's saved redirect bubbles.\"}\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
