{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r2s0.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r2s0.yaml\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r2s0\ntitle: \"Unsigned multiplier with signed corrections\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current shared multiplier still uses a 33x33 signed product to cover\n  all RV32M multiply signedness variants. The high-half forms can instead\n  share a narrower unsigned 32x32 product, with signedness represented by\n  simple 32-bit correction terms. This should reduce the multiply cone on a\n  core whose recent fitness gain came from multiplier datapath simplification.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the sign-selected 33x33 multiplier with one unsigned 32x32 product.\n  Use its low half directly for MUL and its high half for MULHU. For MULH,\n  subtract operand b from the unsigned high half when a is negative and\n  subtract operand a when b is negative; for MULHSU subtract b when a is\n  negative. These modulo-2^32 corrections exactly implement the signed\n  products while avoiding sign-extension bits in the multiplier. Preserve the\n  RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS operations and all division/reminder behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Implement a shared unsigned 32x32 product and RV32M signed-high correction network, retaining existing ALTOPS and division logic.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Add directed and randomized boundary vectors for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU to validate the correction identities.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-001-r2s0\", \"title\"=>\"Unsigned multiplier with signed corrections\", \"category\"=>\"micro_opt\", \"motivation\"=>\"The current shared multiplier still uses a 33x33 signed product to cover\\nall RV32M multiply signedness variants. The high-half forms can instead\\nshare a narrower unsigned 32x32 product, with signedness represented by\\nsimple 32-bit correction terms. This should reduce the multiply cone on a\\ncore whose recent fitness gain came from multiplier datapath simplification.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Replace the sign-selected 33x33 multiplier with one unsigned 32x32 product.\\nUse its low half directly for MUL and its high half for MULHU. For MULH,\\nsubtract operand b from the unsigned high half when a is negative and\\nsubtract operand a when b is negative; for MULHSU subtract b when a is\\nnegative. These modulo-2^32 corrections exactly implement the signed\\nproducts while avoiding sign-extension bits in the multiplier. Preserve the\\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS operations and all division/reminder behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>3, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Implement a shared unsigned 32x32 product and RV32M signed-high correction network, retaining existing ALTOPS and division logic.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\"=>\"Add directed and randomized boundary vectors for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU to validate the correction identities.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
