{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'mul|dsp|synth_gowin|gowin' Makefile fpga cores/bench -g '\"'!experiments/log.jsonl'\"' -g '\"'!worktrees/**'\"' | head -200 && rg -n '\\\\bmul\\\\b|\\\\bmulh|\\\\bmulhu|\\\\bmulhsu' cores/bench/bench programs cores/bench -g '*.S' -g '*.s' -g '*.dump' -g '*.dis' -g '*.lst' 2>/dev/null | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"Makefile:48:# Multi-core: TARGET selects the core under cores/<TARGET>/.\nMakefile:94:# -Wno-MULTITOP: until phase 2's core.sv lands and instantiates everything,\nMakefile:95:# rtl/ legitimately has multiple top modules. Drop this once phase 2 is in.\nMakefile:98:\t  verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+$(RTL_DIR) \\\nMakefile:124:# evaluates the actual MUL/DIV/REM bitvector formulas. SLOW (each\nfpga/scripts/synth.tcl:42:synth_gowin -top core_bench -json $gen_dir/synth.json\ncores/bench/rtl/00_core_pkg_first.sv:2:// Ordered simulation/formal source lists still pass core_pkg.sv explicitly;\nfpga/scripts/nextpnr_run.sh:16:# path; cores/<target>/generated/synth.json for multi-core).\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:32:  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_MUL    = 5'd11;\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:33:  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_MULH   = 5'd12;\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:34:  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_MULHU  = 5'd13;\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:35:  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_MULHSU = 5'd14;\ncores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv:89:            10'b0000001_000: alu_op = ALU_MUL;\ncores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv:90:            10'b0000001_001: alu_op = ALU_MULH;\ncores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv:91:            10'b0000001_010: alu_op = ALU_MULHSU;\ncores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv:92:            10'b0000001_011: alu_op = ALU_MULHU;\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:1:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +8.33%): RV32M multiply variants should share a sign-selected 33x33 product and select the required 32-bit half, since parallel signed/unsigned multiplier cones waste LUTs even though each instruction consumes only one result.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:3:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r2s0 (regression, +20.73%): Replacing a shared 33x33 signed multiplier with a 32x32 unsigned product can regress when MULH/MULHSU require chained conditional 32-bit high-half corrections, because the added subtractor network outweighs any saved multiplier logic on the CoreMark-critical ALU path.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:4:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (improvement, +32.31%): Moving DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a blocking iterative unit removes wide divide/remainder cones from the common EX path, and CoreMark's sparse division use lets the Fmax gain outweigh the rare multi-cycle front-end stalls.\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share RV32 multiply datapath\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\\nevaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\\nevaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the unconditional signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and\\nsigned-unsigned product expressions with one shared 33x33 unsigned modular\\nmultiplier. Select the operands' sign extension from the decoded multiply\\noperation, then select bits [31:0] for MUL or [63:32] for MULH, MULHU, and\\nMULHSU. The low 64 bits of the 33-bit two's-complement product preserve all\\nRV32M result definitions, while removing two large parallel multiplier\\ncones. Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expressions unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 306.38, \"delta_pct\": 8.33, \"vs_baseline\": 8.33, \"fmax_mhz\": 137.61, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9816, \"ff\": 1867, \"seeds\": [136.3, 149.12, 137.61], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:55:35.641639Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +8.33%): RV32M multiply variants should share a sign-selected 33x33 product and select the required 32-bit half, since parallel signed/unsigned multiplier cones waste LUTs even though each instruction consumes only one result.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Unsigned multiplier with signed corrections\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current shared multiplier still uses a 33x33 signed product to cover\\nall RV32M multiply signedness variants. The high-half forms can instead\\nshare a narrower unsigned 32x32 product, with signedness represented by\\nsimple 32-bit correction terms. This should reduce the multiply cone on a\\ncore whose recent fitness gain came from multiplier datapath simplification.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current shared multiplier still uses a 33x33 signed product to cover\\nall RV32M multiply signedness variants. The high-half forms can instead\\nshare a narrower unsigned 32x32 product, with signedness represented by\\nsimple 32-bit correction terms. This should reduce the multiply cone on a\\ncore whose recent fitness gain came from multiplier datapath simplification.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the sign-selected 33x33 multiplier with one unsigned 32x32 product.\\nUse its low half directly for MUL and its high half for MULHU. For MULH,\\nsubtract operand b from the unsigned high half when a is negative and\\nsubtract operand a when b is negative; for MULHSU subtract b when a is\\nnegative. These modulo-2^32 corrections exactly implement the signed\\nproducts while avoiding sign-extension bits in the multiplier. Preserve the\\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS operations and all division/reminder behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a shared unsigned 32x32 product and RV32M signed-high correction network, retaining existing ALTOPS and division logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed and randomized boundary vectors for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU to validate the correction identities.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a shared unsigned 32x32 product and RV32M signed-high correction network, retaining existing ALTOPS and division logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed and randomized boundary vectors for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU to validate the correction identities.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 369.9, \"delta_pct\": 20.73, \"vs_baseline\": 30.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 166.14, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10476, \"ff\": 1875, \"seeds\": [170.44, 145.92, 166.14], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:09:09.962940Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r2s0 (regression, +20.73%): Replacing a shared 33x33 signed multiplier with a 32x32 unsigned product can regress when MULH/MULHSU require chained conditional 32-bit high-half corrections, because the added subtractor network outweighs any saved multiplier logic on the CoreMark-critical ALU path.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:6:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Decoupled iterative divide unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The EX ALU currently instantiates combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU\\nalongside every normal integer operation. Those wide divide/remainder cones\\nconsume LUTs and can constrain the common EX result path despite CoreMark\\nspending almost all of its cycles on ordinary RV32I operations and multiplies.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX ALU currently instantiates combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU\\nalongside every normal integer operation. Those wide divide/remainder cones\\nconsume LUTs and can constrain the common EX result path despite CoreMark\\nspending almost all of its cycles on ordinary RV32I operations and multiplies.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational RV32M divide/remainder implementation with a\\nblocking iterative divide unit that accepts an EX-stage divide instruction,\\nholds front-end issue while it runs, then injects the correctly signed\\nquotient or remainder into the existing EX/MEM path. Keep add/logic/shift\\nand the shared multiplier entirely on the one-cycle EX path. This structural\\nseparation should shorten normal-cycle timing enough to raise Fmax, while\\nthe rare multi-cycle divide latency has little CoreMark IPC cost.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide and remainder datapaths from the fast ALU while retaining the ALTOPS behavior for formal builds.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signed/unsigned restoring iterative divider with start, busy, done, quotient, remainder, and RV32M divide-by-zero/overflow handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU to the divider, hold their EX/MEM advance until completion, and route the selected result into the normal writeback and RVFI payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a divide-busy interlock that freezes younger work without duplicating retirement or disturbing memory-stall behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider request/completion handshake into execute and global pipeline stall control.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Retain fast-ALU checks and add directed RV32M divide/remainder corner cases covering signs, zero divisors, and INT_MIN divided by minus one.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide and remainder datapaths from the fast ALU while retaining the ALTOPS behavior for formal builds.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signed/unsigned restoring iterative divider with start, busy, done, quotient, remainder, and RV32M divide-by-zero/overflow handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU to the divider, hold their EX/MEM advance until completion, and route the selected result into the normal writeback and RVFI payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a divide-busy interlock that freezes younger work without duplicating retirement or disturbing memory-stall behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider request/completion handshake into execute and global pipeline stall control.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Retain fast-ALU checks and add directed RV32M divide/remainder corner cases covering signs, zero divisors, and INT_MIN divided by minus one.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 405.36, \"delta_pct\": 32.31, \"vs_baseline\": 43.33, \"fmax_mhz\": 182.08, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5681, \"ff\": 2226, \"seeds\": [193.35, 179.08, 182.08], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:11:12.351940Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (improvement, +32.31%): Moving DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a blocking iterative unit removes wide divide/remainder cones from the common EX path, and CoreMark's sparse division use lets the Fmax gain outweigh the rare multi-cycle front-end stalls.\"}\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:3:// RV32IM combinational ALU.  Multiply remains on the one-cycle EX path;\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:19:  // All RV32M multiply variants share this one 33x33 two's-complement\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:22:  // product for every variant, while MUL and the three high-half operations\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:24:  logic signed [32:0] mul_a;\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:25:  logic signed [32:0] mul_b;\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:29:  logic signed [65:0] mul_product;\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:35:    // MUL's low half does not depend on signedness; sign-extending both\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:36:    // operands lets it share the same selected datapath as MULH.\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:38:      ALU_MUL, ALU_MULH: begin\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:39:        mul_a = {a[31], a};\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:40:        mul_b = {b[31], b};\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:42:      ALU_MULHU: begin\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:43:        mul_a = {1'b0, a};\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:44:        mul_b = {1'b0, b};\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:46:      ALU_MULHSU: begin\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:47:        mul_a = {a[31], a};\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:48:        mul_b = {1'b0, b};\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:51:        mul_a = 33'b0;\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:52:        mul_b = 33'b0;\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:55:    mul_product = mul_a * mul_b;\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:77:      ALU_MUL:    out = (a + b) ^ 32'h5876063e;\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:78:      ALU_MULH:   out = (a + b) ^ 32'hf6583fb7;\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:79:      ALU_MULHU:  out = (a + b) ^ 32'h949ce5e8;\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:80:      ALU_MULHSU: out = (a - b) ^ 32'hecfbe137;\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:86:      ALU_MUL:    out = mul_product[31:0];\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:87:      ALU_MULH:   out = mul_product[63:32];\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:88:      ALU_MULHU:  out = mul_product[63:32];\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:89:      ALU_MULHSU: out = mul_product[63:32];\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py:26:ALU_MUL    = 11\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py:27:ALU_MULH   = 12\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py:28:ALU_MULHU  = 13\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py:29:ALU_MULHSU = 14\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:3:The ALU is purely combinational for RV32I and multiply operations. The cold\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:15:    ALU_MUL, ALU_MULH, ALU_MULHU, ALU_MULHSU,\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:28:def _mul_expected(op, a, b):\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:29:    \"\"\"Reference RV32M multiply result for each signedness variant.\"\"\"\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:30:    if op == ALU_MULH:\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:32:    elif op == ALU_MULHU:\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:34:    elif op == ALU_MULHSU:\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:38:    return product if op == ALU_MUL else product >> 32\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:128:async def mul(dut):\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:130:    await _check(dut, ALU_MUL, 3, 4, 12)\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:131:    await _check(dut, ALU_MUL, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF, 1)      # (-1)*(-1) low\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:135:async def mulh(dut):\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:138:    await _check(dut, ALU_MULH, 0x80000000, 2, 0xFFFFFFFF)\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:140:    await _check(dut, ALU_MULH, 0x80000000, 0x80000000, 0x40000000)\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:141:    await _check(dut, ALU_MULH, 1, 1, 0)\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:145:async def mulhu(dut):\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:147:    await _check(dut, ALU_MULHU, 0xFFFFFFFF, 2, 1)\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:148:    await _check(dut, ALU_MULHU, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFE)\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:152:async def mulhsu(dut):\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:155:    await _check(dut, ALU_MULHSU, 0x80000000, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0x80000000)\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:157:    await _check(dut, ALU_MULHSU, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF)\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:161:async def shared_multiply_boundaries_and_random(dut):\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:162:    \"\"\"Exercise every sign mode through the shared multiplier datapath.\"\"\"\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:168:    for op in (ALU_MUL, ALU_MULH, ALU_MULHU, ALU_MULHSU):\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:171:                await _check(dut, op, a, b, _mul_expected(op, a, b))\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:180:        for op in (ALU_MUL, ALU_MULH, ALU_MULHU, ALU_MULHSU):\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:181:            await _check(dut, op, a, b, _mul_expected(op, a, b))\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py:11:    ALU_MUL, ALU_MULH, ALU_MULHU, ALU_MULHSU,\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py:63:        (0x023100B3, ALU_MUL),\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py:64:        (0x023110B3, ALU_MULH),\ncores/bench/test/test_d