{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The evidence points to the remaining shared 33×33 multiplier as the likely common-cycle timing limiter: divider removal raised Fmax sharply, while purely combinational multiplier rewrites were counterproductive. I’m proposing a registered, blocking multiplier path that preserves the proven arithmetic form but removes it from ordinary ALU cycles."}}
