{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r3s0.yaml\\\")' && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r3s0.yaml && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r3s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\", \"title\"=>\"Registered shared multiplier path\", \"category\"=>\"micro_opt\", \"motivation\"=>\"The iterative divider removed a cold but very wide arithmetic cone from the\\ncommon EX path and delivered the current best Fmax. The remaining shared\\n33x33 multiplier is still evaluated in the combinational ALU path for every\\ncycle, so its forwarding-to-result cone can now dominate timing even when\\nthe retiring instruction is ordinary RV32I work.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Preserve the validated sign-selected 33x33 multiply arithmetic, but move it\\ninto a small registered blocking multiplier unit. On an RV32M multiply,\\nEX snapshots the fully forwarded operands and operation, stalls younger\\nissue while the unit produces the selected half, then injects one normal\\nEX/MEM result. Ordinary add, logic, shift, address, and branch operations\\nbypass the multiplier entirely. This trades a short fixed latency only for\\nmultiply instructions for a shorter and less congested common EX timing\\npath, analogous to the successful divide isolation without using the\\nregressive unsigned correction network.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>6, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Keep only non-multiply fast ALU operations on the combinational EX result path and retain ALTOPS-compatible operation definitions.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/mul_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Add a registered shared 33x33 sign-selected RV32M multiplier with start, busy, done, and selected-result handshake signals.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Dispatch MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU using snapshotted forwarded operands, hold their EX advance until completion, and inject the completed result into the existing EX/MEM and RVFI flow.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Add a multiplier-busy interlock with the same priority discipline as the divide and memory-stall controls.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Wire multiplier busy status into the pipeline hazard control without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"test/test_mul_unit.py\", \"description\"=>\"Add directed and randomized signedness, high-half, zero, and boundary tests for the registered multiplier handshake and RV32M results.\"}]}\nid: hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\ntitle: \"Registered shared multiplier path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The iterative divider removed a cold but very wide arithmetic cone from the\n  common EX path and delivered the current best Fmax. The remaining shared\n  33x33 multiplier is still evaluated in the combinational ALU path for every\n  cycle, so its forwarding-to-result cone can now dominate timing even when\n  the retiring instruction is ordinary RV32I work.\nhypothesis: |\n  Preserve the validated sign-selected 33x33 multiply arithmetic, but move it\n  into a small registered blocking multiplier unit. On an RV32M multiply,\n  EX snapshots the fully forwarded operands and operation, stalls younger\n  issue while the unit produces the selected half, then injects one normal\n  EX/MEM result. Ordinary add, logic, shift, address, and branch operations\n  bypass the multiplier entirely. This trades a short fixed latency only for\n  multiply instructions for a shorter and less congested common EX timing\n  path, analogous to the successful divide isolation without using the\n  regressive unsigned correction network.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Keep only non-multiply fast ALU operations on the combinational EX result path and retain ALTOPS-compatible operation definitions.\"\n  - file: rtl/mul_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a registered shared 33x33 sign-selected RV32M multiplier with start, busy, done, and selected-result handshake signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Dispatch MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU using snapshotted forwarded operands, hold their EX advance until completion, and inject the completed result into the existing EX/MEM and RVFI flow.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a multiplier-busy interlock with the same priority discipline as the divide and memory-stall controls.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire multiplier busy status into the pipeline hazard control without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_mul_unit.py\n    description: \"Add directed and randomized signedness, high-half, zero, and boundary tests for the registered multiplier handshake and RV32M results.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
