{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"if [ -f cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-001-r4s0.log ]; then sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-001-r4s0.log; fi\nif [ -d cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-001-r4s0 ]; then git -C cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-001-r4s0 diff -- rtl/hazard_unit.sv rtl/core.sv test/test_hazard_unit.py; fi\nrg -n 'load_use_hazard|uses_rs|hazard' cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-001-r4s0/rtl cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-001-r4s0/test 2>/dev/null\"","aggregated_output":"Reading additional input from stdin...\n{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"019f4ed2-7a4c-7c20-9ff9-1ea85b96a426\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’ll review the benchmark’s prior micro-optimization experiments, then record one focused, implementation-ready hypothesis in the required location.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/LESSONS.md && rg -n -i '\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\"|category: micro_opt|micro_opt' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/LESSONS.md && rg -n -i '\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\"|category: micro_opt|micro_opt' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +8.33%): RV32M multiply variants should share a sign-selected 33x33 product and select the required 32-bit half, since parallel signed/unsigned multiplier cones waste LUTs even though each instruction consumes only one result.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, -10.84%): A combinational BTFNT predictor that derives the PC update from imem_data puts instruction fetch, branch decode, immediate extraction, and target addition on the IF-to-PC feedback path, so it must be pipelined or decoupled when its Fmax loss exceeds CoreMark's saved redirect bubbles.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r2s0 (regression, +20.73%): Replacing a shared 33x33 signed multiplier with a 32x32 unsigned product can regress when MULH/MULHSU require chained conditional 32-bit high-half corrections, because the added subtractor network outweighs any saved multiplier logic on the CoreMark-critical ALU path.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (improvement, +32.31%): Moving DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a blocking iterative unit removes wide divide/remainder cones from the common EX path, and CoreMark's sparse division use lets the Fmax gain outweigh the rare multi-cycle front-end stalls.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (regression, +0.69%): Removing imem_data from branch prediction is insufficient when a combinational PC-indexed BTB tag match, counter read, and next-PC mux remain on the fetch feedback path; CoreMark's saved loop-back bubbles did not amortize that added front-end cost.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r3s0 (regression, -27.02%): Registering a blocking 33x33 multiplier without splitting its arithmetic only moves the full-cycle product into a new register-to-register cone while adding EX ownership and interlock logic, so it cannot deliver the divide unit's Fmax benefit without real pipelining or iteration.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): A sequential fetch FIFO must index its storage procedurally with runtime read/write pointers; generate-block hierarchy and prefixes are elaboration-time constructs and reject dynamic queue indices before synthesis.\\n1:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"baseline-bench-2d60805\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Baseline retest for cores/bench\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"improvement\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 282.82, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 0.0, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 0.0, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 127.03, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 9563, \\\"ff\\\": 1866, \\\"seeds\\\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T00:46:51.300788Z\\\", \\\"round_id\\\": 0, \\\"slot\\\": 0}\\n2:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Share RV32 multiply datapath\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\\\\nevaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\\\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\\\\nevaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\\\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace the unconditional signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and\\\\nsigned-unsigned product expressions with one shared 33x33 unsigned modular\\\\nmultiplier. Select the operands' sign extension from the decoded multiply\\\\noperation, then select bits [31:0] for MUL or [63:32] for MULH, MULHU, and\\\\nMULHSU. The low 64 bits of the 33-bit two's-complement product preserve all\\\\nRV32M result definitions, while removing two large parallel multiplier\\\\ncones. Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expressions unchanged.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"improvement\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 306.38, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 8.33, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 8.33, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 137.61, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 9816, \\\"ff\\\": 1867, \\\"seeds\\\": [136.3, 149.12, 137.61], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T00:55:35.641639Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 1, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +8.33%): RV32M multiply variants should share a sign-selected 33x33 product and select the required 32-bit half, since parallel signed/unsigned multiplier cones waste LUTs even though each instruction consumes only one result.\\\"}\\n5:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r2s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Unsigned multiplier with signed corrections\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current shared multiplier still uses a 33x33 signed product to cover\\\\nall RV32M multiply signedness variants. The high-half forms can instead\\\\nshare a narrower unsigned 32x32 product, with signedness represented by\\\\nsimple 32-bit correction terms. This should reduce the multiply cone on a\\\\ncore whose recent fitness gain came from multiplier datapath simplification.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current shared multiplier still uses a 33x33 signed product to cover\\\\nall RV32M multiply signedness variants. The high-half forms can instead\\\\nshare a narrower unsigned 32x32 product, with signedness represented by\\\\nsimple 32-bit correction terms. This should reduce the multiply cone on a\\\\ncore whose recent fitness gain came from multiplier datapath simplification.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace the sign-selected 33x33 multiplier with one unsigned 32x32 product.\\\\nUse its low half directly for MUL and its high half for MULHU. For MULH,\\\\nsubtract operand b from the unsigned high half when a is negative and\\\\nsubtract operand a when b is negative; for MULHSU subtract b when a is\\\\nnegative. These modulo-2^32 corrections exactly implement the signed\\\\nproducts while avoiding sign-extension bits in the multiplier. Preserve the\\\\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS operations and all division/reminder behavior.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a shared unsigned 32x32 product and RV32M signed-high correction network, retaining existing ALTOPS and division logic.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed and randomized boundary vectors for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU to validate the correction identities.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a shared unsigned 32x32 product and RV32M signed-high correction network, retaining existing ALTOPS and division logic.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed and randomized boundary vectors for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU to validate the correction identities.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 369.9, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 20.73, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 30.79, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 166.14, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 10476, \\\"ff\\\": 1875, \\\"seeds\\\": [170.44, 145.92, 166.14], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T01:09:09.962940Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 2, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r2s0 (regression, +20.73%): Replacing a shared 33x33 signed multiplier with a 32x32 unsigned product can regress when MULH/MULHSU require chained conditional 32-bit high-half corrections, because the added subtractor network outweighs any saved multiplier logic on the CoreMark-critical ALU path.\\\"}\\n8:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Registered shared multiplier path\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The iterative divider removed a cold but very wide arithmetic cone from the\\\\ncommon EX path and delivered the current best Fmax. The remaining shared\\\\n33x33 multiplier is still evaluated in the combinational ALU path for every\\\\ncycle, so its forwarding-to-result cone can now dominate timing even when\\\\nthe retiring instruction is ordinary RV32I work.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The iterative divider removed a cold but very wide arithmetic cone from the\\\\ncommon EX path and delivered the current best Fmax. The remaining shared\\\\n33x33 multiplier is still evaluated in the combinational ALU path for every\\\\ncycle, so its forwarding-to-result cone can now dominate timing even when\\\\nthe retiring instruction is ordinary RV32I work.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Preserve the validated sign-selected 33x33 multiply arithmetic, but move it\\\\ninto a small registered blocking multiplier unit. On an RV32M multiply,\\\\nEX snapshots the fully forwarded operands and operation, stalls younger\\\\nissue while the unit produces the selected half, then injects one normal\\\\nEX/MEM result. Ordinary add, logic, shift, address, and branch operations\\\\nbypass the multiplier entirely. This trades a short fixed latency only for\\\\nmultiply instructions for a shorter and less congested common EX timing\\\\npath, analogous to the successful divide isolation without using the\\\\nregressive unsigned correction network.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Keep only non-multiply fast ALU operations on the combinational EX result path and retain ALTOPS-compatible operation definitions.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mul_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a registered shared 33x33 sign-selected RV32M multiplier with start, busy, done, and selected-result handshake signals.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Dispatch MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU using snapshotted forwarded operands, hold their EX advance until completion, and inject the completed result into the existing EX/MEM and RVFI flow.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a multiplier-busy interlock with the same priority discipline as the divide and memory-stall controls.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire multiplier busy status into the pipeline hazard control without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_mul_unit.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed and randomized signedness, high-half, zero, and boundary tests for the registered multiplier handshake and RV32M results.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Keep only non-multiply fast ALU operations on the combinational EX result path and retain ALTOPS-compatible operation definitions.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mul_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a registered shared 33x33 sign-selected RV32M multiplier with start, busy, done, and selected-result handshake signals.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Dispatch MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU using snapshotted forwarded operands, hold their EX advance until completion, and inject the completed result into the existing EX/MEM and RVFI flow.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a multiplier-busy interlock with the same priority discipline as the divide and memory-stall controls.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire multiplier busy status into the pipeline hazard control without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_mul_unit.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed and randomized signedness, high-half, zero, and boundary tests for the registered multiplier handshake and RV32M results.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 295.83, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -27.02, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 4.6, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 138.47, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4680666, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 5962, \\\"ff\\\": 2425, \\\"seeds\\\": [138.47, 140.39, 129.3], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T01:35:15.695432Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 3, \\\"