hecks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 5}\n15-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Cold iterative high-half multiply unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The shared signed 33x33 multiplier is present on every EX-stage cycle even\\nthough CoreMark primarily needs the low-half MUL result. The signed and\\nunsigned high-half variants are substantially colder compiler operations,\\nyet their operand-selection and wide-product cone remain on the common\\nALU timing path after divide/remainder have already been isolated.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The shared signed 33x33 multiplier is present on every EX-stage cycle even\\nthough CoreMark primarily needs the low-half MUL result. The signed and\\nunsigned high-half variants are substantially colder compiler operations,\\nyet their operand-selection and wide-product cone remain on the common\\nALU timing path after divide/remainder have already been isolated.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep architectural MUL as a one-cycle unsigned low-32-bit product, whose\\nresult is independent of operand signedness, and dispatch MULH, MULHU, and\\nMULHSU to a blocking iterative high-product unit. The unit snapshots its\\noperands and signedness, performs a shift/add product over multiple cycles,\\nthen injects the required high half through the normal EX/MEM path while\\nyounger issue is interlocked. This removes the 33-bit signed product and\\nhigh-half selection logic from every ordinary EX cycle; the occasional\\nmulti-cycle high multiply should be amortized by the improved Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Make the fast MUL path a low-half unsigned product and remove real high-half multiply selection from the common combinational ALU cone, while retaining the matching ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mulhi_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signedness-aware iterative high-half multiplier with start/busy/done/result handshake and ALTOPS-compatible formal behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU to the new unit, snapshot forwarded operand metadata, and insert its completed result into EX/MEM exactly once.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the long-operation interlock so a high-half multiply freezes younger issue without replaying or duplicating retirements.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the high-half-multiply busy indication into the existing global execute-stall control without changing the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Keep exact low-half MUL checks and add directed MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU signedness and edge-case vectors through the iterative execution path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Make the fast MUL path a low-half unsigned product and remove real high-half multiply selection from the common combinational ALU cone, while retaining the matching ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mulhi_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signedness-aware iterative high-half multiplier with start/busy/done/result handshake and ALTOPS-compatible formal behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU to the new unit, snapshot forwarded operand metadata, and insert its completed result into EX/MEM exactly once.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the long-operation interlock so a high-half multiply freezes younger issue without replaying or duplicating retirements.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the high-half-multiply busy indication into the existing global execute-stall control without changing the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"descr