s/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-003-r3s2/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-68017/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3}\n11:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Decode-aware load-use interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock currently compares a preceding load destination to both\\nraw register-field positions of every fetched instruction. Immediate fields\\nand destination fields are therefore mistaken for source registers, causing\\navoidable bubbles in common CoreMark instruction sequences.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock currently compares a preceding load destination to both\\nraw register-field positions of every fetched instruction. Immediate fields\\nand destination fields are therefore mistaken for source registers, causing\\navoidable bubbles in common CoreMark instruction sequences.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make the load-use hazard detector aware of whether the IF/ID opcode actually\\nconsumes rs1 and/or rs2. Preserve the one-cycle interlock for real dependent\\nconsumers, while suppressing it for operand-immediate ALU operations, loads,\\nJAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, EBREAK, and illegal encodings whose bit fields are\\nnot architectural sources. This removes false bubbles without changing the\\nPC, memory, RVFI, or arithmetic critical paths.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each load-use register comparison with decode-derived rs1/rs2 use bits, retaining existing redirect and bus-stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive and connect IF/ID source-use classification signals to the hazard unit without altering the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed cases proving real load dependencies stall once while immediate and no-source e