hat encode immediates, destinations,\\nor reserved data can therefore create unnecessary bubbles in CoreMark's\\ndense arithmetic and address-generation sequences.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock compares a load destination with both raw register\\nbit fields of every fetched word. Fields that encode immediates, destinations,\\nor reserved data can therefore create unnecessary bubbles in CoreMark's\\ndense arithmetic and address-generation sequences.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the raw-field load-use comparison with an exhaustive, opcode-local\\nsource-use table in the hazard unit. Classify rs1 as live only for OP,\\nOP-IMM, LOAD, STORE, BRANCH, and JALR, and rs2 only for OP, STORE, and\\nBRANCH; gate the corresponding comparisons with these bits and IF/ID valid.\\nKeep every true one-cycle load dependency stalled, including all RV32M OP\\noperations, branches, stores, and JALR. This removes false bubbles without\\nadding work to the fetch or EX arithmetic timing paths.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive exhaustive opcode-local rs1/rs2-use bits from the IF/ID instruction and gate only the load-use comparisons with them, preserving all existing redirect and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Exhaustively test source-use classification for valid RV32IM opcodes, invalid/reserved forms, x0, and every true load dependency so false bubbles are removed without permitting stale operands.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive exhaustive opcode-local rs1/rs2-use bits from the IF/ID instruction and gate only the load-use comparisons with them, preserving all existing redirect and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\", \"descr