costly decode-stage comparator and operand-forwarding network that made the\\nearlier full branch-resolution attempt fragile. Gate the early redirect on\\nID acceptance and give an older EX redirect priority across all stalls.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add ID/EX metadata marking a direct JAL whose fetch redirect was accepted in decode.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize valid direct JAL instructions, form the PC-relative target, and emit an acceptance-qualified early-redirect request while latching its metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate PC-update redirect selection from EX wrong-path output squashing so an accepted decode-stage JAL is retained while the PC advances to its target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress only the duplicate EX redirect for a JAL already redirected in decode; retain JAL result, RVFI pc_wdata, JALR, and branch behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose or qualify the ID acceptance condition so early JAL redirection cannot occur while ID/EX is held or an older EX redirect squashes it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Arbitrate older EX recovery ahead of an accepted decode-stage JAL redirect and wire the split fetch-control paths without changing the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_core.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed JAL call/return, consecutive JAL, load-use hold, dmem-stall, and simultaneous older-redirect cases that check RVFI PC order and return-address writes.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add ID/EX metadata marking a direct JAL whose fetch redirect was accepted in decode.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize valid direct JAL instructions, form the PC-relative target, and emit an acceptance-qualified early-redirect request while latching its metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate PC-update redirect selection from EX wrong-path output squashing so an accepted decode-stage JAL is retained while the PC advances to its target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress only the duplicate EX redirect for a JAL already redirected in decode; retain JAL result, RVFI pc_wdata, JALR, and branch behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose or qualify the ID acceptance condition so early JAL redirection cannot occur while ID/EX is held or an older EX redirect squashes it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Arbitrate older EX recovery ahead of an accepted decode-stage JAL redirect and wire the split fetch-control paths without changing the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_core.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed JAL call/return, consecutive JAL, load-use hold, dmem-stall, and simultaneous older-redirect cases that check RVFI PC order and return-address writes.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 161.77, \"delta_pct\": -62.42, \"vs_baseline\": -42.8, \"fmax_mhz\": 71.86, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4442158, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5736, \"ff\": 2199, \"seeds\": [70.77, 71.86, 73.86], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:44:32.240279Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 8}\nfpga/scripts/synth.tcl:42:synth_gowin -top core_bench -json $gen_dir/synth.json\nfpga/scripts/nextpnr_run.sh:16:# path; cores/<target>/generated/synth.json for multi-core).\nfpga/scripts/nextpnr_run.sh:26:  --timing-allow-fail \\\nfpga/core_bench.sv:6://   1. The CPU's critical path is what gets timed — synthesizing an SoC\nfpga/core_bench.sv:9://      logic. Fmax then has no relation to the re