{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r9s0.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r9s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r9s0\ntitle: \"Precompute PC-relative control targets\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current EX redirect cone forms pc + immediate for every conditional\n  branch and direct JAL at the same time it resolves the branch predicate and\n  selects the next PC. CoreMark frequently executes loop-control branches, so\n  shortening this registered EX-to-PC feedback path can raise Fmax without\n  changing retirement throughput or speculative behavior.\nhypothesis: |\n  Form and register pc + immediate in ID together with the existing immediate\n  and instruction payload, then use that registered value in EX for branch\n  targets and direct-JAL targets. Keep JALR's forwarded rs1 + immediate\n  calculation, branch predicate, redirect timing, misalignment detection, and\n  RVFI pc_wdata semantics unchanged. This relocates a 32-bit adder from the\n  branch decision/redirect path into the earlier ID-to-ID/EX path, where it is\n  independent of forwarding and branch comparison, reducing the critical\n  control-flow cone while preserving the pipeline's current IPC.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a registered PC-relative immediate target field to the ID/EX pipeline payload.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute and latch pc plus decoded immediate atomically with each accepted ID/EX instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered PC-relative target for BRANCH and direct JAL resolution while retaining JALR, traps, redirects, and RVFI behavior.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed positive and negative branch/JAL target, redirect, and misaligned-target tests that check retirement PCs and RVFI pc_wdata.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
