{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/LESSONS.md && rg -n -i '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"|category: structural|structural' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +8.33%): RV32M multiply variants should share a sign-selected 33x33 product and select the required 32-bit half, since parallel signed/unsigned multiplier cones waste LUTs even though each instruction consumes only one result.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, -10.84%): A combinational BTFNT predictor that derives the PC update from imem_data puts instruction fetch, branch decode, immediate extraction, and target addition on the IF-to-PC feedback path, so it must be pipelined or decoupled when its Fmax loss exceeds CoreMark's saved redirect bubbles.\n3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Decode-stage branch resolution\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Restructure the front end so conditional branches resolve in decode using\\nthe register-file read values and explicit bypasses from EX/MEM and WB.\\nRedirect the PC and squash only the fetched wrong-path instruction in the\\nsame decode cycle; retain EX resolution for JALR and preserve a targeted\\nload-to-branch interlock until load data is available. This removes one\\nrecovery cycle for the common backward conditional branch while retaining\\nsingle-retire RVFI ordering and the existing memory interface.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide decode-stage bypass selects so branches compare the architecturally newest operands.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide decode-stage bypass selects so branches compare the architecturally newest operands.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false,