{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; d=YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.yaml\\\"); abort \\\"bad id\\\" unless d[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\\\"; abort \\\"bad category\\\" unless d[\\\"category\\\"] == \\\"structural\\\"; abort \\\"bad impact\\\" unless d.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\").is_a?(Integer); abort \\\"bad files\\\" unless d[\\\"changes\\\"].all? { |c| c[\\\"file\\\"].match?(%r{\\\\A(?:rtl/[\"'^/]+'\"\\\\.sv|test/test_[\"'^/]+'\"\\\\.py)\\\\z}) }; puts \\\"YAML structure verified\\\"' && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"YAML structure verified\nid: hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Decoupled iterative divide unit\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The EX ALU currently instantiates combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU\n  alongside every normal integer operation. Those wide divide/remainder cones\n  consume LUTs and can constrain the common EX result path despite CoreMark\n  spending almost all of its cycles on ordinary RV32I operations and multiplies.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the combinational RV32M divide/remainder implementation with a\n  blocking iterative divide unit that accepts an EX-stage divide instruction,\n  holds front-end issue while it runs, then injects the correctly signed\n  quotient or remainder into the existing EX/MEM path. Keep add/logic/shift\n  and the shared multiplier entirely on the one-cycle EX path. This structural\n  separation should shorten normal-cycle timing enough to raise Fmax, while\n  the rare multi-cycle divide latency has little CoreMark IPC cost.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove real combinational divide and remainder datapaths from the fast ALU while retaining the ALTOPS behavior for formal builds.\"\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: \"Add a signed/unsigned restoring iterative divider with start, busy, done, quotient, remainder, and RV32M divide-by-zero/overflow handling.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Dispatch DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU to the divider, hold their EX/MEM advance until completion, and route the selected result into the normal writeback and RVFI payload.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a divide-busy interlock that freezes younger work without duplicating retirement or disturbing memory-stall behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the divider request/completion handshake into execute and global pipeline stall control.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Retain fast-ALU checks and add directed RV32M divide/remainder corner cases covering signs, zero divisors, and INT_MIN divided by minus one.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
