{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r3s1.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r3s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r3s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r3s1\ntitle: \"Decoupled sequential fetch queue\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current IF stage couples every instruction-bus ready pulse directly to\n  PC advance, so a random imem stall immediately freezes the entire pipeline.\n  CoreMark also has load-use, data-memory, and occasional divide stalls during\n  which sequential instruction bandwidth is otherwise unused.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the single combinational fetch payload with a small sequential\n  instruction FIFO and an independent fetch PC. While decode or execute is\n  stalled, the front end continues to fill unused FIFO entries whenever imem\n  is ready; while imem is temporarily not ready, decode consumes buffered\n  instructions. A redirect atomically invalidates queued wrong-path entries\n  and restarts fetching at the resolved target. This preserves the existing\n  EX-stage branch decision and single-retire RVFI boundary while converting\n  available slack into tolerance of the benchmark's random instruction stalls.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add the fetch-queue payload type and any queue-depth constants needed by the decoupled front end.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the direct PC-to-ID payload with a small sequential prefetch FIFO, separate fetch/consume pointers, ready-qualified fills, and redirect invalidation.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire decode-consume backpressure and existing redirect control to the queued fetch interface without changing the top-level contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Separate decode availability from raw imem readiness so a queued instruction can issue during an imem stall while preserving load, dmem, and divider interlocks.\"\n  - file: test/test_if_stage.py\n    description: \"Add directed queue tests for sequential fill/drain, imem backpressure masking, and redirect flushing of wrong-path entries.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
