 EX result path despite CoreMark\\nspending almost all of its cycles on ordinary RV32I operations and multiplies.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX ALU currently instantiates combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU\\nalongside every normal integer operation. Those wide divide/remainder cones\\nconsume LUTs and can constrain the common EX result path despite CoreMark\\nspending almost all of its cycles on ordinary RV32I operations and multiplies.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational RV32M divide/remainder implementation with a\\nblocking iterative divide unit that accepts an EX-stage divide instruction,\\nholds front-end issue while it runs, then injects the correctly signed\\nquotient or remainder into the existing EX/MEM path. Keep add/logic/shift\\nand the shared multiplier entirely on the one-cycle EX path. This structural\\nseparation should shorten normal-cycle timing enough to raise Fmax, while\\nthe rare multi-cycle divide latency has little CoreMark IPC cost.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide and remainder datapaths from the fast ALU while retaining the ALTOPS behavior for formal builds.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signed/unsigned restoring iterative divider with start, busy, done, quotient, remainder, and RV32M divide-by-zero/overflow handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU to the divider, hold their EX/MEM advance until completion, and route the selected result into the normal writeback and RVFI payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a divide-busy interlock that freezes younger work without duplicating retirement or disturbing memory-stall behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider request/completion handshake into execute and global pipeline stall control.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Retain fast-ALU checks and add directed RV32M divide/remainder corner cases covering signs, zero divisors, and INT_MIN divided by minus one.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide and remainder datapaths from the fast ALU while retaining the ALTOPS behavior for formal builds.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signed/unsigned restoring iterative divider with start, busy, done, quotient, remainder, and RV32M divide-by-zero/overflow handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU to the divider, hold their EX/MEM advance until completion, and route the selected result into the normal writeback and RVFI payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a divide-busy interlock that freezes younger work without duplicating retirement or disturbing memory-stall behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider request/completion handshake into execute and global pipeline stall control.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Retain fast-ALU checks and add directed RV32M divide/remainder corner cases covering signs, zero divisors, and INT_MIN divided by minus one.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 405.36, \"delta_pct\": 32.31, \"vs_baseline\": 43.33, \"fmax_mhz\": 182.08, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5681, \"ff\": 2226, \"seeds\": [193.35, 179.08, 182.08], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:11:12.351940Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (improvement, +32.31%): Moving DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a blocking iterative unit removes wide divide/remainder cones from the common EX path, and CoreMark's sparse division use lets the Fmax gain outweigh the rare multi-cycle front-end stalls.\"}\n9:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Decoupled sequential fetch queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current IF stage couples every instruction-bus ready pulse directly to\\nPC advance, so a random imem stall immediately freezes the entire pipeline.\\nCoreMark also has load-use, data-memory, and occasional divide stalls during\\nwhich sequential instruction bandwidth is otherwise unused.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current IF stage couples every instruction-bus ready pulse directly to\\nPC advance, so a random imem stall immediately freezes the entire pipeline.\\nCoreMark also has load-use, data-memory, and occasional divide stalls during\\nwhich sequential instruction bandwidth is otherwise unused.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the single combinational fetch payload with a small sequential\\ninstruction FIFO and an independent fetch PC. While decode or execute is\\nstalled, the front end continues to fill unused FIFO entries whenever imem\\nis ready; while imem is temporarily not ready, decode consumes buffered\\ninstructions. A redirect atomically invalidates queued wrong-path entries\\nand restarts fetching at the resolved target. This preserves the existing\\nEX-stage branch decision and single-retire RVFI boundary while converting\\navailable slack into tolerance of the benchmark's random instruction stalls.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the fetch-queue payload type and any queue-depth constants needed by the decoupled front end.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct PC-to-ID payload with a small sequential prefetch FIFO, separate fetch/consume pointers, ready-qualified fills, and redirect invalidation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-consume backpressure and existing redirect control to the queued fetch interface without changing the top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate decode availability from raw imem readiness so a queued instruction can issue during an imem stall while preserving load, dmem, and divider interlocks.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed queue tests for sequential fill/drain, imem backpressure masking, and redirect flushing of wrong-path entries.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the fetch-queue payload type and any queue-depth constants needed by the decoupled front end.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct PC-to-ID payload with a small sequential prefetch FIFO, separate fetch/consume pointers, ready-qualified fills, and redirect invalidation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-consume backpressure and existing redirect control to the queued fetch interface without changing the top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate decode availability from raw imem readiness so a queued instruction can issue during an imem stall while preserving load, dmem, and divider interlocks.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed queue tests for sequential fill/drain, imem backpressure masking, and redirect flushing of wrong-path entries.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"build_failed: yosys synth: cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv:62: ERROR: Index in generate block prefix syntax is not constant!\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): A sequential fetch FIFO must index its storage procedurally with runtime read/write pointers; generate-block hierarchy and prefixes are elaboration-time constructs and reject dynamic queue indices before synthesis.\"}\n12:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Procedural decoupled instruction queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Random instruction-memory backpressure currently freezes the PC and decode\\npath immediately, even when a prior fetch could have supplied useful work.\\nThe CoreMark evaluation injects instruction stalls, while load-use, data-memory,\\nand divide waits create opportunities to prefetch sequential instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Random instruction-memory backpressure currently freezes the PC and decode\\npath immediately, even when a prior fetch could have supplied useful work.\\nThe CoreMark evaluation injects instruction stalls, while load-use, data-memory,\\nand divide waits create opportunities to prefetch sequential instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the direct combinational IF-to-ID path with a four-entry instruction\\nqueue driven by a separate fetch PC. Implement its storage as a normal packed\\narray indexed procedurally by runtime read/write pointers, never as generated\\nhierarchy. A ready-qualified fill may run while downstream is interlocked, and\\ndecode consumes an already buffered instruction during temporary imem stalls.\\nOn an EX redirect, atomically discard all queued entries, reset the pointers\\nand count, and restart the fetch PC at the architectural target; no pre-redirect\\ninstruction may reach ID. This converts available front-end slack into\\ninstruction-stall coverage without putting prediction logic on the PC feedback\\npath or changing the single-retire RVFI boundary.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a fetch-packet bundle carrying PC and instruction, plus queue-size and pointer-width constants.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct fetch payload with a four-entry procedural storage array, runtime read/write pointers, occupancy counter, ready-qualified fill, decode dequeue, and redirect flush.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate raw instruction-bus readiness from decode availability so a nonempty queue can feed ID during an imem stall while preserving memory, load-use, and divider interlocks.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-consume permission and queue-empty state through the front end while retaining EX redirect priority and the nret=1 external contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for runtime pointer wraparound, simultaneous dequeue/fill, imem-stall masking, downstream interlocks, and redirect invalidation with PC/RVFI ordering checks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a fetch-packet bundle carrying PC and instruction, plus queue-size and pointer-width constants.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct fetch payload with a four-entry procedural storage array, runtime read/write pointers, occupancy counter, ready-qualified fill, decode dequeue, and redirect flush.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate raw instruction-bus readiness from decode availability so a nonempty queue can feed ID during an imem stall while preserving memory, load-use, and divider interlocks.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-consume permission and queue-empty state through the front end while retaining EX redirect priority and the nret=1 external contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for runtime pointer wraparound, simultaneous dequeue/fill, imem-stall masking, downstream interlocks, and redirect invalidation with PC/RVFI ordering checks.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 330.11, \"delta_pct\": -18.56, \"vs_baseline\": 16.72, \"fmax_mhz\": 155.06, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4697199, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5854, \"ff\": 2299, \"seeds\": [146.35, 158.43, 155.06], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:50:36.434439Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (regression, -18.56%): A four-entry procedural IF queue can lose CoreMark fitness when its pointer/count, dequeue arbitration, and redirect-flush control cost more than the transient imem stalls that prefetch can cover, so front-end decoupling needs measured slack rather than assumed stall hiding.\"}\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +8.33%): RV32M multiply variants should share a sign-selected 33x33 product and select the required 32-bit half, since parallel signed/unsigned multiplier cones waste LUTs even though each instruction consumes only one result.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, -10.84%): A combinational BTFNT predictor that derives the PC update from imem_data puts instruction fetch, branch decode, immediate extraction, and target addition on the IF-to-PC feedback path, so it must be pipelined or decoupled when its Fmax loss exceeds CoreMark's saved redirect bubbles.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r2s0 (regression, +20.73%): Replacing a shared 33x33 signed multiplier with a 32x32 unsigned product can regress when MULH/MULHSU require chained conditional 32-bit high-half corrections, because the added subtractor network outweighs any saved multiplier logic on the CoreMark-critical ALU path.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (improvement, +32.31%): Moving DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a blocking iterative unit removes wide divide/remainder cones from the common EX path, and CoreMark's sparse division use lets the Fmax gain outweigh the rare multi-cycle front-end stalls.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (regression, +0.69%): Removing imem_data from branch prediction is insufficient when a combinational PC-indexed BTB tag match, counter read, and next-PC mux remain on the fetch feedback path; CoreMark's saved loop-back bubbles did not amortize that added front-end cost.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r3s0 (regression, -27.02%): Registering a blocking 33x33 multiplier without splitting its arithmetic only moves the full-cycle product into a new register-to-register cone while adding EX ownership and interlock logic, so it cannot deliver the divide unit's Fmax benefit without real pipelining or iteration.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): A sequential fetch FIFO must index its storage procedurally with runtime read/write pointers; generate-block hierarchy and prefixes are elaboration-time constructs and reject dynamic queue indices before synthesis.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r4s0 (broken, n/a): Decode-qualified load-use detection must classify every architectural source in the same valid/timing domain as operand capture, because suppressing a real dependency lets stale register data reach EX and is caught by RVFI register checks.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (regression, -18.56%): A four-entry procedural IF queue can lose CoreMark fitness when its pointer/count, dequeue arbitration, and redirect-flush control cost more than the transient imem stalls that prefetch can cover, so front-end decoupling needs measured slack rather than assumed stall hiding.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
