{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/LESSONS.md && sed -n '1,220p' schemas/hypothesis.schema.json && rg -n -i 'load.use|load-use|load forwarding|memory.*forward|forward.*load|bypass' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/LESSONS.md && sed -n '1,220p' schemas/hypothesis.schema.json && rg -n -i 'load.use|load-use|load forwarding|memory.*forward|forward.*load|bypass' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +8.33%): RV32M multiply variants should share a sign-selected 33x33 product and select the required 32-bit half, since parallel signed/unsigned multiplier cones waste LUTs even though each instruction consumes only one result.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, -10.84%): A combinational BTFNT predictor that derives the PC update from imem_data puts instruction fetch, branch decode, immediate extraction, and target addition on the IF-to-PC feedback path, so it must be pipelined or decoupled when its Fmax loss exceeds CoreMark's saved redirect bubbles.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r2s0 (regression, +20.73%): Replacing a shared 33x33 signed multiplier with a 32x32 unsigned product can regress when MULH/MULHSU require chained conditional 32-bit high-half corrections, because the added subtractor network outweighs any saved multiplier logic on the CoreMark-critical ALU path.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (improvement, +32.31%): Moving DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a blocking iterative unit removes wide divide/remainder cones from the common EX path, and CoreMark's sparse division use lets the Fmax gain outweigh the rare multi-cycle front-end stalls.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (regression, +0.69%): Removing imem_data from branch prediction is insufficient when a combinational PC-indexed BTB tag match, counter read, and next-PC mux remain on the fetch feedback path; CoreMark's saved loop-back bubbles did not amortize that added front-end cost.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r3s0 (regression, -27.02%): Registering a blocking 33x33 multiplier without splitting its arithmetic only moves the full-cycle product into a new register-to-register cone while adding EX ownership and interlock logic, so it cannot deliver the divide unit's Fmax benefit without real pipelining or iteration.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): A sequential fetch FIFO must index its storage procedurally with runtime read/write pointers; generate-block hierarchy and prefixes are elaboration-time constructs and reject dynamic queue indices before synthesis.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r4s0 (broken, n/a): Decode-qualified load-use detection must classify every architectural source in the same valid/timing domain as operand capture, because suppressing a real dependency lets stale register data reach EX and is caught by RVFI register checks.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (regression, -18.56%): A four-entry procedural IF queue can lose CoreMark fitness when its pointer/count, dequeue arbitration, and redirect-flush control cost more than the transient imem stalls that prefetch can cover, so front-end decoupling needs measured slack rather than assumed stall hiding.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r5s2 (broken, n/a): A registered lookahead BTB must treat its response PC and predicted next PC as a fetch-acceptance transaction, invalidating or holding them consistently across redirects and stalls, or stale predictions can misassociate with conditional branches and violate RVFI control-flow checks.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r6s0 (improvement, +1.51%): Encoding BEQ/BNE and signed/unsigned relational branches from one 33-bit subtract's zero, sign, and borrow flags shares a carry-chain-friendly EX cone, modestly improving CoreMark loop-branch timing without changing redirect behavior.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): A write-behind store buffer must make buffer admission, external write acknowledgement, and RVFI retirement one ordered transaction boundary, since retiring a store while its request can outlive or be overwritten by younger MEM traffic violates architectural load/store ordering and register-state checks.\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 (broken, n/a): A PC-only branch predictor must validate the fetched instruction's branch identity or rely on immutable instruction memory, because formal's per-cycle symbolic imem can reuse a trained PC for a non-branch and make the predictor skip its required PC+4.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:8:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r4s0 (broken, n/a): Decode-qualified load-use detection must classify every architectural source in the same valid/timing domain as operand capture, because suppressing a real dependency lets stale register data reach EX and is caught by RVFI register checks.\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Decode-stage branch resolution\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Restructure the front end so conditional branches resolve in decode using\\nthe register-file read values and explicit bypasses from EX/MEM and WB.\\nRedirect the PC and squash only the fetched wrong-path instruction in the\\nsame decode cycle; retain EX resolution for JALR and preserve a targeted\\nload-to-branch interlock until load data is available. This removes one\\nrecovery cycle for the common backward conditional branch while retaining\\nsingle-retire RVFI ordering and the existing memory interface.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide decode-stage bypass selects so branches compare the architecturally newest operands.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide decode-stage bypass selects so branches compare the architecturally newest operands.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\ng trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Status: failed\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:18 (18)\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed