{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r7s1.yaml\\\")' && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r7s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r7s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\", \"title\"=>\"MEM-to-EX load forwarding\", \"category\"=>\"structural\", \"motivation\"=>\"The present five-stage pipeline unconditionally injects a bubble for every\\nadjacent load consumer, even though the benchmark memory is zero-wait when\\nio_dmemReady is asserted. CoreMark's pointer, list, and matrix kernels use\\nmany load-dependent address and arithmetic chains, so this fixed IPC loss is\\na more direct target than another speculative front-end structure.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Restructure the load-result path so the combinationally extracted MEM-stage\\nload value can bypass directly to the simultaneously executing dependent\\ninstruction in EX. Remove the ordinary one-cycle load-use bubble, but only\\npermit that bypass when the older load is in EX/MEM and dmem is ready; on a\\ndmem stall, retain the existing pipeline hold until the response is valid.\\nThe normal MEM/WB forwarding remains as the fallback for older loads, and\\nRVFI continues to retire the original load and dependent instruction in\\nprogram order. This should improve CoreMark iterations per cycle without\\nadding predictor state or changing the external memory or RVFI contracts.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>6, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Expose the already computed sign/zero-extended load result as a valid-qualified combinational bypass value alongside the registered MEM/WB payload.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM-load forwarding selection that chooses the MEM-stage load bypass instead of the EX/MEM address result.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Accept the MEM-stage load bypass operand and select it for either source before ALU, branch, store-data, and RVFI source-value capture.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Remove the default adjacent load-use bubble while preserving the dmem-ready-qualified full-pipeline hold that prevents a consumer from advancing before its load response exists.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Wire the MEM-stage bypass data and load-valid qualification into execute forwarding and retain existing redirect, divider, and dmem-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"test/test_mem_stage.py\", \"description\"=>\"Add directed load-to-ALU, load-to-branch, load-to-store-data, byte/halfword extension, and delayed-dmem-response cases that verify no stale operand reaches EX or RVFI.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
