\navoidable bubbles in common CoreMark instruction sequences.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make the load-use hazard detector aware of whether the IF/ID opcode actually\\nconsumes rs1 and/or rs2. Preserve the one-cycle interlock for real dependent\\nconsumers, while suppressing it for operand-immediate ALU operations, loads,\\nJAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, EBREAK, and illegal encodings whose bit fields are\\nnot architectural sources. This removes false bubbles without changing the\\nPC, memory, RVFI, or arithmetic critical paths.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each load-use register comparison with decode-derived rs1/rs2 use bits, retaining existing redirect and bus-stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive and connect IF/ID source-use classification signals to the hazard unit without altering the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed cases proving real load dependencies stall once while immediate and no-source encodings with matching bit fields do not stall.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each load-use register comparison with decode-derived rs1/rs2 use bits, retaining existing redirect and bus-stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive and connect IF/ID source-use classification signals to the hazard unit without altering the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed cases proving real load dependencies stall once while immediate and no-source encodings with matching bit fields do not stall.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\n.vcd\\nSBY 22:41:51 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:20