sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire the predictor, metadata path, qualified recovery, and EX training without changing the nret=1 I/O or RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed warm-up, repeated-loop, final-exit, trained-PC non-branch replacement, signature-mismatch, and imem/dmem-stall RVFI PC-sequencing tests.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/last_branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a resettable one-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor holding PC, target, direction, and resolved instruction signature, with EX-advance-qualified training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add fetch prediction-valid, predicted target, and signature-match metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so the prediction remains bound to its fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use only the small registered-PC predictor lookup for the speculative successor and carry its transaction metadata for every accepted fetch without decoding imem data in the PC-select path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch predictor transaction metadata atomically with decoded instruction state across ordinary holds and flushes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve branches architecturally, recover only control-qualified prediction mismatches, and force PC+4 recovery for a predicted hit that is not the trained conditional branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Integrate predictor recovery with redirect, load-use, divide, and memory-stall priorities while ensuring wrong-path payloads cannot advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire the predictor, metadata path, qualified recovery, and EX training without changing the nret=1 I/O or RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.p