{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r9s1.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r9s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r9s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r9s1\ntitle: \"In-order memory completion queue\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The injected dmem backpressure currently freezes every pipeline stage as\n  soon as a load or store reaches EX/MEM. Most stalls are short, but they\n  prevent independent younger ALU work from advancing and make memory\n  handshaking part of the pipeline-wide enable network. The earlier store\n  buffer failed because it allowed a store to retire before the externally\n  ordered transaction completed, not because overlap itself is invalid.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the single coupled MEM/WB boundary with a two-entry in-order\n  completion queue. A memory operation occupies the head entry until its\n  dmem handshake completes; its RVFI record and architectural retirement\n  occur only after that completion. While the head is waiting, one younger\n  non-memory EX result may enter the second entry, but cannot retire early.\n  Loads and stores behind an unresolved memory head remain interlocked, and\n  store data/masks stay stable until acknowledgement. This isolates short\n  dmem waits from EX and decode, preserves strictly ordered RVFI retirement\n  and memory visibility, and avoids putting a dmem-return forwarding cone on\n  the EX path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Define a compact completion-entry payload with execution, memory, and RVFI fields plus explicit ready/valid state for two in-order slots.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Convert the coupled MEM/WB register into the completion-queue producer: hold a memory head until its bus handshake, snapshot its RVFI memory payload, and admit only an ordering-safe younger result.\"\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume only the queue head for register-file writeback and expose a head-retire record so no younger completed instruction can write or retire first.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace blanket dmem pipeline freezing with queue-capacity and memory-order interlocks; preserve load-use, redirect, divide, and bus-stall priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the completion queue, head-only RVFI retirement, writeback, and backpressure controls while retaining the nret=1 top-level contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add delayed-load and delayed-store sequences with independent younger ALU work, dependent accesses, and RVFI-order checks proving ordered retirement and stable requests.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
