{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r2s2.yaml && rg -n \\\"hypothesis\\\\.schema|safe_load|yaml\\\\.\\\" tools schemas Makefile\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r2s2\ntitle: \"PC-indexed dynamic loop predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark repeatedly executes a small set of conditional loop branches. The\n  previous static predictor saved cycles but placed instruction-memory data,\n  branch decode, immediate construction, and target addition on the fetch\n  PC feedback path, causing an unacceptable Fmax regression.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small direct-mapped branch target buffer with a two-bit saturating\n  counter per entry. Fetch indexes it solely with the registered PC; a valid\n  tag match and taken counter select a previously learned target, otherwise\n  fetch falls through. EX continues to resolve every branch and updates the\n  entry with the resolved direction and target, then redirects only on a\n  predicted-next-PC mismatch. This warms up after one taken loop edge while\n  avoiding any io_imemData-to-PC combinational dependency, preserving timing\n  better than BTFNT while removing recurring loop-back recovery bubbles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a small PC-indexed direct-mapped BTB with tags, branch targets, valid bits, and two-bit saturating direction counters; update it only from resolved valid conditional branches.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the fetch/decode and downstream pipeline bundles so EX can compare prediction with the architectural resolved PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Select PC+4 or the predictor target from registered-PC predictor outputs without decoding or using io_imemData on the PC feedback path.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the fetch prediction metadata with each decoded instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the resolved branch next PC with the carried predicted next PC, emit a redirect only on mismatch, and expose resolved-branch training information.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat a prediction mismatch as the control recovery event while retaining existing load-use and memory-backpressure priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate and wire the predictor, EX training path, prediction metadata, and misprediction recovery without changing the nret=1 top-level contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add directed warm-up, repeated taken-loop, final not-taken exit, alias/tag-miss, and bus-stall tests that check PC/RVFI control-flow correctness.\"\ntools/tournament.py:262:    except (jsonschema.ValidationError, FileNotFoundError, yaml.YAMLError) as e:\ntools/eval/test_formal_nret.py:41:    # Some cores (legacy baseline) don't have core.yaml. Treat as default\ntools/eval/formal.py:21:    \"\"\"Read the `nret` field from a core.yaml. Defaults to 2 when the file\ntools/eval/formal.py:32:    y = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:48:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:134:    \"\"\"Write the `current:` section of cores/<target>/core.yaml.\ntools/orchestrator.py:152:    y = yaml.safe_load(yaml_path.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:162:    yaml_path.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(y, sort_keys=False))\ntools/orchestrator.py:365:                    y = yaml.safe_load(candidate.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:446:        hyp = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/orchestrator.py:604:    # Copy and rewrite core.yaml.\ntools/orchestrator.py:606:        y = yaml.safe_load((src / \"core.yaml\").read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:609:     