{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff --check && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; h = YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.yaml\\\"); abort \\\"bad id\\\" unless h[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\\\"; abort \\\"bad category\\\" unless h[\\\"category\\\"] == \\\"predictor\\\"; abort \\\"bad impact\\\" unless h.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\").is_a?(Integer) && h.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"confidence\\\") == \\\"medium\\\"; abort \\\"bad change path\\\" unless h.fetch(\\\"changes\\\").all? { |c| c.fetch(\\\"file\\\").match?(%r{\\\\A(?:rtl/[\"'^/]+'\"\\\\.sv|test/test_[\"'^/]+'\"\\\\.py)\\\\z}) }; puts \\\"YAML and required fields valid\\\"' && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"YAML and required fields valid\nid: hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\ntitle: \"Validated lookahead BTB predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Taken loop-closing branches still discard two younger instructions because\n  resolution occurs in EX. Earlier predictors recovered some cycles but lost\n  Fmax when lookup logic entered the PC feedback loop; the registered\n  lookahead version instead failed because its prediction state was not\n  rigorously aligned across redirects and stalls.\nhypothesis: |\n  Implement a small direct-mapped conditional-branch BTB whose lookup is made\n  for sequential PC+4 and registered before it can influence fetch. A response\n  may redirect only when its recorded query PC exactly equals the current fetch\n  PC; otherwise fetch deterministically falls through and invalidates the\n  stale response. EX trains only resolved valid branches and carries the exact\n  predicted next PC for mismatch recovery. Redirects, instruction stalls, and\n  downstream holds invalidate or preserve the response according to whether\n  the matching fetched instruction was actually accepted. This removes hot\n  loop recovery bubbles while keeping tag comparison, counter read, and target\n  selection out of the PC-to-PC feedback path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact direct-mapped BTB with registered PC+4 lookup responses, query-PC tags, valid bits, and resolved-branch-only target/direction training.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend fetch and pipeline payloads with predicted-next-PC, prediction-valid, and fetch-PC metadata needed to prove response alignment.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume a registered prediction only on an exact current-PC match, issue the next sequential lookahead query, and invalidate stale responses on redirect or non-sequential flow.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch prediction metadata only with an accepted IF instruction so ID/EX cannot pair a branch with a different lookup response.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the resolved architectural next PC with the carried prediction, redirect only on mismatch, and expose precisely qualified conditional-branch BTB training events.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Define predictor-response hold and invalidation priority for load-use, bus, divider, and EX redirect events without changing their existing retirement behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor lookup, response-valid alignment, EX training, and misprediction recovery while retaining the nret=1 external contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add checks for sequential lookahead hits, taken-loop and final-exit recovery, redirect-stale-response suppression, imem stalls, and RVFI PC-order correctness.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
