hesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark's repeated loop-closing branches can recover IPC, but both earlier\\npredictors regressed because their lookup logic was directly on the PC\\nfeedback path. A useful predictor must retain a short fetch path while\\nmaking its target available before the loop branch is consumed.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Query a small tagged BTB one sequential instruction ahead, using fetch PC+4,\\nand register the hit, direction, target, and queried PC. On the following\\ncycle that registered response belongs to the current sequentially fetched\\ninstruction; if it is a taken branch prediction, IF advances to the saved\\ntarget while still delivering the branch itself to ID. Carry the predicted\\nnext PC to EX and redirect only when architectural resolution disagrees.\\nThis predicts hot loop-closing branches without imem-data decode, BTB tag\\ncompare, counter read, or target selection on the PC-to-PC timing path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small tagged, direct-mapped two-bit-counter BTB whose lookup response is registered from a PC+4 lookahead query and whose entries train only on resolved valid conditional branches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the IF/ID and downstream payloads so execution can verify the fetch decision precisely.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Issue the sequential PC+4 predictor query and select the next fetch PC from the registered response when it matches the current fetch PC, without flushing the correctly delivered predicted branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fetch packet's predicted next PC with the decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved control-flow next PC against the carried prediction, emit redirects only for mis