\": \"Random instruction-memory backpressure currently freezes the PC and decode\\npath immediately, even when a prior fetch could have supplied useful work.\\nThe CoreMark evaluation injects instruction stalls, while load-use, data-memory,\\nand divide waits create opportunities to prefetch sequential instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Random instruction-memory backpressure currently freezes the PC and decode\\npath immediately, even when a prior fetch could have supplied useful work.\\nThe CoreMark evaluation injects instruction stalls, while load-use, data-memory,\\nand divide waits create opportunities to prefetch sequential instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the direct combinational IF-to-ID path with a four-entry instruction\\nqueue driven by a separate fetch PC. Implement its storage as a normal packed\\narray indexed procedurally by runtime read/write pointers, never as generated\\nhierarchy. A ready-qualified fill may run while downstream is interlocked, and\\ndecode consumes an already buffered instruction during temporary imem stalls.\\nOn an EX redirect, atomically discard all queued entries, reset the pointers\\nand count, and restart the fetch PC at the architectural target; no pre-redirect\\ninstruction may reach ID. This converts available front-end slack into\\ninstruction-stall coverage without putting prediction logic on the PC feedback\\npath or changing the single-retire RVFI boundary.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a fetch-packet bundle carrying PC and instruction, plus queue-size and pointer-width constants.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct fetch payload with a four-entry procedural storage array, runtime read/write pointers, occupancy counter, ready-qualified fill, decode dequeue, and redirect flush.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate raw instruction-bus readiness from decode availability so a nonempty queue can feed ID during an imem stall while preserving memory, load-use, and divider interlocks.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-consume permission and queue-empty state through the front end while retaining EX redirect priority and the nret=1 external contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for runtime pointer wraparound, simultaneous dequeue/fill, imem-stall masking, downstream interlocks, and redirect invalidation with PC/RVFI ordering checks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a fetch-packet bundle carrying PC and instruction, plus queue-size and pointer-width constants.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct fetch payload with a four-entry procedural storage array, runtime read/write pointers, occupancy counter, ready-qualified fill, decode dequeue, and redirect flush.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate raw instruction-bus readiness from decode availability so a nonempty queue can feed ID during an imem stall while preserving memory, load-use, and divider interlocks.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-consume permission and queue-empty state through the front end while retaining EX redirect priority and the nret=1 external contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for runtime pointer wraparound, simultaneous dequeue/fill, imem-stall masking, downstream interlocks, and redirect invalidation with PC/RVFI ordering checks.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 330.11, \"delta_pct\": -18.56, \"vs_baseline\": 16.72, \"fmax_mhz\": 155.06, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4697199, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5854, \"ff\": 2299, \"seeds\": [146.35, 158.43, 155.06], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:50:36.434439Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (regression, -18.56%): A four-entry procedural IF queue can lose CoreMark fitness when its pointer/count, dequeue arbitration, and redirect-flush control cost more than the transient imem stalls that prefetch can cover, so front-end decoupling needs measured slack rather than assumed stall hiding.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:13:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Return-address-stack fetch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark contains many small function calls and returns. The current EX-stage\\nJALR resolution fetches and then squashes two sequential instructions on\\nevery return, while prior branch predictors lost Fmax by placing a BTB\\nlookup or branch-target calculation on the fetch feedback path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark contains many small function calls and returns. The current EX-stage\\nJALR resolution fetches and then squashes two sequential instructions on\\nevery return, while prior branch predictors lost Fmax by placing a BTB\\nlookup or branch-target calculation on the fetch feedback path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a shallow committed return-address stack and predict only canonical\\nreturns (`jalr x0, x1/x5, 0`) in IF. The prediction is just an instruction\\nfield match and a mux of the registered RAS top, avoiding branch-immediate\\nextraction, target addition, tags, and counter RAM on the PC path. Train\\npushes and pops only when the corresponding JAL/JALR has resolved in EX;\\ncarry the predicted next PC to EX and retain existing redirect recovery for\\nany mismatch. Correct returns therefore avoid the existing two younger\\nwrong-path instructions without changing conditional-branch behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/return_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small registered RAS with resolved-call push and resolved-return pop inputs, plus a combinational valid/top-address query interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend fetch and ID/EX payloads with the predicted next-PC metadata needed to validate a return prediction at EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only canonical ra/t0 JALR returns and select the registered RAS top as their predicted next PC; all other instructions keep PC+4.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fetch packet's predicted next PC beside the decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved control-flow next PC with the carried prediction, redirect only on mismatch, and emit ordered call/return RAS update events after validation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat a control-flow prediction mismatch as the flush condition while retaining existing bus, load-use, and divide interlock priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the RAS predictor, fetch metadata, EX validation, and update events without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed nested-call/return, empty-stack, noncanonical-JALR, misprediction-recovery, and imem-stall tests with RVFI PC-order checks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/return_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small registered RAS with resolved-call push and resolved-return pop inputs, plus a combinational valid/top-address query interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend fetch and ID/EX payloads with the predicted next-PC metadata needed to validate a return prediction at EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only canonical ra/t0 JALR returns and select the registered RAS top as their predicted next PC; all other instructions keep PC+4.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fetch packet's predicted next PC beside the decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved control-flow next PC with the carried prediction, redirect only on mismatch, and emit ordered call/return RAS update events after validation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat a control-flow prediction mismatch as the flush condition while retaining existing bus, load-use, and divide interlock priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the RAS predictor, fetch metadata, EX validation, and update events without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed nested-call/return, empty-stack, noncanonical-JALR, misprediction-recovery, and imem-stall tests with RVFI PC-order checks.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 364.95, \"delta_pct\": -9.97, \"vs_baseline\": 29.04, \"fmax_mhz\": 163.43, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4478102, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6228, \"ff\": 2486, \"seeds\": [160.36, 163.43, 167.08], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:48:59.027285Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 4}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:14:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r5s0\", \"title\": \"Exhaustive source-aware load interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock compares a load destination with both raw register\\nbit fields of every fetched word. Fields that encode immediates, destinations,\\nor reserved data can therefore create unnecessary bubbles in CoreMark's\\ndense arithmetic and address-generation sequences.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock compares a load destination with both raw register\\nbit fields of every fetched word. Fields that encode immediates, destinations,\\nor reserved data can therefore create unnecessary bubbles in CoreMark's\\ndense arithmetic and address-generation sequences.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the raw-field load-use comparison with an exhaustive, opcode-local\\nsource-use table in the hazard unit. Classify rs1 as live only for OP,\\nOP-IMM, LOAD, STORE, BRANCH, and JALR, and rs2 only for OP, STORE, and\\nBRANCH; gate the corresponding comparisons with these bits and IF/ID valid.\\nKeep every true one-cycle load dependency stalled, including all RV32M OP\\noperations, branches, stores, and JALR. This removes false bubbles without\\nadding work to the fetch or EX arithmetic timing paths.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive exhaustive opcode-local rs1/rs2-use bits from the IF/ID instruction and gate only the load-use comparisons with them, preserving all existing redirect and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Exhaustively test source-use classification for valid RV32IM opcodes, invalid/reserved forms, x0, and every true load dependency so false bubbles are removed without permitting stale operands.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive exhaustive opcode-local rs1/rs2-use bits from the IF/ID instruction and gate only the load-use comparisons with them, preserving all existing redirect and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Exhaustively test source-use classification for valid RV32IM opcodes, invalid/reserved forms, x0, and every true load dependency so false b