n 100\\nfind cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses -maxdepth 1 -type f -print | sort | tail -n 30\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\\n hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 Backward-taken fetch branch prediction\\noutcome= regression fitness= 252.17 delta= -10.84 fmax= 108.67 lut= 9601\\nnotes= \\n\\n hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 PC-indexed dynamic loop predictor\\noutcome= regression fitness= 308.5 delta= 0.69 fmax= 131.46 lut= 12633\\nnotes= \\n\\n hyp-20260710-003-r3s2 Lookahead registered BTB predictor\\noutcome= broken fitness= None delta= None fmax= None lut= None\\nnotes= \\n\\n hyp-20260710-003-r4s2 Return-address-stack fetch predictor\\noutcome= regression fitness= 364.95 delta= -9.97 fmax= 163.43 lut= 6228\\nnotes= \\n\\n hyp-20260710-003-r5s2 Validated lookahead BTB predictor\\noutcome= broken fitness= None delta= None fmax= None lut= None\\nnotes= \\ncores/bench/core.yaml:19:  source_id: hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:1:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"baseline-bench-2d60805\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Baseline retest for cores/bench\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"improvement\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 282.82, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 0.0, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 0.0, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 127.03, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 9563, \\\"ff\\\": 1866, \\\"seeds\\\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T00:46:51.300788Z\\\", \\\"round_id\\\": 0, \\\"slot\\\": 0}\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Share RV32 multiply datapath\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\\\\nevaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\\\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\\\\nevaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\\\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace the unconditional signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and\\\\nsigned-unsigned product expressions with one shared 33x33 unsigned modular\\\\nmultiplier. Select the operands' sign extension from the decoded multiply\\\\noperation, then select bits [31:0] for MUL or [63:32] for MULH, MULHU, and\\\\nMULHSU. The low 64 bits of the 33-bit two's-complement product preserve all\\\\nRV32M result definitions, while removing two large parallel multiplier\\\\ncones. Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expressions unchanged.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"improvement\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 306.38, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 8.33, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 8.33, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 137.61, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 9816, \\\"ff\\\": 1867, \\\"seeds\\\": [136.3, 149.12, 137.61], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T00:55:35.641639Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 1, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +8.33%): RV32M multiply variants should share a sign-selected 33x33 product and select the required 32-bit half, since parallel signed/unsigned multiplier cones waste LUTs even though each instruction consumes only one result.\\\"}\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Decode-stage branch resolution\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Restructure the front end so conditional branches resolve in decode using\\\\nthe register-file read values and explicit bypasses from EX/MEM and WB.\\\\nRedirect the PC and squash only the fetched wrong-path instruction in the\\\\nsame decode cycle; retain EX resolution for JALR and preserve a targeted\\\\nload-to-branch interlock until load data is available. This removes one\\\\nrecovery cycle for the common backward conditional branch while retaining\\\\nsingle-retire RVFI ordering and the existing memory interface.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 7, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provide decode-stage bypass selects so branches compare the architecturally newest operands.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 7, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\\\