oduct's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 306.38, \"delta_pct\": 8.33, \"vs_baseline\": 8.33, \"fmax_mhz\": 137.61, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9816, \"ff\": 1867, \"seeds\": [136.3, 149.12, 137.61], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:55:35.641639Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +8.33%): RV32M multiply variants should share a sign-selected 33x33 product and select the required 32-bit half, since parallel signed/unsigned multiplier cones waste LUTs even though each instruction consumes only one result.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Decode-stage branch resolution\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Restructure the front end so conditional branches resolve in decode using\\nthe register-file read values and explicit bypasses from EX/MEM and WB.\\nRedirect the PC and squash only the fetched wrong-path instruction in the\\nsame decode cycle; retain EX resolution for JALR and preserve a targeted\\nload-to-branch interlock until load data is available. This removes one\\nrecovery cycle for the common backward conditional branch while retaining\\nsingle-retire RVFI ordering and the existing memory interface.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide decode-stage bypass selects so branches compare the architecturally newest operands.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redi