{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.id == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\\\") | \\\"ID: \\\\(.id)\\\\nTITLE: \\\\(.title)\\\\n\\\\(.hypothesis.hypothesis)\\\\n\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && for f in cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r[3456]s2.last; do echo \\\"\"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,120p' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"ID: hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\nTITLE: Lookahead registered BTB predictor\nQuery a small tagged BTB one sequential instruction ahead, using fetch PC+4,\nand register the hit, direction, target, and queried PC. On the following\ncycle that registered response belongs to the current sequentially fetched\ninstruction; if it is a taken branch prediction, IF advances to the saved\ntarget while still delivering the branch itself to ID. Carry the predicted\nnext PC to EX and redirect only when architectural resolution disagrees.\nThis predicts hot loop-closing branches without imem-data decode, BTB tag\ncompare, counter read, or target selection on the PC-to-PC timing path.\n\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\nTITLE: Validated lookahead BTB predictor\nImplement a small direct-mapped conditional-branch BTB whose lookup is made\nfor sequential PC+4 and registered before it can influence fetch. A response\nmay redirect only when its recorded query PC exactly equals the current fetch\nPC; otherwise fetch deterministically falls through and invalidates the\nstale response. EX trains only resolved valid branches and carries the exact\npredicted next PC for mismatch recovery. Redirects, instruction stalls, and\ndownstream holds invalidate or preserve the response according to whether\nthe matching fetched instruction was actually accepted. This removes hot\nloop recovery bubbles while keeping tag comparison, counter read, and target\nselection out of the PC-to-PC feedback path.\n\n\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r3s2.last\nWrote and validated the predictor hypothesis:\n\n[hyp-20260710-003-r3s2.yaml](/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r3s2.yaml)\n\nIt proposes a registered, `PC+4` lookahead BTB to avoid putting predictor lookup on the PC feedback path.cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r4s2.last\nWrote and validated the predictor hypothesis:\n\n[hyp-20260710-003-r4s2.yaml](/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r4s2.yaml)\n\nIt proposes a shallow return-address-stack predictor to remove return-path flushes without repeating the BTB/fetch-critical-path regressions.cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.last\nWrote and validated [hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.yaml](/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.yaml).\n\nIt proposes a PC-aligned, registered lookahead BTB that keeps predictor lookup off the PC feedback path and explicitly suppresses stale predictions after redirects or stalls.cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r6s2.last\nWrote and schema-validated the predictor hypothesis: [hyp-20260710-003-r6s2.yaml](/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r6s2.yaml).\n\nIt proposes a minimal one-entry last-resolved loop-target predictor to avoid the table and timing cost of prior BTB designs.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The earlier one-entry predictor was closest to the right timing shape, but it only checked predictions for branch instructions. I’m refining that into a speculation-safe version: every fetched instruction carries its predicted next PC, so a symbolic-memory non-branch hit is recovered as a normal misprediction rather than skipping architectural control flow."}}
