{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; h = YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r7s2.yaml\\\"); abort \\\"bad id\\\" unless h[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\\\"; abort \\\"bad category\\\" unless h[\\\"category\\\"] == \\\"predictor\\\"; abort \\\"bad impact\\\" unless h.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\").is_a?(Integer) && h.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"confidence\\\") == \\\"medium\\\"; abort \\\"bad paths\\\" unless h[\\\"changes\\\"].all? { |c| c[\\\"file\\\"].match?(%r{\\\\A(?:rtl/|test/test_)}) }; puts \\\"YAML structure and paths validated (#{h[\\\"changes\\\"].length} changes).\\\"' && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r7s2.yaml && git status --short cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r7s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"YAML structure and paths validated (8 changes).\nid: hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\ntitle: \"Speculation-safe loop target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark repeatedly executes a few loop-closing conditional branches, where\n  the EX-stage redirect discards two younger instructions on each taken edge.\n  Prior BTBs either harmed the PC feedback path or treated a PC hit as proof\n  that the fetched word was still a branch, which is invalid under symbolic\n  instruction memory and broke RVFI PC sequencing.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry last-resolved conditional-branch predictor, but make its\n  prediction a transaction carried by every fetched instruction rather than a\n  branch-only promise. The entry stores branch PC, target, and last direction;\n  its small registered-PC equality and target mux remain the only logic added\n  to fetch. IF/ID and ID/EX carry predicted_next_pc for all accepted fetches.\n  In EX, compare that value against the architectural next PC for every valid\n  instruction: non-control instructions resolve to PC+4, branches and jumps\n  resolve normally. Any mismatch redirects and flushes, including a predictor\n  hit whose symbolic imem word is no longer a branch. Train the entry only\n  when a valid resolved conditional branch advances from EX, and bind prediction\n  metadata to its fetch PC across imem/dmem stalls and redirects. This retains\n  the timing advantage of a one-entry PC-only predictor while making all stale\n  or aliased hits recoverable under RVFI.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/last_branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a one-entry PC/target/direction predictor with reset state and an EX-advance-qualified conditional-branch training interface.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add fetch-PC and predicted-next-PC fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so prediction remains paired with the instruction that accepted it.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the one-entry predictor only to choose the fetch successor, and emit the exact predicted-next-PC transaction for every fetched instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch prediction metadata atomically with decoded instruction state while preserving existing flush and hold semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute architectural next PC for every valid instruction, redirect on any predicted-versus-actual mismatch, and expose precisely qualified conditional-branch training signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Integrate universal misprediction recovery with redirect, load-use, long-operation, and memory-stall priorities without advancing stale fetch metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor lookup, EX training, transaction metadata, and recovery while retaining the nret=1 external and RVFI contracts.\"\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add directed tests for loop warm-up and exit, a trained-PC non-branch instruction replacement, redirects, and imem/dmem stall transaction ownership.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
