nation against\\nboth raw IF/ID bit fields, even when the following instruction does not read\\none or either field. Those false matches insert avoidable bubbles after loads\\nwithout shortening any real data dependency or changing memory timing.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Derive explicit uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 signals from the validated decode of\\nthe IF/ID instruction, and gate the existing load-use comparisons with those\\nsignals and IF/ID validity. Classify every architectural source exactly:\\nOP, STORE, and BRANCH use both; OP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR use rs1 only; all\\nremaining legal instructions and traps use neither. Keep the existing\\none-cycle stall for every true dependency, so the MEM/WB forwarding boundary\\nand the dmem-to-EX timing path remain unchanged while false interlocks no\\nlonger cost CoreMark issue cycles.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose validated decode-local uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 signals, defaulting both low for illegal or operand-free encodings.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the decoded source-use qualifiers alongside the IF/ID decode outputs without changing operand capture or pipeline payload timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire source-use qualifiers from decode into the load-use hazard decision.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each load-use register comparison with the corresponding architecturally consumed source and IF/ID valid while preserving dmem, redirect, and divide priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed adjacent-load cases for real rs1/rs2 dependencies and each operand-free or single-source encoding, checking both architectural results and bubble behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv