}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize valid direct JAL instructions, form the PC-relative target, and emit an acceptance-qualified early-redirect request while latching its metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate PC-update redirect selection from EX wrong-path output squashing so an accepted decode-stage JAL is retained while the PC advances to its target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress only the duplicate EX redirect for a JAL already redirected in decode; retain JAL result, RVFI pc_wdata, JALR, and branch behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose or qualify the ID acceptance condition so early JAL redirection cannot occur while ID/EX is held or an older EX redirect squashes it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Arbitrate older EX recovery ahead of an accepted decode-stage JAL redirect and wire the split fetch-control paths without changing the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_core.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed JAL call/return, consecutive JAL, load-use hold, dmem-stall, and simultaneous older-redirect cases that check RVFI PC order and return-address writes.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add ID/EX metadata marking a direct JAL whose fetch redirect was accepted in decode.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize valid direct JAL instructions, form the PC-relative target, and emit an acceptance-qualified early-redirect request while latching its metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate PC-update redirect selection from EX wrong-path output squashing so an accepted decode-stage JAL is retained while the PC advances to its target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress only the duplicate EX redirect for a JAL already redirected in decode; retain JAL result, RVFI pc_wdata, JALR, and branch behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose or qualify the ID acceptance condition so early JAL redirection cannot occur while ID/EX is held or an older EX redirect squashes it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Arbitrate older EX recovery ahead of an accepted decode-stage JAL redirect and wire the split fetch-control paths without changing the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_core.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed JAL call/return, consecutive JAL, load-use hold, dmem-stall, and simultaneous older-redirect cases that check RVFI PC order and return-address writes.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 161.77, \"delta_pct\": -62.42, \"vs_baseline\": -42.8, \"fmax_mhz\": 71.86, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4442158, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5736, \"ff\": 2199, \"seeds\": [70.77, 71.86, 73.86], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:44:32.240279Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 8}\n25:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"Signature-qualified loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly revisits a small number of loop-closing branches, but\\nprevious BTB attempts either put a large table on the fetch feedback path or\\npaid for a wide universal predicted-next-PC comparison in execute. A tiny\\npredictor can retain the temporal-locality benefit if alias recovery is\\nexplicit and restricted to the control cases that need it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly revisits a small number of loop-closing branches, but\\nprevious BTB attempts either put a large table on the fetch feedback path or\\npaid for a wide universal predicted-next-PC comparison in execute. A tiny\\npredictor can retain the temporal-locality benefit if alias recovery is\\nexplicit and restricted to the control cases that need it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a one-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor that stores branch\\nPC, target, direction, and the resolved instruction word as a signature.\\nIF uses only registered PC equality, direction, and target muxing to select\\nthe speculative successor; the instruction signature is carried as\\nsideband validation metadata and is not placed in the PC-select cone. EX\\nretains architectural branch resolution and redirects only for a predicted\\ncontrol instruction whose resolved successor differs, or for a predicted\\nhit that resolves as a non-branch (including a symbolic-imem signature\\nmismatch), explicitly restoring PC+4. This avoids assuming PC identity\\nproves instruction identity, while replacing the prior universal 32-bit\\nnext-PC compare with narrow prediction-valid/control-qualified recovery.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/last_branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a resettable one-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor holding PC, target, direction, and resolved instruction signature, with EX-advance-qualified training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add fetch prediction-valid, predicted target, and signature-match metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so the prediction remains bound to its fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use only the small registered-PC predictor lookup for the speculative successor and carry its transaction metadata for every accepted fetch without decoding imem data in the PC-select path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch predictor transaction metadata atomically with decoded instruction state across ordinary holds and flushes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve branches architecturally, recover only control-qualified prediction mismatch