{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"test -f cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r11s0.yaml && echo 'hypothesis file present'\ngit check-ignore -v cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r11s0.yaml || true\nsed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r11s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"hypothesis file present\n.gitignore:85:cores/*/experiments/hypotheses/\tcores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r11s0.yaml\nid: hyp-20260711-001-r11s0\ntitle: \"Decoder-owned load-use source masks\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The load-use interlock currently compares a load destination against both\n  raw rs bit fields of every fetched instruction. Immediate and no-source\n  encodings can therefore create bubbles even when they cannot consume the\n  loaded value, reducing CoreMark issue rate without protecting a real hazard.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make the validated decoder the single source of uses_rs1 and uses_rs2\n  metadata, then carry those bits with the IF/ID payload to gate the existing\n  load-use comparisons. Classify OP, STORE, and BRANCH as two-source;\n  OP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR as rs1-only; and JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, and EBREAK\n  as source-free. Illegal or unrecognized encodings remain conservatively\n  two-source so the interlock cannot weaken trap-path operand capture. This\n  removes only false bubbles while retaining the current pipeline, forwarding,\n  memory timing, RVFI payload, and all true load dependencies.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Export exact uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 signals only from positively validated instruction arms, with conservative two-source defaults for illegal encodings.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Route the decoder-owned source-use metadata alongside the decoded IF/ID instruction for hazard detection without changing operand or control capture.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the source-use bits from decode to the load-use interlock while preserving existing imem, dmem, divide, and redirect arbitration.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Gate each raw register-number comparison with its corresponding decoder-owned source-use bit and retain the exact one-cycle stall for every live source match.\"\n  - file: test/test_hazard.py\n    description: \"Add directed load-followed-by tests for each source-free, rs1-only, and two-source encoding, including illegal instructions and genuine dependent branches, stores, and RV32M operations.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
