raffic violates architectural load/store ordering and register-state checks.\"}\n19:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"One-entry loop target predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark's hottest control flow is dominated by repeatedly executed loop\\nbranches, but prior multi-entry BTB and RAS attempts either placed too much\\nlogic on the fetch feedback path or introduced difficult response-state\\nownership across stalls and redirects. A predictor much smaller than a BTB\\ncan still capture temporal locality in the innermost loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark's hottest control flow is dominated by repeatedly executed loop\\nbranches, but prior multi-entry BTB and RAS attempts either placed too much\\nlogic on the fetch feedback path or introduced difficult response-state\\nownership across stalls and redirects. A predictor much smaller than a BTB\\ncan still capture temporal locality in the innermost loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a one-entry last-resolved conditional-branch predictor. It stores only\\nthe PC, resolved target, and last direction of the most recently resolved\\nvalid conditional branch; fetch predicts taken only when the registered PC\\nexactly matches that entry and the stored direction is taken. This replaces\\na table lookup, tag array, and saturating-counter logic with a single\\nequality check and target mux, while preserving EX as the sole architectural\\nresolver. The fetched instruction carries an explicit predicted-next-PC\\ntransaction; EX redirects only on a mismatch and trains the entry only when\\nthat branch actually advances, with redirect and all front-end holds keeping\\nprediction metadata paired with its accepted instruction.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/last_branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single registered PC/target/direction entry, combinational exact-PC prediction output, and resolved-valid conditional-branch training interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid metadata to the fetch and ID/EX payloads so recovery compares the prediction belonging to the retiring control instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select the sequential PC or the one-entry predicted target and emit prediction metadata only for the instruction accepted at the corresponding fetch PC.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch fetch prediction metadata atomically with the decoded instruction, preserving it through ordinary ID holds and bubbles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare each resolved conditional branch's architectural next PC against its carried prediction, issue recovery only on mismatch, and emit precisely qualified training data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Make prediction-mismatch recovery coexist with imem, dmem, load-use, and long-operation priorities without allowing a stale prediction to advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire the one-entry predictor, training, fetch metadata, and mismatch recovery while retaining the nret=1 external interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed repeated-loop, alternating-loop displacement, final-exit, redirect, and imem/dmem-stall tests that verify RVFI PC sequencing and exact metadata ownership.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/last_branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single registered PC/target/direction entry, combinational exact-PC prediction output, and resolved-valid conditional-branch training interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid metadata to the fetch and ID/EX payloads so recovery compares the prediction belonging to the retiring control instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select the sequential PC or the one-entry predicted target and emit prediction metadata only for the instruction accepted at the corresponding fetch PC.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch fetch prediction metadata atomically with the decoded instruction, preserving it through ordinary ID holds and bubbles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare each resolved conditional branch's architectural next PC against its carried prediction, issue recovery only on mismatch, and emit precisely qualified training data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Make prediction-mismatch recovery coexist with imem, dmem, load-use, and long-operation priorities without allowing a stale prediction to advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire the one-entry predictor, training, fetch metadata, and mismatch recovery while retaining the nret=1 external interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed repeated-loop, alternating-loop displacement, final-exit, redirect, and imem/dmem-stall tests that verify RVFI PC sequencing and exact metadata ownership.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\nwd_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 23:18:44 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: pc_fwd_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 23:18:44 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_pc_fwd_check_sv_41_55 at rvfi_pc_fwd_check.sv:41.6-41.69 step 20\\nSBY 23:18:44 [pc_fwd_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\nSBY 23:19:25 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:01  waiting for solver (1 minute)\\nSBY 23:19:52 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:27  Status: passed\\nSBY 23:19:52 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished 