en\t\t\tOrdered one-entry store buffer\nhyp-20260710-003-r6s2\tpredictor\tbroken\t\t\tOne-entry loop target predictor\nhyp-20260710-001-r7s0\tmicro_opt\timprovement\t430.45\t4.61\tFixed lane memory extraction\nhyp-20260710-002-r7s1\tstructural\tregression\t364.7\t-11.37\tMEM-to-EX load forwarding\nhyp-20260710-003-r7s2\tpredictor\tregression\t167.49\t-59.3\tSpeculation-safe loop target predictor\nhyp-20260710-001-r8s0\tmicro_opt\tbroken\t\t\tExact source-aware load interlock\nhyp-20260710-002-r8s1\tstructural\tregression\t161.77\t-62.42\tDecode-accepted direct JAL redirect\nhyp-20260710-003-r8s2\tpredictor\tbroken\t\t\tSignature-qualified loop predictor\nhyp-20260710-001-r9s0\tmicro_opt\tregression\t419.9\t-2.45\tPrecompute PC-relative control targets\nhyp-20260710-002-r9s1\tstructural\tbroken\t\t\tIn-order memory completion queue\nhyp-20260710-003-r9s2\tpredictor\tregression\t343.92\t-20.1\tEpoch-bound registered loop predictor\nhyp-20260711-001-r10s0\tmicro_opt\tregression\t412.88\t-4.08\tShare ALU barrel shifter\nhyp-20260711-002-r10s1\tstructural\tbroken\t\t\tElastic registered fetch boundary\nhyp-20260711-003-r10s2\tpredictor\tbroken\t\t\tRegistered decode BTFNT predictor\nhyp-20260711-001-r11s0\tmicro_opt\tbroken\t\t\tDecoder-owned load-use source masks\nhyp-20260711-002-r11s1\tstructural\tregression\t355.48\t-17.42\tTwo-stage partial-product multiplier\nhyp-20260711-003-r11s2\tpredictor\tbroken\t\t\tAtomic registered BTFNT front end\n9-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Decoupled sequential fetch queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current IF stage couples every instruction-bus ready pulse directly to\\nPC advance, so a random imem stall immediately freezes the entire pipeline.\\nCoreMark also has load-use, data-memory, and occasional divide stalls during\\nwhich sequential instruction bandwidth is otherwise unused.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current IF stage couples every instruction-bus ready pulse directly to\\nPC advance, so a random imem stall immediately freezes the entire pipeline.\\nCoreMark also has load-use, data-memory, and occasional divide stalls during\\nwhich sequential instruction bandwidth is otherwise unused.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the single combinational fetch payload with a small sequential\\ninstruction FIFO and an independent fetch PC. While decode or execute is\\nstalled, the front end continues to fill unused FIFO entries whenever imem\\nis ready; while imem is temporarily not ready, decode consumes buffered\\ninstructions. A redirect atomically invalidates queued wrong-path entries\\nand restarts fetching at the resolved target. This preserves the existing\\nEX-stage branch decision and single-retire RVFI boundary while converting\\navailable slack into tolerance of the benchmark's random instruction stalls.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the fetch-queue payload type and any queue-depth constants needed by the decoupled front end.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct PC-to-ID payload with a small sequential prefetch FIFO, separate fetch/consume pointers, ready-qualified fills, and redirect invalidation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-consume backpressure and existing redirect control to the queued fetch interface without changing the top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate decode availability from raw imem readiness so a queued instruction can issue during an imem stall while preserving load, dmem, and divider interlocks.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed queue tests for sequential fill/drain, imem backpressure masking, and redirect flushing of wrong-path entries.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the fetch-queue payload type and any queue-depth constants needed by the decoupled front end.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct PC-to-ID payload with a small sequential prefetch FIFO, separate fetch/consume pointers, ready-qualified fills, and redirect invalidation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-consume backpressure and existing redirect control to the queued fetch interface without changing the top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate decode availability from raw imem readiness so a queued instruction can issue during an imem stall while preserving load, dmem, and divider interlocks.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed queue tests for sequential fill/drain, imem backpressure masking, and redirect flushing of wrong-path entries.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"build_failed: yosys synth: cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv:62: ERROR: Index in generate block prefix syntax is not constant!\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): A sequential fetch FIFO must index its storage procedurally with runtime read/write pointers; generate-block hierarchy and prefixes are elaboration-time constructs and reject dynamic queue indices before synthesis.\"}\n10-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Lookahead registered BTB predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark's repeated loop-closing branches can recover IPC, but both earlier\\npredictors regressed because their lookup logic was directly on the PC\\nfeedback path. A useful predictor must retain a short fetch path while\\nmaking its target available before the loop branch is consumed.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark's repeated loop-closing branches can recover IPC, but both earlier\\npredictors regressed because their lookup logic was directly on the PC\\nfeedback path. A useful predictor must retain a short fetch path while\\nmaking its target available before the loop branch is consumed.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Query a small tagged BTB one sequential instruction ahead, using fetch PC+4,\\nand register the hit, direction, target, and queried PC. On the following\\ncycle that registered response belongs to the current sequentially fetched\\ninstruction; if it is a taken branch prediction, IF advances to the saved\\ntarget while still delivering the branch itself to ID. Carry the predicted\\nnext PC to EX and redirect only when architectural resolution disagrees.\\nThis predicts hot loop-closing branches without imem-data decode, BTB tag\\ncompare, counter read, or target selection on the PC-to-PC timing path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small tagged, direct-mapped two-bit-counter BTB whose lookup response is registered from a PC+4 lookahead query and whose entries train only on resolved valid conditional branches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the IF/ID and downstream payloads so execution can verify the fetch decision precisely.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Issue the sequential PC+4 predictor query and select the next fetch PC from the registered response when it matches the current fetch PC, without flushing the correctly delivered predicted branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fetch packet's predicted next PC with the decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved control-flow next PC against the carried prediction, emit redirects only for mismatches, and expose valid conditional-branch training fields.\"}, {\"file\": \