eness checks.\"}\n31-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Registered decode BTFNT predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly executes backward conditional loop branches, but prior\\nfetch-stage predictors lost Fmax by putting instruction-memory data or BTB\\nlookup in the PC feedback path. A predictor can still remove a recovery\\nbubble if it acts after a registered fetch payload, rather than directly\\nfrom the instruction-memory response.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly executes backward conditional loop branches, but prior\\nfetch-stage predictors lost Fmax by putting instruction-memory data or BTB\\nlookup in the PC feedback path. A predictor can still remove a recovery\\nbubble if it acts after a registered fetch payload, rather than directly\\nfrom the instruction-memory response.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a real registered IF/ID payload and apply static backward-taken,\\nforward-not-taken prediction in decode only for a decoded, valid conditional\\nbranch with a negative B immediate. Decode supplies the predicted target to\\nthe PC register for the next fetch, so instruction-memory data, branch\\ndecode, immediate extraction, and target addition are separated across the\\nIF/ID register instead of one PC-to-PC timing cone. Carry a small\\npredicted-branch/predicted-taken bit with the instruction; EX performs its\\nexisting architectural branch resolution and recovers only for that\\nprediction's direction/target mismatch. Thus non-branch instructions avoid\\nthe universal 32-bit successor comparison that made the epoch predictor\\nslow, while symbolic instruction memory is safe because prediction is\\nqualified from the registered instruction itself.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add registered fetch payload and branch-prediction metadata fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Turn the combinational fetch output into a stall-aware IF/ID register and accept a decode-stage predicted redirect with defined EX-recovery priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode valid conditional branches from the registered fetch payload, form negative B-immediate targets, and emit/latch BTFNT prediction metadata without consulting branch operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain architectural branch resolution and issue recovery only for a carried, qualified branch prediction whose resolved successor disagrees.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Arbitrate decode prediction, EX misprediction recovery, load-use, divide, and bus holds so prediction metadata and fetch acceptance stay aligned.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the registered fetch path, decode predictor, carried metadata, and qualified EX recovery while preserving the nret=1 RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed backward-loop warm-up, final not-taken exit, forward-taken recovery, imem/dmem stall, and symbolic instruction-change tests with RVFI PC-order assertions.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add registered fetch payload and branch-prediction metadata fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Turn the combinational fetch output into a stall-aware IF/ID register and accept a decode-stage predicted redirect with defined EX-recovery priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode valid conditional branches from the registered fetch payload, form negative B-immediate targets, and emit/latch BTFNT prediction metadata without consulting branch operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"desc