currently compares a load destination against both\\nraw rs bit fields of every fetched instruction. Immediate and no-source\\nencodings can therefore create bubbles even when they cannot consume the\\nloaded value, reducing CoreMark issue rate without protecting a real hazard.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make the validated decoder the single source of uses_rs1 and uses_rs2\\nmetadata, then carry those bits with the IF/ID payload to gate the existing\\nload-use comparisons. Classify OP, STORE, and BRANCH as two-source;\\nOP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR as rs1-only; and JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, and EBREAK\\nas source-free. Illegal or unrecognized encodings remain conservatively\\ntwo-source so the interlock cannot weaken trap-path operand capture. This\\nremoves only false bubbles while retaining the current pipeline, forwarding,\\nmemory timing, RVFI payload, and all true load dependencies.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Export exact uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 signals only from positively validated instruction arms, with conservative two-source defaults for illegal encodings.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the decoder-owned source-use metadata alongside the decoded IF/ID instruction for hazard detection without changing operand or control capture.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the source-use bits from decode to the load-use interlock while preserving existing imem, dmem, divide, and redirect arbitration.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each raw register-number comparison with its corresponding decoder-owned source-use bit and retain the exact one-cycle stall for every live source match.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed load-followed-by tests for each source-free, rs1-only, and two-source encoding, including illegal instructions and genuine depe