fi_reg_check.sv:44.6-44.59 step 20\\nSBY 23:08:57 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-001-r5s0/formal/last_run-68450.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-001-r5s0/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-68450/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 5}\n17:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Shared branch subtract flags\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"EX currently elaborates equality and signed/unsigned relational comparisons for\\nevery branch condition. CoreMark executes frequent loop-control branches, so\\ntheir comparator cone is a promising Fmax and LUT target without changing IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"EX currently elaborates equality and signed/unsigned relational comparisons for\\nevery branch condition. CoreMark executes frequent loop-control branches, so\\ntheir comparator cone is a promising Fmax and LUT target without changing IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the six separately expressed branch comparisons with one 33-bit\\nsubtract/flag network in EX. Derive equality from the difference, signed less-\\nthan from operand signs plus the difference sign, and unsigned less-than from\\nthe subtraction borrow; select the requested BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU result.\\nThis should map to one carry-chain-friendly arithmetic cone instead of parallel\\ncomparator logic while retaining the existing EX-stage redirect timing, stalls,\\nand RVFI PC behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a shared subtract, zero, signed-less-than, and unsigned-borrow flag path for all six conditional branch predicates.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed signed and unsigned branch boundary programs, including taken and not-taken cases, to validate control-flow and RVFI retirement PCs.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a shared subtract, zero, signed-less-than, and unsigned-borrow flag path for all six conditional branch predicates.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed signed and unsigned branch boundary programs, including taken and not-taken cases, to validate control-flow and RVFI retirement PCs.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 411.5, \"delta_pct\": 1.51, \"vs_baseline\": 45.5, \"fmax_mhz\": 184.84, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5789, \"ff\": 2220, \"seeds\": [165.95, 196.23, 184.84], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:21:20.670665Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r6s0 (improvement, +1.51%): Encoding BEQ/BNE and signed/unsigned relational branches from one 33-bit subtract's zero, sign, and borrow flags shares a carry-chain-friendly EX cone, modestly improving CoreMark loop-branch timing without changing redirect behavior.\"}\n20:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Fixed lane memory extraction\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The MEM stage currently uses a variable 32-bit right shift to extract every\\nbyte or halfword load from combinational dmem data. On the FPGA benchmark\\nwrapper this sits directly after the dmem read mux and before MEM/WB state,\\nso its barrel-mux cone can constrain Fmax for a result that needs only one\\nof four fixed byte lanes or one of two aligned halfword lanes.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The MEM stage currently uses a variable 32-bit right shift to extract every\\nbyte or halfword load from combinational dmem data. On the FPGA benchmark\\nwrapper this sits directly after the dmem read mux and before MEM/WB state,\\nso its barrel-mux cone can constrain Fmax for a result that needs only one\\nof four fixed byte lanes or one of two aligned halfword lanes.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace variable-shift based load extraction and variable-shift byte-mask\\nformation with fixed, address-indexed lane muxes. Select byte data with a\\nfour-arm addr[1:0] case, select aligned halfword data with addr[1], and form\\nSB/SH masks from the same fixed cases. Preserve the existing misalignment\\ntrap and dmem gating exactly, keep word loads/stores direct, and retain all\\nRVFI memory payload semantics. This removes a general 32-bit barrel-shift\\nnetwork from the dmem-return path without changing pipeline timing or IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace variable right-shift load extraction and shifted byte-mask expressions with fixed byte/halfword lane muxes while retaining alignment traps, dmem outputs, and RVFI masks.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_mem_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add exhaustive byte-lane and aligned-halfword load/store checks, including sign extension, masks, and misaligned-access dmem gating.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace variable right-shift load extraction and shifted byte-mask expressions with fixed byte/halfword lane muxes while retaining alignment traps, dmem outputs, and RVFI masks.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_mem_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add exhaustive byte-lane and aligned-halfword load/store checks, including sign extension, masks, and misaligned-access dmem gating.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 430.45, \"delta_pct\": 4.61, \"vs_baseline\": 52.2, \"fmax_mhz\": 193.35, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5763, \"ff\": 2216, \"seeds\": [182.88, 193.35, 202.27], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:30:58.229373Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r7s0 (improvement, +4.61%): On an FPGA MEM path, replacing variable 32-bit load shifts and shifted store masks with fixed addr-indexed byte/halfword lane muxes removes a barrel-mux cone after dmem and improves Fmax when alignment trapping already restricts halfword selection.\"}\n23:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r8s0\", \"title\": \"Exact source-aware load interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock currently compares a preceding load destination against\\nboth raw IF/ID bit fields, even when the following instruction does not read\\none or either field. Those false matches insert avoidable bubbles after loads\\nwithout shortening any real data dependency or changing memory timing.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock currently compares a preceding load destination against\\nboth raw IF/ID bit fields, even when the following instruction does not read\\none or either field. Those false matches insert avoidable bubbles after loads\\nwithout shortening any real data dependency or changing memory timing.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Derive explicit uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 signals from the validated decode of\\nthe IF/ID instruction, and gate the existing load-use comparisons with those\\nsignals and IF/ID validity. Classify every architectural source exactly:\\nOP, STORE, and BRANCH use both; OP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR use rs1 only; all\\nremaining legal instructions and traps use neither. Keep the existing\\none-cycle stall for every true dependency, so the MEM/WB forwarding boundary\\nand the dmem-to-EX timing path remain unchanged while false interlocks no\\nlonger cost CoreMark issue cycles.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose validated decode-local uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 signals, defaulting both low for illegal or operand-free encodings.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the decoded source-use qualifiers alongside the IF/ID decode outputs without changing operand capture or pipeline payload timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire source-use qualifiers from decode into the load-use hazard decision.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each load-use register comparison with the corresponding architecturally consumed source and IF/ID valid while preserving dmem, redirect, and divide priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed adjacent-load cases for real rs1/rs2 dependencies and each operand-free or single-source encoding, checking both architectural results and bubble behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose validated decode-local uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 signals, defaulting both low for illegal or operand-free encodings.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the decoded source-use qualifiers alongside the IF/ID decode outputs without changing operand capture or pipeline payload timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire source-use qualifiers from decode into the load-use hazard decision.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each load-use register comparison with the corresponding architecturally consumed source and IF/ID valid while preserving dmem, redirect, and divide priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed adjacent-load cases for real rs1/rs2 dependencies and each operand-free or single-source encoding, checking both architectural results and bubble behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\nce to VCD file: engine_0/trace0.vcd\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] engine_0: ##   0:00:16  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace0_tb.v\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] engine_0: ##   0:00:16  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace0.smtc\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] engine_0: ##   0:00:16  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace0.yw\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] engine_0: ##   0:00:17  Status: passed\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:17 (17)\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:12 (12)\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] summary: cover trace: cover/engine_0/trace0.vcd\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] summary:   reached cover statement rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__cover_cover_stmts_vh_1_48 at cover_stmts.vh:1.23-1.55 step 20\\nSBY 23:40:56 [cover] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\n\\nFormal: 52 passed, 1 failed\\nFailed: reg_ch0\\n\\n--- reg_ch0/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\\nSBY 23:40:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 9..\\nSBY 23:40:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 10..\\nSBY 23:40:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 11..\\nSBY 23:40:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 12..\\nSBY 23:40:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 13..\\nSBY 23:40:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 14..\\nSBY 23:40:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 15..\\nSBY 23:40:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 16..\\nSBY 23:40:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 17..