kward branches) and function calls (JAL).\\\\nCurrently, all branches and jumps resolve in EX, incurring a 2-cycle penalty. A static predictor\\\\nin the ID stage can achieve a 0-cycle penalty for correctly predicted backward branches and JALs,\\\\nsignificantly boosting IPC without impacting Fmax like complex dynamic predictors.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"We will predict JAL and backward branches (imm < 0) as Taken during the ID stage, immediately\\\\nredirecting the IF stage. Forward branches and JALR will be predicted Not Taken. The EX stage\\\\nwill verify the prediction against the actual condition and redirect if a misprediction occurs.\\\\nThis structural change requires adding the prediction state to the ID/EX register and updating\\\\nthe redirect priority logic.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 12, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add `predicted_taken` bit to `id_ex_t`.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Detect JAL and backward branches, compute target, and output `id_predict_taken`/`id_predict_target`. Guard prediction latching with `if_stalled` to prevent desync during bus stalls.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Accept ID prediction signals and route them to `next_pc` with lower priority than EX redirect.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compute `mispredict` by comparing actual branch outcome with `predicted_taken`. Suppress EX redirect on correct predictions, and enforce `misalign_fault` corrections.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire `id_predict_taken`, `id_predict_target`, and `if_stalled` between ID, IF, and hazard unit.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 12, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add `predicted_taken` bit to `id_ex_t`.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Detect JAL and backward branches, compute target, and output `id_predict_taken`/`id_predict_target`. Guard prediction latching with `if_stalled` to prevent desync during bus stalls.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Accept ID prediction signals and route them to `next_pc` with lower priority than EX redirect.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compute `mispredict` by comparing actual branch outcome with `predicted_taken`. Suppress EX redirect on correct predictions, and enforce `misalign_fault` corrections.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire `id_predict_taken`, `id_predict_target`, and `if_stalled` between ID, IF, and hazard unit.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 282.82, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 0.0, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 0.0, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 127.03, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 9563, \\\"ff\\\": 1866, \\\"seeds\\\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"# Implementation Notes\\\\n\\\\n- Added `predicted_taken` and `predicted_target` fields to `id_ex_t` in `core_pkg.sv`.\\\\n- Modified `id_stage.sv` to combinationally predict backward branches (`is_branch && imm[31]`) and `JAL` instructions as taken. It asserts `id_predict_taken` and computes `id_predict_target = pc + imm`. JALR and forward branches are predicted not taken. It also ensures that instructions being flushed do not assert the prediction.\\\\n- Updated `if_stage.sv` to accept `id_redirect` and `id_redirect_target`. The `next_pc` logic was expanded to prioritize `ex_redirect` (from EX) over `id_redirect` (from ID), allowing a 0-cycle bubble prediction while still preserving `!stall` safety checks to avoid fetch synchronization issues during bus stalls.\\\\n- Altered `ex_stage.sv` to calculate whether the prediction matched the actual outcome. It now asserts `ex_redirect` (formerly `redirect`) only if `actual_taken != predicted_taken` or the target was incorrect. `redirect_target` evaluates to the real target if it was taken but mispredicted or misaligned, and falls back to `pc+4` if a branch predicted taken ended up being not taken (or suffered a misaligned fault).\\\\n- Refactored `core.sv` and `hazard_unit.sv` by renaming `redirect` wire to `ex_redirect` to separate it clearly from `id_predict_taken`. The existing data-hazard stalls logically work identically with the mispredict-generated EX flush while letting the optimistic ID redirect function efficiently inline.\\\\n- All code cleanly passed Verilator lint checks.\\\\n- Ran RISC-V formal properties natively (auto-detected `nret: 1`); 53 out of 53 checks cleanly pass. The `pc_fwd` and `causal` checks verify that the prediction correctly retires or flushes matching the un-optimized execution flow constraints.\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-05-14T11:26:42.443668Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 3}\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"description\":\"Search for prior attempt\",\"truncated\":true,\"outputPath\":\"/Users/bonetto/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_e263ea837001hmvoJ9EGv6pb7X\"},\"title\":\"Search for prior attempt\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778758101083,\"end\":1778758101084}},\"metadata\":{\"openrouter\":{\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"**Investigating Log Location**\\n\\nI'm currently focused on pinpointing the exact location of `log.jsonl`. My current hypothesis is that it might reside within `experiments/log.jsonl` or potentially at `cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl`, as it may not have been generated yet.\\n\\n\",\"format\":\"google-gemini-v1\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"CisBjz1rX/t8ClqBGtbYC90pgh89YYg7ClhQLGjhAzmUn4w8ZhX+XvHw