four-entry instruction\\nqueue driven by a separate fetch PC. Implement its storage as a normal packed\\narray indexed procedurally by runtime read/write pointers, never as generated\\nhierarchy. A ready-qualified fill may run while downstream is interlocked, and\\ndecode consumes an already buffered instruction during temporary imem stalls.\\nOn an EX redirect, atomically discard all queued entries, reset the pointers\\nand count, and restart the fetch PC at the architectural target; no pre-redirect\\ninstruction may reach ID. This converts available front-end slack into\\ninstruction-stall coverage without putting prediction logic on the PC feedback\\npath or changing the single-retire RVFI boundary.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a fetch-packet bundle carrying PC and instruction, plus queue-size and pointer-width constants.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct fetch payload with a four-entry procedural storage array, runtime read/write pointers, occupancy counter, ready-qualified fill, decode dequeue, and redirect flush.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate raw instruction-bus readiness from decode availability so a nonempty queue can feed ID during an imem stall while preserving memory, load-use, and divider interlocks.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-consume permission and queue-empty state through the front end while retaining EX redirect priority and the nret=1 external contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for runtime pointer wraparound, simultaneous dequeue/fill, imem-stall masking, downstream interlocks, and redirect invalidation with PC/RVFI ordering checks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \