{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg '\\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | jq -r '[.id,.title,.outcome,(.fitness // \\\"na\\\"),(.delta_pct // \\\"na\\\"),(.hypothesis.hypothesis // .hypothesis // \\\"\\\")]|@tsv'\"","aggregated_output":"baseline-bench-2d60805\tBaseline retest for cores/bench\timprovement\t282.82\t0.0\t\nhyp-20260710-001-r1s0\tShare RV32 multiply datapath\timprovement\t306.38\t8.33\tReplace the unconditional signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and\\nsigned-unsigned product expressions with one shared 33x33 unsigned modular\\nmultiplier. Select the operands' sign extension from the decoded multiply\\noperation, then select bits [31:0] for MUL or [63:32] for MULH, MULHU, and\\nMULHSU. The low 64 bits of the 33-bit two's-complement product preserve all\\nRV32M result definitions, while removing two large parallel multiplier\\ncones. Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expressions unchanged.\\n\nhyp-20260710-001-r2s0\tUnsigned multiplier with signed corrections\tregression\t369.9\t20.73\tReplace the sign-selected 33x33 multiplier with one unsigned 32x32 product.\\nUse its low half directly for MUL and its high half for MULHU. For MULH,\\nsubtract operand b from the unsigned high half when a is negative and\\nsubtract operand a when b is negative; for MULHSU subtract b when a is\\nnegative. These modulo-2^32 corrections exactly implement the signed\\nproducts while avoiding sign-extension bits in the multiplier. Preserve the\\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS operations and all division/reminder behavior.\\n\nhyp-20260710-001-r3s0\tRegistered shared multiplier path\tregression\t295.83\t-27.02\tPreserve the validated sign-selected 33x33 multiply arithmetic, but move it\\ninto a small registered blocking multiplier unit. On an RV32M multiply,\\nEX snapshots the fully forwarded operands and operation, stalls younger\\nissue while the unit produces the selected half, then injects one normal\\nEX/MEM result. Ordinary add, logic, shift, address, and branch operations\\nbypass the multiplier entirely. This trades a short fixed latency only for\\nmultiply instructions for a shorter and less congested common EX timing\\npath, analogous to the successful divide isolation without using the\\nregressive unsigned correction network.\\n\nhyp-20260710-001-r4s0\tDecode-aware load-use interlock\tbroken\tna\tna\tMake the load-use hazard detector aware of whether the IF/ID opcode actually\\nconsumes rs1 and/or rs2. Preserve the one-cycle interlock for real dependent\\nconsumers, while suppressing it for operand-immediate ALU operations, loads,\\nJAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, EBREAK, and illegal encodings whose bit fields are\\nnot architectural sources. This removes false bubbles without changing the\\nPC, memory, RVFI, or arithmetic critical paths.\\n\nhyp-20260710-001-r5s0\tExhaustive source-aware load interlock\tbroken\tna\tna\tReplace the raw-field load-use comparison with an exhaustive, opcode-local\\nsource-use table in the hazard unit. Classify rs1 as live only for OP,\\nOP-IMM, LOAD, STORE, BRANCH, and JALR, and rs2 only for OP, STORE, and\\nBRANCH; gate the corresponding comparisons with these bits and IF/ID valid.\\nKeep every true one-cycle load dependency stalled, including all RV32M OP\\noperations, branches, stores, and JALR. This removes false bubbles without\\nadding work to the fetch or EX arithmetic timing paths.\\n\nhyp-20260710-001-r6s0\tShared branch subtract flags\timprovement\t411.5\t1.51\tReplace the six separately expressed branch comparisons with one 33-bit\\nsubtract/flag network in EX. Derive equality from the difference, signed less-\\nthan from operand signs plus the difference sign, and unsigned less-than from\\nthe subtraction borrow; select the requested BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU result.\\nThis should map to one carry-chain-friendly arithmetic cone instead of parallel\\ncomparator logic while retaining the existing EX-stage redirect timing, stalls,\\nand RVFI PC behavior.\\n\nhyp-20260710-001-r7s0\tFixed lane memory extraction\timprovement\t430.45\t4.61\tReplace variable-shift based load extraction and variable-shift byte-mask\\nformation with fixed, address-indexed lane muxes. Select byte data with a\\nfour-arm addr[1:0] case, select aligned halfword data with addr[1], and form\\nSB/SH masks from the same fixed cases. Preserve the existing misalignment\\ntrap and dmem gating exactly, keep word loads/stores direct, and retain all\\nRVFI memory payload semantics. This removes a general 32-bit barrel-shift\\nnetwork from the dmem-return path without changing pipeline timing or IPC.\\n\nhyp-20260710-001-r8s0\tExact source-aware load interlock\tbroken\tna\tna\tDerive explicit uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 signals from the validated decode of\\nthe IF/ID instruction, and gate the existing load-use comparisons with those\\nsignals and IF/ID validity. Classify every architectural source exactly:\\nOP, STORE, and BRANCH use both; OP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR use rs1 only; all\\nremaining legal instructions and traps use neither. Keep the existing\\none-cycle stall for every true dependency, so the MEM/WB forwarding boundary\\nand the dmem-to-EX timing path remain unchanged while false interlocks no\\nlonger cost CoreMark issue cycles.\\n\nhyp-20260710-001-r9s0\tPrecompute PC-relative control targets\tregression\t419.9\t-2.45\tForm and register pc + immediate in ID together with the existing immediate\\nand instruction payload, then use that registered value in EX for branch\\ntargets and direct-JAL targets. Keep JALR's forwarded rs1 + immediate\\ncalculation, branch predicate, redirect timing, misalignment detection, and\\nRVFI pc_wdata semantics unchanged. This relocates a 32-bit adder from the\\nbranch decision/redirect path into the earlier ID-to-ID/EX path, where it is\\nindependent of forwarding and branch comparison, reducing the critical\\ncontrol-flow cone while preserving the pipeline's current IPC.\\n\nhyp-20260711-001-r10s0\tShare ALU barrel shifter\tregression\t412.88\t-4.08\tReplace the three variable-shift expressions with one right-shift barrel\\ndatapath. For SLL, reverse the operand bits before the shared logical\\nright shift and reverse the result afterward; for SRL and SRA, feed the\\noperand directly and select zero or sign fill. Bit reversal is pure wiring,\\nso this removes duplicate wide shift-mux cones while preserving one-cycle\\nALU latency, forwarding, branch timing, and every RV32I shift result.\\n\nhyp-20260711-001-r11s0\tDecoder-owned load-use source masks\tbroken\tna\tna\tMake the validated decoder the single source of uses_rs1 and uses_rs2\\nmetadata, then carry those bits with the IF/ID payload to gate the existing\\nload-use comparisons. Classify OP, STORE, and BRANCH as two-source;\\nOP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR as rs1-only; and JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, and EBREAK\\nas source-free. Illegal or unrecognized encodings remain conservatively\\ntwo-source so the interlock cannot weaken trap-path operand capture. This\\nremoves only false bubbles while retaining the current pipeline, forwarding,\\nmemory timing, RVFI payload, and all true load dependencies.\\n\nhyp-20260711-001-r12s0\tValidity-masked LUTRAM register file\tregression\t377.26\t-12.36\tKeep architectural reset semantics with a resettable 32-bit valid bitmap,\\nwhile leaving the 32-bit register-data array unreset and marking it for\\ndistributed RAM inference. Reads from invalid entries return zero, and a\\nsame-cycle write remains the highest-priority bypass, so x0, reset, and\\nwrite-first behavior remain identical. This removes reset fanout and should\\nmap the two asynchronous read ports to a shallower LUTRAM implementation,\\nimproving Fmax without adding pipeline latency or changing RVFI state.\\n\nhyp-20260711-001-r13s0\tShare PC-relative target adder\tregression\t380.36\t-11.64\tMaterialize one pc-relative target wire in EX and use it for both conditional\\nbranch targets and non-JALR jump targets, including the EX/MEM branch-target\\nmetadata. Keep JALR on its independent forwarded rs1 + immediate path and\\nretain the existing misalignment and redirect semantics. Making this common\\nsubexpression explicit should force one carry-chain-friendly adder rather\\nthan duplicate arithmetic and routing, improving Fmax without changing IPC\\nor moving any control decision earlier in the pipeline.\\n\nhyp-20260711-001-r14s0\tRVFI-safe source-masked load interlock\tbroken\tna\tna\tDefine validated uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 metadata once for each legal RV32IM\\nopcode/funct combination, then use it in both the load-use interlock and\\nID/EX operand capture. OP, STORE, and BRANCH keep two live sources;\\nOP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR keep rs1 only; JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, EBREAK, and\\ntraps have no live sources. Mask an unused source address and value to x0\\nbefore ID/EX so forwarding and RVFI cannot observe a stale pseudo-source.\\nThis removes only provably false load-use bubbles while preserving every\\ntrue dependency, the existing MEM-to-EX timing boundary, and trap safety.\\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
