/worktrees/hyp-20260711-001-r11s0/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-51902/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 11}\n41:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r14s0\", \"title\": \"RVFI-safe source-masked load interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock compares both raw register-field positions of every\\nIF/ID word, so immediate fields and source-free instructions can create\\nbubbles after a load. Earlier source-aware attempts failed formal because\\nsuppressing a stall while retaining a pseudo-source let stale data reach\\nthe RVFI source payload.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock compares both raw register-field positions of every\\nIF/ID word, so immediate fields and source-free instructions can create\\nbubbles after a load. Earlier source-aware attempts failed formal because\\nsuppressing a stall while retaining a pseudo-source let stale data reach\\nthe RVFI source payload.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Define validated uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 metadata once for each legal RV32IM\\nopcode/funct combination, then use it in both the load-use interlock and\\nID/EX operand capture. OP, STORE, and BRANCH keep two live sources;\\nOP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR keep rs1 only; JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, EBREAK, and\\ntraps have no live sources. Mask an unused source address and value to x0\\nbefore ID/EX so forwarding and RVFI cannot observe a stale pseudo-source.\\nThis removes only provably false load-use bubbles while preserving every\\ntrue dependency, the existing MEM-to-EX timing boundary, and trap safety.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/source_use.sv\", \"description\": \"Add one validated RV32IM source-use classifier shared by decode capture and hazard logic, with conservative source use for any encoding not explicitly accepted.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use source-use metadata to mask unused rs addresses and data to x0 as ID/EX is captured, keeping forwarding and RVFI source payloads architecturally safe.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each raw-field load-use comparison with the shared source-use result and IF/ID validity, retaining the existing one-cycle interlock for every real consumer.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the IF/ID instruction and source-use qualification into the hazard path without changing the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add load-followed-by-immediate, load-followed-by-source-free, and true rs1/rs2 dependency tests that check retirement and RVFI source fields.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/source_use.sv\", \"description\": \"Add one validated RV32IM source-use classifier shared by decode capture and hazard logic, with conservative source use for any encoding not explicitly accepted.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use source-use metadata to mask unused rs addresses and data to x0 as ID/EX is captured, keeping forwarding and RVFI source payloads architecturally safe.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each raw-field load-use comparison with the shared source-use result and IF/ID validity, retaining the existing one-cycle interlock for every real consumer.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the IF/ID instruction and source-use qualification into the hazard path without changing the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add load-followed-by-immediate, load-followed-by-source-free, and true rs1/rs2 dependency tests that check retirement and RVFI source fields.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 14}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
