{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id == \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\\\") | {id,title,hypothesis,fitness,delta_pct,fmax_mhz,ipc_coremark,cycles,lut4,ff,implementation_notes,lesson}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\",\"title\":\"Cold iterative high-half multiply unit\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The shared signed 33x33 multiplier is present on every EX-stage cycle even\\nthough CoreMark primarily needs the low-half MUL result. The signed and\\nunsigned high-half variants are substantially colder compiler operations,\\nyet their operand-selection and wide-product cone remain on the common\\nALU timing path after divide/remainder have already been isolated.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Keep architectural MUL as a one-cycle unsigned low-32-bit product, whose\\nresult is independent of operand signedness, and dispatch MULH, MULHU, and\\nMULHSU to a blocking iterative high-product unit. The unit snapshots its\\noperands and signedness, performs a shift/add product over multiple cycles,\\nthen injects the required high half through the normal EX/MEM path while\\nyounger issue is interlocked. This removes the 33-bit signed product and\\nhigh-half selection logic from every ordinary EX cycle; the occasional\\nmulti-cycle high multiply should be amortized by the improved Fmax.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Make the fast MUL path a low-half unsigned product and remove real high-half multiply selection from the common combinational ALU cone, while retaining the matching ALTOPS behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mulhi_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a signedness-aware iterative high-half multiplier with start/busy/done/result handshake and ALTOPS-compatible formal behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Dispatch MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU to the new unit, snapshot forwarded operand metadata, and insert its completed result into EX/MEM exactly once.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the long-operation interlock so a high-half multiply freezes younger issue without replaying or duplicating retirements.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the high-half-multiply busy indication into the existing global execute-stall control without changing the nret=1 interface.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_alu.py\",\"description\":\"Keep exact low-half MUL checks and add directed MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU signedness and edge-case vectors through the iterative execution path.\"}]},\"fitness\":349.82,\"delta_pct\":-13.7,\"fmax_mhz\":157.13,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4491735,\"lut4\":6385,\"ff\":2585,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"lesson\":null}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
