ng a store while its request can outlive or be overwritten by younger MEM traffic violates architectural load/store ordering and register-state checks.\\\"}\\n21:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"MEM-to-EX load forwarding\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The present five-stage pipeline unconditionally injects a bubble for every\\\\nadjacent load consumer, even though the benchmark memory is zero-wait when\\\\nio_dmemReady is asserted. CoreMark's pointer, list, and matrix kernels use\\\\nmany load-dependent address and arithmetic chains, so this fixed IPC loss is\\\\na more direct target than another speculative front-end structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The present five-stage pipeline unconditionally injects a bubble for every\\\\nadjacent load consumer, even though the benchmark memory is zero-wait when\\\\nio_dmemReady is asserted. CoreMark's pointer, list, and matrix kernels use\\\\nmany load-dependent address and arithmetic chains, so this fixed IPC loss is\\\\na more direct target than another speculative front-end structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Restructure the load-result path so the combinationally extracted MEM-stage\\\\nload value can bypass directly to the simultaneously executing dependent\\\\ninstruction in EX. Remove the ordinary one-cycle load-use bubble, but only\\\\npermit that bypass when the older load is in EX/MEM and dmem is ready; on a\\\\ndmem stall, retain the existing pipeline hold until the response is valid.\\\\nThe normal MEM/WB forwarding remains as the fallback for older loads, and\\\\nRVFI continues to retire the original load and dependent instruction in\\\\nprogram order. This should improve CoreMark iterations per cycle without\\\\nadding predictor state or changing the external memory or RVFI contracts.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the already computed sign/zero-extended load result as a valid-qualified combinational bypass value alongside the registered MEM/WB payload.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM-load forwarding selection that chooses the MEM-stage load bypass instead of the EX/MEM address result.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Accept the MEM-stage load bypass operand and select it for either source before ALU, branch, store-data, and RVFI source-value capture.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove the default adjacent load-use bubble while preserving the dmem-ready-qualified full-pipeline hold that prevents a consumer from advancing before its load response exists.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the MEM-stage bypass data and load-valid qualification into execute forwarding and retain existing redirect, divider, and dmem-stall priorities.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_mem_stage.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed load-to-ALU, load-to-branch, load-to-store-data, byte/halfword extension, and delayed-dmem-response cases that verify no stale operand reaches EX or RVFI.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the already computed sign/zero-extended load result as a valid-qualified combinational bypass value alongside the registered MEM/WB payload.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM-load forwarding selection that chooses the MEM-stage load bypass instead of the EX/MEM address result.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Accept the MEM-stage load bypass operand and select it for either source before ALU, branch, store-data, and RVFI source-value capture.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove the default adjacent load-use bubble while preserving the dmem-ready-qualified full-pipeline hold that prevents a consumer from advancing before its load response exists.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the MEM-stage bypass data and load-valid qualification into execute forwarding and retain existing redirect, divider, and dmem-stall priorities.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_mem_stage.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed load-to-ALU, load-to-branch, load-to-store-data, byte/halfword extension, and delayed-dmem-response cases that verify no stale operand reaches EX or RVFI.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 364.7, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -11.37, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 28.95, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 156.37, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4287593, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 5875, \\\"ff\\\": 2200, \\\"seeds\\\": [156.37, 161.63, 153.16], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T02:32:59.674616Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 7, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r7s1 (regression, -11.37%): Zero-wait MEM-to-EX forwarding creates a dmem-return-to-load-format-to-operand-mux-to-ALU critical path, so CoreMark's saved load-use bubbles can be outweighed by Fmax loss unless the load response is timing-isolated.\\\"}\\n24:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Decode-accepted direct JAL redirect\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Every direct JAL has a PC-relative target encoded in its own instruction, but\\\\nthe current pipeline waits until EX to redirect it and discards younger\\\\nfall-through work. CoreMark uses calls and helper loops often enough that\\\\nthis fixed, non-speculative control penalty is worth removing.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Every direct JAL has a PC-relative target encoded in its own instruction, but\\\\nthe current pipeline waits until EX to redirect it and discards younger\\\\nfall-through work. CoreMark uses calls and helper loops often enough that\\\\nthis fixed, non-speculative control penalty is worth removing.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Resolve only direct JAL in decode when that instruction is accepted into\\\\nID/EX. Form its immediate target from the fetched instruction and update the\\\\nfetch PC at the same edge, while carrying an already-redirected bit so EX\\\\npreserves the JAL RVFI pc_wdata and return-address result without issuing a\\\\nsecond redirect. Leave conditional branches and JALR in EX, avoiding the\\\\ncostly decode-stage comparator and operand-forwarding network that made the\\\\nearlier full branch-resolution attempt fragile. Gate the early redirect on\\\\nID acceptance and give an older EX redirect priority across all stalls.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add ID/EX metadata marking a direct JAL whose fetch redirect was accepted in decode.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Recognize valid direct JAL instructions, form the PC-relative target, and emit an acceptance-qualified early-redirect request while latching its metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Separate PC-update redirect selection from EX wrong-path output squashing so an accepted decode-stage JAL is retained while the PC advances to its target.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Suppress only the duplicate EX redirect for a JAL already redirected in decode; retain JAL result, RVFI pc_wdata, JALR, and branch behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose or qualify the ID acceptance condition so early JAL redirection cannot occur while ID/EX is held or an older EX redirect squashes it.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Arbitrate older EX recovery ahead of an accepted decode-stage JAL redirect and wire the split fetch-control paths without changing the nret=1 interface.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_core.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed JAL call/return, consecutive JAL, load-use hold, dmem-stall, and simultaneous older-redirect cases that check RVFI PC order and return-address writes.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add ID/EX metadata marking a direct JAL whose fetch redirect was accepted in decode.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Recognize valid direct JAL instructions, form the PC-relative target, and emit an acceptance-qualified early-redirect request while latching its metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Separate PC-update redirect selection from EX wrong-path output squashing so an accepted decode-stage JAL is retained while the PC advances to its target.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Suppress only the duplicate EX redirect for a JAL already redirected in decode; retain JAL result, RVFI pc_wdata, JALR, and branch behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose or qualify the ID acceptance condition so early JAL redirection cannot occur while ID/EX is held or an older EX redirect squashes it.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Arbitrate older EX recovery ahead of an accepted decode-stage JAL redirect and wire the split fetch-control paths without changing the nret=1 interface.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_core.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed JAL call/return, consecutive JAL, load-use hold, dmem-stall, and simultaneous older-redirect cases that check RVFI PC order and return-address writes.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 161.77, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -62.42, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": -42.8, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 71.86, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4442158, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 5736, \\\"ff\\\": 2199, \\\"seeds\\\": [70.77, 71.86, 73.86], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T02:44:32.240279Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 8}\\n27:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r9s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"In-order memory completion queue\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The injected dmem backpressure currently freezes every pipeline stage as\\\\nsoon as a load or store reaches EX/MEM. Most stalls are short, but they\\\\nprevent independent younger ALU work from advancing and make memory\\\\nhandshaking part of the pipeline-wide enable network. The earlier store\\\\nbuffer failed because it allowed a store to retire before the externally\\\\nordered transaction completed, not because overlap itself is invalid.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The injected dmem backpressure currently freezes every pipeline stage as\\\\nsoon as a load or store reaches EX/MEM. Most stalls are short, but they\\\\nprevent independent younger ALU work from advancing and make memory\\\\nhandshaking part of the pipeline-wide enable network. The earlier store\\\\nbuffer failed because it allowed a store to retire before the externally\\\\nordered transaction completed, not because overlap itself is invalid.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace the single coupled MEM/WB boundary with a two-entry in-order\\\\ncompletion queue. A memory operation occupies the head entry until its\\\\ndmem handshake completes; its RVFI record and architectural retirement\\\\noccur only after that completion. While the head is waiting, one younger\\\\nnon-memory EX result may enter the second entry, but cannot retire early.\\\\nLoads and stores behind an unresolved memory head remain interlocked, and\\\\nstore data/masks stay stable until acknowledgement. This isolates short\\\\ndmem waits from EX and decode, preserves strictly ordered RVFI retirement\\\\nand memory visibility, and avoids putting a dmem-return forwarding cone on\\\\nthe EX path.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Define a compact completion-entry payload with execution, memory, and RVFI fields plus explicit ready/valid state for two in-order slots.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Convert the coupled MEM/WB register into the completion-queue producer: hold a memory head until its bus handshake, snapshot its RVFI memory payload, and admit only an ordering-safe younger result.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/wb_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Consume only the queue head for register-file writeback and expose a head-retire record so no younger completed instruction can write or retire first.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace blanket dmem pipeline freezing with queue-capacity and memory-order interlocks; preserve load-use, redirect, divide, and bus-stall priorities.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the completion queue, head-only RVFI retirement, writeback, and backpressure controls while retaining the nret=1 top-level contract.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"descriptio