 from every ordinary EX cycle; the occasional\\\\nmulti-cycle high multiply should be amortized by the improved Fmax.\\\\n\\\",\\\"expected_impact\\\":{\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\":5,\\\"confidence\\\":\\\"medium\\\"},\\\"changes\\\":[{\\\"file\\\":\\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Make the fast MUL path a low-half unsigned product and remove real high-half multiply selection from the common combinational ALU cone, while retaining the matching ALTOPS behavior.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"rtl/mulhi_unit.sv\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Add a signedness-aware iterative high-half multiplier with start/busy/done/result handshake and ALTOPS-compatible formal behavior.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Dispatch MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU to the new unit, snapshot forwarded operand metadata, and insert its completed result into EX/MEM exactly once.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Extend the long-operation interlock so a high-half multiply freezes younger issue without replaying or duplicating retirements.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"rtl/core.sv\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Wire the high-half-multiply busy indication into the existing global execute-stall control without changing the nret=1 interface.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"test/test_alu.py\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Keep exact low-half MUL checks and add directed MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU signedness and edge-case vectors through the iterative execution path.\\\"}]},\\\"fitness\\\":349.82,\\\"delta_pct\\\":-13.7,\\\"fmax_mhz\\\":157.13,\\\"ipc_coremark\\\":0.000002,\\\"cycles\\\":4491735,\\\"lut4\\\":6385,\\\"ff\\\":2585,\\\"implementation_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"lesson\\\":null}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"find cores/bench/experiments -maxdepth 3 -type f | sed -n '1,160p'; rg -n -i 'dsp|multiplier|critical|timing|fmax' cores/benc