byte or halfword load from combinational dmem data. On the FPGA benchmark\\n  wrapper this sits directly after the dmem read mux and before MEM/WB state,\\n  so its barrel-mux cone can constrain Fmax for a result that needs only one\\n  of four fixed byte lanes or one of two aligned halfword lanes.\\nhypothesis: |\\n  Replace variable-shift based load extraction and variable-shift byte-mask\\n  formation with fixed, address-indexed lane muxes. Select byte data with a\\n  four-arm addr[1:0] case, select aligned halfword data with addr[1], and form\\n  SB/SH masks from the same fixed cases. Preserve the existing misalignment\\n  trap and dmem gating exactly, keep word loads/stores direct, and retain all\\n  RVFI memory payload semantics. This removes a general 32-bit barrel-shift\\n  network from the dmem-return path without changing pipeline timing or IPC.\\nexpected_impact:\\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\\n  confidence: medium\\nchanges:\\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\\n    description: \\\"Replace variable right-shift load extraction and shifted byte-mask expressions with fixed byte/halfword lane muxes while retaining alignment traps, dmem outputs, and RVFI masks.\\\"\\n  - file: test/test_mem_stage.py\\n    description: \\\"Add exhaustive byte-lane and aligned-halfword load/store checks, including sign extension, masks, and misaligned-access dmem gating.\\\"\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\n  \"iterations\": 28,\n  \"accepted\": 5,\n  \"rejected\": 12,\n  \"broken\": 11,\n  \"broken_by_class\": {\n    \"formal_failed\": 10,\n    \"build_failed\": 1\n  },\n  \"baseline_fitness\": 282.82,\n  \"final_fitness\": 430.45,\n  \"best_fitness\": 430.45,\n  \"best_round\": 20,\n  \"delta_pct\": 52.19927869316173,\n  \"best_lut4\": 5763,\n  \"best_ff\": 2216,\n  \"best_fmax_mhz\": 193.35,\n  \"best_iterations\": 10,\n  \"best_cycles\": 4491817,\n  \"best_ipc_coremark\": 2e-06\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
