{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i \\\"structural|hyp-20260711-002-r10s1|hyp-20260710-002-r9s1|hyp-20260710-001-r3s0|elastic|completion|pipeline|fetch\\\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md && sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/LESSONS.md && rg -n -i '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"|category: structural' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/LESSONS.md:2:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, -10.84%): A combinational BTFNT predictor that derives the PC update from imem_data puts instruction fetch, branch decode, immediate extraction, and target addition on the IF-to-PC feedback path, so it must be pipelined or decoupled when its Fmax loss exceeds CoreMark's saved redirect bubbles.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:5:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (regression, +0.69%): Removing imem_data from branch prediction is insufficient when a combinational PC-indexed BTB tag match, counter read, and next-PC mux remain on the fetch feedback path; CoreMark's saved loop-back bubbles did not amortize that added front-end cost.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:6:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r3s0 (regression, -27.02%): Registering a blocking 33x33 multiplier without splitting its arithmetic only moves the full-cycle product into a new register-to-register cone while adding EX ownership and interlock logic, so it cannot deliver the divide unit's Fmax benefit without real pipelining or iteration.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:7:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): A sequential fetch FIFO must index its storage procedurally with runtime read/write pointers; generate-block hierarchy and prefixes are elaboration-time constructs and reject dynamic queue indices before synthesis.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:9:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (regression, -18.56%): A four-entry procedural IF queue can lose CoreMark fitness when its pointer/count, dequeue arbitration, and redirect-flush control cost more than the transient imem stalls that prefetch can cover, so front-end decoupling needs measured slack rather than assumed stall hiding.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:10:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r5s2 (broken, n/a): A registered lookahead BTB must treat its response PC and predicted next PC as a fetch-acceptance transaction, invalidating or holding them consistently across redirects and stalls, or stale predictions can misassociate with conditional branches and violate RVFI control-flow checks.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:13:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 (broken, n/a): A PC-only branch predictor must validate the fetched instruction's branch identity or rely on immutable instruction memory, because formal's per-cycle symbolic imem can reuse a trained PC for a non-branch and make the predictor skip its required PC+4.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:16:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r8s2 (broken, n/a): A signature-mismatched conditional-branch prediction must redirect to the resolved PC+4 even when the branch is not taken, because treating it as a cold not-taken branch without recovery leaves the already-applied stale taken target on the fetch path and violates RVFI PC-forward progress.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:17:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r9s1 (broken, n/a): A decoupled in-order completion queue must make dequeue an atomic retirement event for RVFI payload/order, register-file writeback, and PC-forward state, because separate retire and commit views can misalign architectural instruction state across queue transitions.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:20:- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r10s1 (broken, n/a): A one-entry elastic IF/ID boundary must make fetch fill/dequeue and ID/EX advancement a single valid-ready transaction, because consuming or refilling an entry out of step with decode can misassociate instruction state and break RVFI PC-forward, register, and liveness checks.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:21:- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r10s2 (broken, n/a): A decode-stage branch prediction redirect must atomically invalidate or suppress the already-issued sequential fetch payload, because otherwise a fall-through instruction can survive alongside the predicted target and widespread conditional-branch RVFI PC checks fail.\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Decode-stage branch resolution\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Restructure the front end so conditional branches resolve in decode using\\nthe register-file read values and explicit bypasses from EX/MEM and WB.\\nRedirect the PC and squash only the fetched wrong-path instruction in the\\nsame decode cycle; retain EX resolution for JALR and preserve a targeted\\nload-to-branch interlock until load data is available. This removes one\\nrecovery cycle for the common backward conditional branch while retaining\\nsingle-retire RVFI ordering and the existing memory interface.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide decode-stage bypass selects so branches compare the architecturally newest operands.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide decode-stage bypass selects so branches compare the architecturally newest operands.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\ng trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Status: failed\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:18 (18)\\nSBY 21:54:54 [