ktrees/hyp-20260711-002-r10s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-27262/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r10s1 (broken, n/a): A one-entry elastic IF/ID boundary must make fetch fill/dequeue and ID/EX advancement a single valid-ready transaction, because consuming or refilling an entry out of step with decode can misassociate instruction state and break RVFI PC-forward, register, and liveness checks.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\"structural\\\") | [.id, .title, .outcome, (.fitness // \\\"-\\\"), (.delta_pct // \\\"-\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && jq -r 'select(.id == \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r8s0\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r8s2\\\") | [.id,.title,.category,.outcome,.hypothesis.hypothesis] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\"structural\\\") | [.id, .title, .outcome, (.fitness // \\\"-\\\"), (.delta_pct // \\\"-\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && jq -r 'select(.id == \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r8s0\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r8s2\\\") | [.id,.title,.category,.outcome,.hypothesis.hypothesis] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\tDecode-stage branch resolution\tbroken\t-\t-\nhyp-20260710-002-r2s1\tDecoupled iterative divide unit\timprovement\t405.36\t32.31\nhyp-20260710-002-r3s1\tDecoupled sequential fetch queue\tbroken\t-\t-\nhyp-20260710-002-r4s1\tProcedural decoupled instruction queue\tregression\t330.11\t-18.56\nhyp-20260710-002-r5s1\tCold iterative high-half multiply unit\tregression\t349.82\t-13.7\nhyp-20260710-002-r6s1\tOrdered one-entry store buffer\tbroken\t-\t-\nhyp-20260710-002-r7s1\tMEM-to-EX load forwarding\tregression\t364.7\t-11.37\nhyp-20260710-002-r8s1\tDecode-accepted direct JAL redirect\tregression\t161.77\t-62.42\nhyp-20260710-002-r9s1\tIn-order memory completion queue\tbroken\t-\t-\nhyp-20260711-002-r10s1\tElastic registered fetch boundary\tbroken\t-\t-\nhyp-20260710-001-r8s0\tExact source-aware load interlock\tmicro_opt\tbroken\tDerive explicit uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 signals from the validated decode of\\nthe IF/ID instruction, and gate the existing load-use comparisons with those\\nsignals and IF/ID validity. Classify every architectural source exactly:\\nOP, STORE, and BRANCH use both; OP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR use rs1 only; all\\nremaining legal instructions and traps use neither. Keep the existing\\none-cycle stall for every true dependency, so the MEM/WB forwarding boundary\\nand the dmem-to-EX timing path remain unchanged while false interlocks no\\nlonger cost CoreMark issue cycles.\\n\nhyp-20260710-002-r8s1\tDecode-accepted direct JAL redirect\tstructural\tregression\tResolve only direct JAL in decode when that instruction is accepted into\\nID/EX. Form its immediate target from the fetched instruction and update the\\nfetch PC at the same edge, while carrying an already-redirected bit so EX\\npreserves the JAL RVFI pc_wdata and return-address result without issuing a\\nsecond redirect. Leave conditional branches and JALR in EX, avoiding the\\ncostly decode-stage comparator and operand-forwarding network that made the\\nearlier full branch-resolution attempt fragile. Gate the early redirect on\\nID acceptance and give an older EX redirect priority across all stalls.\\n\nhyp-20260710-003-r8s2\tSignature-qualified loop predictor\tpredictor\tbroken\tAdd a one-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor that stores branch\\nPC, target, direction, and the resolved instruction word as a signature.\\nIF uses only registered PC equality, direction, and target muxing to select\\nthe speculative successor; the instruction signature is carried as\\nsideband validation metadata and is not placed in the PC-select cone. EX\\nretains architectural branch resolution and redirects only for a predicted\\ncontrol instruction whose resolved successor differs, or for a predicted\\nhit that resolves as a non-branch (including a symbolic-imem signature\\nmismatch), explicitly restoring PC+4. This avoids assuming PC identity\\nproves instruction identity, while replacing the prior universal 32-bit\\nnext-PC compare with narrow prediction-valid/control-qualified recovery.\\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
