SCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mul_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a two-stage signedness-selected partial-product multiplier with operand/result registers, RV32M high/low selection, and a start/busy/done handshake.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch all MUL-family operations to the new unit, snapshot forwarded sources and instruction metadata, and emit the completed result into EX/MEM exactly once.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the long-operation interlock for the multiplier's two-stage lifecycle while preserving load-use, redirect, divide, and dmem-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire multiplier busy/completion control into execute and global stall signals without changing the nret=1 interface or RVFI retirement boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add exact RV32M multiply high/low corner and randomized vectors, including dependent consumers and consecutive multiply retirement ordering.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the real 33x33 product from the fast ALU and retain only non-multiply operations plus matching RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mul_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a two-stage signedness-selected partial-product multiplier with operand/result registers, RV32M high/low selection, and a start/busy/done handshake.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch all MUL-family operations to the new unit, snapshot forwarded sources and instruction metadata, and emit the completed result into EX/MEM exactly once.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the long-operation interlock for the multiplier's two-stage lifecycle while preserving load-use, redirect, divide, and dmem-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire multiplier busy/completion control into execute and global stall signals without changing the nret=1 interface or RVFI retirement boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add exact RV32M multiply high/low corner and randomized vectors, including dependent consumers and consecutive multiply retirement ordering.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 355.48, \"delta_pct\": -17.42, \"vs_baseline\": 25.69, \"fmax_mhz\": 166.39, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4680666, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6224, \"ff\": 2556, \"seeds\": [177.3, 166.39, 160.15], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T03:22:53.733150Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r11s1 (regression, -17.42%): Splitting RV32M multiplication into parallel partial products and a blocking recombination stage can still regress CoreMark when the extra EX interlock and wide shifted-sum reduction cost more than removing the monolithic multiplier from the normal ALU cone, especially for sparse multiplies.\"}\n34:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r11s2\", \"title\": \"Atomic registered BTFNT front end\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly takes backward conditional loop branches, while the\\ncurrent EX-stage resolver fetches two sequential wrong-path instructions.\\nEarlier fetch predictors hurt Fmax by extending the PC feedback path, and\\nthe prior registered decode predictor failed because its sequential fetch\\npayload was not invalidated atomically with a predicted redirect.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly takes backward conditional loop branches, while the\\ncurrent EX-stage resolver fetches two sequential wrong-path instructions.\\nEarlier fetch predictors hurt Fmax by extending the PC feedback path, and\\nthe prior registered decode predictor failed because its sequential fetch\\npayload was not invalidated atomically with a predicted redirect.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Insert one stall-aware registered IF/ID fetch payload and perform static\\nbackward-taken, forward-not-taken prediction only when that registered,\\nvalid instruction decodes as a conditional branch with a negative B\\nimmediate. Treat prediction as an atomic valid-ready transaction: when\\ndecode advances the predicted branch into ID/EX, replace the concurrently\\nissued sequential fetch payload with an invalid entry and redirect the PC\\nto the predicted target. Carry branch-only prediction metadata to EX;\\nEX recovers on a direction or target mismatch, while unpredicted\\ninstructions retain normal PC+4 behavior without a universal successor\\ncomparator. This removes hot loop-back recovery work while keeping\\ninstruction decode and target formation behind the fetch register.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add IF/ID registered-payload and branch-only prediction metadata fields, including the predicted successor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-entry stall-aware IF/ID register whose fill, dequeue, predicted redirect, EX recovery, and invalidation follow one atomic acceptance protocol.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect valid backward conditional branches from the registered payload, form their target, and emit prediction only when the payload advances into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry qualified branch prediction metadata and recover only a resolved predicted branch whose direction or target disagrees.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define ready/hold and redirect precedence so load-use, bus stalls, divider ownership, prediction, and EX recovery cannot consume or retain a wrong-path fetch entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the atomic fetch transaction, prediction metadata, and EX recovery while preserving the existing single-retire RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem/dmem-stall, and divide-hold tests that verify no sequential payload retires after a predicted redirect.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add IF/ID registered-payload and branch-only prediction metadata fields, including the predicted successor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-entry stall-aware IF/ID register whose fill, dequeue, predicted redirect, EX recovery, and invalidation follow one atomic acceptance protocol.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect valid backward conditional branches from the registered payload, form their target, and emit prediction only when the payload advances into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry qualified branch prediction metadata and recover only a resolved predicted branch whose direction or target disagrees.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define ready/hold and redirect precedence so load-use, bus stalls, divider ownership, prediction, and EX recovery cannot consume or retain a wrong-path fetch entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the atomic fetch transaction, prediction metadata, and EX recovery while preserving the existing single-retire RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem/dmem-stall, and divide-hold tests that verify no sequential payload retires after a predicted redirect.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\":