{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.fitness \"'!= null) | [.fitness,.id,.category,.title,.fmax_mhz,.cycles] | @tsv'\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | sort -nr | head -12 && jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\\\") | .hypothesis.hypothesis, .implementation_notes' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"430.45\thyp-20260710-001-r7s0\tmicro_opt\tFixed lane memory extraction\t193.35\t4491817\n419.9\thyp-20260710-001-r9s0\tmicro_opt\tPrecompute PC-relative control targets\t188.61\t4491817\n412.88\thyp-20260711-001-r10s0\tmicro_opt\tShare ALU barrel shifter\t185.46\t4491817\n411.5\thyp-20260710-001-r6s0\tmicro_opt\tShared branch subtract flags\t184.84\t4491817\n405.36\thyp-20260710-002-r2s1\tstructural\tDecoupled iterative divide unit\t182.08\t4491817\n377.26\thyp-20260711-001-r12s0\tmicro_opt\tValidity-masked LUTRAM register file\t169.46\t4491817\n369.9\thyp-20260710-001-r2s0\tmicro_opt\tUnsigned multiplier with signed corrections\t166.14\t4491485\n364.95\thyp-20260710-003-r4s2\tpredictor\tReturn-address-stack fetch predictor\t163.43\t4478102\n364.7\thyp-20260710-002-r7s1\tstructural\tMEM-to-EX load forwarding\t156.37\t4287593\n358.51\thyp-20260711-003-r12s2\tpredictor\tAtomic single-ahead BTFNT predictor\t167.56\t4673734\n355.48\thyp-20260711-002-r11s1\tstructural\tTwo-stage partial-product multiplier\t166.39\t4680666\n349.82\thyp-20260710-002-r5s1\tstructural\tCold iterative high-half multiply unit\t157.13\t4491735\nKeep architectural MUL as a one-cycle unsigned low-32-bit product, whose\nresult is independent of operand signedness, and dispatch MULH, MULHU, and\nMULHSU to a blocking iterative high-product unit. The unit snapshots its\noperands and signedness, performs a shift/add product over multiple cycles,\nthen injects the required high half through the normal EX/MEM path while\nyounger issue is interlocked. This removes the 33-bit signed product and\nhigh-half selection logic from every ordinary EX cycle; the occasional\nmulti-cycle high multiply should be amortized by the improved Fmax.\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
