rt fetch at the architectural target. This adds only a compact\\nready/valid boundary, breaks the imem-to-decode critical path, and can\\nabsorb one instruction response while the back end is stalled without\\nchanging in-order execution or the RVFI retirement boundary.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the combinational fetch payload with a one-entry registered elastic buffer, independent fetch PC, ready-qualified fill, simultaneous consume/refill, and redirect invalidation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the registered fetch payload and decode-consume handshake while preserving EX redirect priority and the nret=1 port contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Distinguish instruction-buffer availability from raw imem readiness so a buffered instruction may issue during an imem stall while load, dmem, and divide interlocks retain their existing priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose acceptance/backpressure for the registered fetch entry without changing decode legality, operand capture, or the ID/EX retirement payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for fill, hold, simultaneous dequeue/refill, imem backpressure, downstream stalls, and redirect flushing with preserved PC order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the combinational fetch payload with a one-entry registered elastic buffer, independent fetch PC, ready-qualified fill, simultaneous consume/refill, and redirect invalidation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the registered fetch payload and decode-consume handshake while preserving EX redirect priority and the nret=1 port contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv