e injected dmem backpressure currently freezes every pipeline stage as\\nsoon as a load or store reaches EX/MEM. Most stalls are short, but they\\nprevent independent younger ALU work from advancing and make memory\\nhandshaking part of the pipeline-wide enable network. The earlier store\\nbuffer failed because it allowed a store to retire before the externally\\nordered transaction completed, not because overlap itself is invalid.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the single coupled MEM/WB boundary with a two-entry in-order\\ncompletion queue. A memory operation occupies the head entry until its\\ndmem handshake completes; its RVFI record and architectural retirement\\noccur only after that completion. While the head is waiting, one younger\\nnon-memory EX result may enter the second entry, but cannot retire early.\\nLoads and stores behind an unresolved memory head remain interlocked, and\\nstore data/masks stay stable until acknowledgement. This isolates short\\ndmem waits from EX and decode, preserves strictly ordered RVFI retirement\\nand memory visibility, and avoids putting a dmem-return forwarding cone on\\nthe EX path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a compact completion-entry payload with execution, memory, and RVFI fields plus explicit ready/valid state for two in-order slots.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Convert the coupled MEM/WB register into the completion-queue producer: hold a memory head until its bus handshake, snapshot its RVFI memory payload, and admit only an ordering-safe younger result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume only the queue head for register-file writeback and expose a head-retire record so no younger completed instruction can write or retire first.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace blanket dmem pipeline freezing with queue-capacity and memory-order interlocks; preserve load-use, redirect, divide, and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the completion queue, head-only RVFI retirement, writeback, and backpressure controls while retaining the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add delayed-load and delayed-store sequences with independent younger ALU work, dependent accesses, and RVFI-order checks proving ordered retirement and stable requests.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a compact completion-entry payload with execution, memory, and RVFI fields plus explicit ready/valid state for two in-order slots.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Convert the coupled MEM/WB register into the completion-queue producer: hold a memory head until its bus handshake, snapshot its RVFI memory payload, and admit only an ordering-safe younger result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume only the queue head for register-file writeback and expose a head-retire record so no younger completed instruction can write or retire first.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace blanket dmem pipeline freezing with queue-capacity and memory-order interlocks; preserve load-use, redirect, divide, and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the completion queue, head-only RVFI retirement, writeback, and backpressure controls while retaining the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add delayed-load and delayed-store sequences with independent younger ALU work, dependent accesses, and RVFI-order checks proving ordered retirement and stable requests.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_faile