\nselects the next PC. CoreMark frequently executes loop-control branches, so\\nshortening this registered EX-to-PC feedback path can raise Fmax without\\nchanging retirement throughput or speculative behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Form and register pc + immediate in ID together with the existing immediate\\nand instruction payload, then use that registered value in EX for branch\\ntargets and direct-JAL targets. Keep JALR's forwarded rs1 + immediate\\ncalculation, branch predicate, redirect timing, misalignment detection, and\\nRVFI pc_wdata semantics unchanged. This relocates a 32-bit adder from the\\nbranch decision/redirect path into the earlier ID-to-ID/EX path, where it is\\nindependent of forwarding and branch comparison, reducing the critical\\ncontrol-flow cone while preserving the pipeline's current IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative immediate target field to the ID/EX pipeline payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch pc plus decoded immediate atomically with each accepted ID/EX instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the registered PC-relative target for BRANCH and direct JAL resolution while retaining JALR, traps, redirects, and RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed positive and negative branch/JAL target, redirect, and misaligned-target tests that check retirement PCs and RVFI pc_wdata.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative immediate target field to the ID/EX pipeline payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch pc plus decoded immediate atomically with each accepted ID/EX instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the registered PC-relative target for BRANCH and direct JAL resolution while retaining JALR, traps, redirects, and RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed positive and negative branch/JAL target, redirect, and misaligned-target tests that check retirement PCs and RVFI pc_wdata.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 419.9, \"delta_pct\": -2.45, \"vs_baseline\": 48.47, \"fmax_mhz\": 188.61, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5825, \"ff\": 2248, \"seeds\": [188.61, 195.96, 182.85], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:53:12.574433Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 9}\n28:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Epoch-bound registered loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly executes hot backward conditional branches, but every\\nprevious direct fetch predictor either lengthened the PC feedback path or\\nlet a registered prediction become detached from the instruction it was\\nmeant to accelerate under stalls and redirects.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly executes hot backward conditional branches, but every\\nprevious direct fetch predictor either lengthened the PC feedback path or\\nlet a registered prediction become detached from the instruction it was\\nmeant to accelerate under stalls and redirects.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a one-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor whose lookup is\\nissued only for the sequential candidate PC+4 and whose response is\\nregistered at the same edge that advances the fetch PC to that candidate.\\nThe response carries its queried PC and a fetch epoch; it may select its\\nstored target only for that exact next accepted fetch, then is consumed.\\nRedirects increment the epoch and invalidate the response, while imem,\\ndmem, and divide holds retain or discard it according to whether its query\\nPC was actually accepted. EX carries the prediction transaction with every\\nfetched instruction and compares the architectural successor for every\\nvalid instruction, recovering to PC+4 for symbolic-imem non-branch alias\\nhits as well as normal direction/target mispredictions. This saves one\\nhot-loop recovery cycle without putting BTB lookup, target selection, or\\ninstruction decode in the PC-to-PC combinational path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/lookahead_loop_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a resettable one-entry last-taken branch record plus a registered PC+4 lookup response tagged with query PC and fetch epoch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add accepted-fetch prediction transaction fields, including queried PC, predicted successor, valid bit, and epoch, to the pipeline payloads.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture a registered lookahead response only on a sequential fetch acceptance, consume it only for its exact tagged PC and epoch, and prioritize older EX recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the predictor transaction atomically with the fetched instruction so ordinary holds and flushes cannot detach metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare each valid instruction's architectural successor against its carried prediction, recover every mismatch including non-branch alias hits, and emit advance-qualified branch training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define fetch-acceptance and redirect/hold precedence so predictor response creation, consumption, and invalidation match pipeline progress.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire predictor lookup, epoch management, accepted-fetch metadata, EX recovery, and branch training while preserving the nret=1 top-level RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed warm-up, repeated-loop, final-exit, redirect, imem/dmem-stall, divide-hold, and symbolic-PC-alias recovery tests with RVFI PC-order checks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/lookahead_loop_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a resettable one-entry last-taken branch record plus a registered PC+4 lookup response tagged with query PC and fetch epoch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add accepted-fetch prediction transaction fields, including queried PC, predicted successor, valid bit, and epoch, to the pipeline payloads.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture a registered lookahead response only on a sequential fetch acceptance, consume it only for its exact tagged PC and epoch, and prioritize older EX recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the predictor transaction atomically with the fetched instruction so ordinary holds and flushes cannot detach metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare each valid instruction's architectural successor against its carried prediction, recover every mismatch including non-branch alias hits, and emit advance-qualified branch training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define fetch-acceptance and redirect/hold precedence so predictor response creation, consumption, and invalidation match pipeline progress.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire predictor lookup, epoch management, accepted-fetch metadata, EX recovery, and branch training while preserving the nret=1 top-level RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed warm-up, repeated-loop, final-exit, redirect, imem/dmem-stall, divide-hold, and symbolic-PC-alias recovery tests with RVFI PC-order checks.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 343.92, \"delta_pct\": -20.1, \"vs_baseline\": 21.6, \"fmax_mhz\": 148.59, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4320468, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5975, \"ff\": 2379, \"seeds\": [156.74, 148.59, 142.33], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:57:47.515089Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260710-003-r9s2 (regression, -20.10%): An epoch-safe registered loop predictor can still lose badly when every EX instruction computes and 32-bit-compares an architectural successor against carried prediction metadata, because that recovery logic extends the hot EX redirect cone more than CoreMark amortizes the saved loop-back bubble.\"}\n29:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r10s0\", \"title\": \"Share ALU barrel shifter\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The ALU currently describes independent variable left, logical-right, and\\narithmetic-right shifts. These wide mux networks consume LUTs even though\\nan instruction selects only one shift result, and they sit in the common\\nsingle-cycle EX datapath used by CoreMark integer code.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The ALU currently describes independent variable left, logical-right, and\\narithmetic-right shifts. These wide mux networks consume LUTs even though\\nan instruction selects only one shift result, and they sit in the common\\nsingle-cycle EX datapath used by CoreMark integer code.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the three variable-shift expressions with one right-shift barrel\\ndatapath. For SLL, reverse the operand bits before the shared logical\\nright shift and reverse the result afterward; for SRL and SRA, feed the\\noperand directly and select zero or sign fill. Bit reversal is pure wiring,\\nso this removes duplicate wide shift-mux cones while preserving one-cycle\\nALU latency, forwarding, branch timing, and every RV32I shift result.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a shared right-shift barrel datapath with wire-only bit reversal for SLL and selectable sign extension for SRA, preserving all non-shift and ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add exhaustive shift-count boundary vectors and randomized SLL/SRL/SRA checks, including sign-bit and all-ones operands, against RV32I reference results.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a shared right-shift barrel datapath with wire-only bit reversal for SLL and selectable sign extension for SRA, preserving all non-shift and ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add exhaustive shift-count boundary vectors and randomized SLL/SRL/SRA checks, including sign-bit and all-ones operands, against RV32I reference results.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 412.88, \"delta_pct\": -4.08, \"vs_baseline\": 45.99, \"fmax_mhz\": 185.46, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5597, \"ff\": 2217, \"seeds\": [188.29, 173.88, 185.46], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T03:10:19.961425Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r10s0 (regression, -4.08%): Sharing RV32I shifts through a 33-bit arithmetic-right barrel with pre/post bit-reversal can hurt CoreMark because the direction/sign-control muxing and reversal routing extend the hot EX shift-result path more than the removed parallel shift cones save.\"}\n31:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Registered decode BTFNT predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly executes backward conditional loop branches, but prior\\nfetch-stage predictors lost Fmax by putting instruction-memory data or BTB\\nlookup in the PC feedback path. A predictor can still remove a recovery\\nbubble if it acts after a registered fetch payload, rather than directly\\nfrom the instruction-memory response.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly executes backward conditional loop branches, but prior\\nfetch-stage predictors lost Fmax by putting instruction-memory data or BTB\\nlookup in the PC feedback path. A predictor can still remove a recovery\\nbubble if it acts after a registered fetch payload, rather than directly\\nfrom the instruction-memory response.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a real registered IF/ID payload and apply static backward-taken,\\nforward-not-taken prediction in decode only for a decoded, valid conditional\\nbranch with a negative B immediate. Decode supplies the predicted target to\\nthe PC register for the next fetch, so instruction-memory data, branch\\ndecode, immediate extraction, and target addition are separated across the\\nIF/ID register instead of one PC-to-PC timing cone. Carry a small\\npredicted-branch/predicted-taken bit with the instruction; EX performs its\\nexisting architectural branch resolution and recovers only for that\\nprediction's direction/target mismatch. Thus non-branch instructions avoid\\nthe universal 32-bit successor comparison that made the epoch predictor\\nslow, while symbolic instruction memory is safe because prediction is\\nqualified from the registered instruction itself.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add registered fetch payload and branch-prediction metadata fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Turn the combinational fetch output into a stall-aware IF/ID register and accept a decode-stage predicted redirect with defined EX-recovery priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode valid conditional branches from the registered fetch payload, form negative B-immediate targets, and emit/latch BTFNT prediction metadata without consulting branch operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain architectural branch resolution and issue recovery only for a carried, qualified branch prediction whose resolved successor disagrees.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Arbitrate decode prediction, EX misprediction recovery, load-use, divide, and bus holds so prediction metadata and fetch acceptance stay aligned.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the registered fetch path, decode predictor, carried metadata, and qualified EX recovery while preserving the nret=1 RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed backward-loop warm-up, final not-taken exit, forward-taken recovery, imem/dmem stall, and symbolic instruction-change tests with RVFI PC-order assertions.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add registered fetch payload and branch-prediction metadata fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Turn the combinational fetch output into a stall-aware IF/ID register and accept a decode-stage predicted redirect with defined EX-recovery priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode valid conditional branches from the registered fetch payload, form negative B-immediate targets, and emit/latch BTFNT prediction metadata without consulting branch operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain architectural branch resolution and issue recovery only for a carried, qualified branch prediction whose resolved successor disagrees.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"descripti