 CoreMark frequently executes loop-control branches, so\\nshortening this registered EX-to-PC feedback path can raise Fmax without\\nchanging retirement throughput or speculative behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Form and register pc + immediate in ID together with the existing immediate\\nand instruction payload, then use that registered value in EX for branch\\ntargets and direct-JAL targets. Keep JALR's forwarded rs1 + immediate\\ncalculation, branch predicate, redirect timing, misalignment detection, and\\nRVFI pc_wdata semantics unchanged. This relocates a 32-bit adder from the\\nbranch decision/redirect path into the earlier ID-to-ID/EX path, where it is\\nindependent of forwarding and branch comparison, reducing the critical\\ncontrol-flow cone while preserving the pipeline's current IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative immediate target field to the ID/EX pipeline payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch pc plus decoded immediate atomically with each accepted ID/EX instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the registered PC-relative target for BRANCH and direct JAL resolution while retaining JALR, traps, redirects, and RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed positive and negative branch/JAL target, redirect, and misaligned-target tests that check retirement PCs and RVFI pc_wdata.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative immediate target field to the ID/EX pipeline payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch pc plus decoded immediate atomically with each accepted ID/EX instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the registered PC-relative target for BRANCH and direct JAL resolution while retaining JALR, traps, redirects, and RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed positive and negative branch/JAL target, redirect, and misaligned-target tests that check retirement PCs and RVFI pc_wdata.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 419.9, \"delta_pct\": -2.45, \"vs_baseline\": 48.47, \"fmax_mhz\": 188.61, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5825, \"ff\": 2248, \"seeds\": [188.61, 195.96, 182.85], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:53:12.574433Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 9}\n27-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"In-order memory completion queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The injected dmem backpressure currently freezes every pipeline stage as\\nsoon as a load or store reaches EX/MEM. Most stalls are short, but they\\nprevent independent younger ALU work from advancing and make memory\\nhandshaking part of the pipeline-wide enable network. The earlier store\\nbuffer failed because it allowed a store to retire before the externally\\nordered transaction completed, not because overlap itself is invalid.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The injected dmem backpressure currently freezes every pipeline stage as\\nsoon as a load or store reaches EX/MEM. Most stalls are short, but they\\nprevent independent younger ALU work from advancing and make memory\\nhandshaking part of the pipeline-wide enable network. The earlier store\\nbuffer failed because it allowed a store to retire before the externally\\nordered transaction completed, not because overlap itself is invalid.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the single coupled MEM/WB boundary with a two-entry in-order\\ncompletion queue. A memory operation occupies the head entry until its\\ndmem handshake completes; its RVFI record and architectural retirement\\noccur only after that completion. While the head is waiting, one younger\\nnon-memory EX result may enter the second entry, but cannot retire early.\\nLoads and stores behind an unresolved memory head remain interlocked, and\\nstore data/masks stay stable until acknowledgement. This isolates short\\ndmem waits from EX and decode, preserves strictly ordered RVFI retirement\\nand memory visibility, and avoids putting a dmem-return forwarding cone on\\nthe EX path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a compact completion-entry payload with execution, memory, and RVFI fields plus explicit ready/valid state for two in-order slots.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Convert the coupled MEM/WB register into the completion-queue producer: hold a memory head until its bus handshake, snapshot its RVFI memory payload, and admit only an ordering-safe younger result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume only the queue head for register-file writeback and expose a head-retire record so no younger completed instruction can write or retire first.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace blanket dmem pipeline freezing with queue-capacity and memory-order interlocks; preserve load-use, redirect, divide, and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the completion queue, head-only RVFI retirement, writeback, and backpressure controls while retaining the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add delayed-load and delayed-store sequences with independent younger ALU work, dependent accesses, and RVFI-order checks proving ordered retirement and stable requests.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\