on's branch identity or rely on immutable instruction memory, because formal's per-cycle symbolic imem can reuse a trained PC for a non-branch and make the predictor skip its required PC+4.\\\"}\\n21:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"MEM-to-EX load forwarding\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The present five-stage pipeline unconditionally injects a bubble for every\\\\nadjacent load consumer, even though the benchmark memory is zero-wait when\\\\nio_dmemReady is asserted. CoreMark's pointer, list, and matrix kernels use\\\\nmany load-dependent address and arithmetic chains, so this fixed IPC loss is\\\\na more direct target than another speculative front-end structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The present five-stage pipeline unconditionally injects a bubble for every\\\\nadjacent load consumer, even though the benchmark memory is zero-wait when\\\\nio_dmemReady is asserted. CoreMark's pointer, list, and matrix kernels use\\\\nmany load-dependent address and arithmetic chains, so this fixed IPC loss is\\\\na more direct target than another speculative front-end structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Restructure the load-result path so the combinationally extracted MEM-stage\\\\nload value can bypass directly to the simultaneously executing dependent\\\\ninstruction in EX. Remove the ordinary one-cycle load-use bubble, but only\\\\npermit that bypass when the older load is in EX/MEM and dmem is ready; on a\\\\ndmem stall, retain the existing pipeline hold until the response is valid.\\\\nThe normal MEM/WB forwarding remains as the fallback for older loads, and\\\\nRVFI continues to retire the original load and dependent instruction in\\\\nprogram order. This should improve CoreMark iterations per cycle without\\\\nadding predictor state or changing the external memory or RVFI contracts.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the already computed sign/zero-extended load result as a valid-qualified combinational bypass value alongside the registered MEM/WB payload.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM-load forwarding selection that chooses the MEM-stage load bypass instead of the EX/MEM address result.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Accept the MEM-stage load bypass operand and select it for either source before ALU, branch, store-data, and RVFI source-value capture.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove the default adjacent load-use bubble while preserving the dmem-ready-qualified full-pipeline hold that prevents a consumer from advancing before its load response exists.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the MEM-stage bypass data and load-valid qualification into execute forwarding and retain existing redirect, divider, and dmem-stall priorities.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_mem_stage.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed load-to-ALU, load-to-branch, load-to-store-data, byte/halfword extension, and delayed-dmem-response cases that verify no stale operand reaches EX or RVFI.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the already computed sign/zero-extended load result as a valid-qualified combinational bypass value alongside the registered MEM/WB payload.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM-load forwarding selection that chooses the MEM-stage load bypass instead of the EX/MEM address result.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Accept the MEM-stage load bypass operand and select it for either source before ALU, branch, store-data, and RVFI source-value capture.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove the default adjacent load-use bubble while preserving the dmem-ready-qualified full-pipeline hold that prevents a consumer from advancing before its load response exists.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the MEM-stage bypass data and load-valid qualification into execute forwarding and retain existing redirect, divider, and dmem-stall priorities.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_mem_stage.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed load-to-ALU, load-to-branch, load-to-store-data, byte/halfword extension, and delayed-dmem-response cases that verify no stale operand reaches EX or RVFI.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 364.7, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -11.37, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 28.95, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 156.37, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4287593, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 5875, \\\"ff\\\": 2200, \\\"seeds\\\": [156.37, 161.63, 153.16], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T02:32:59.674616Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 7, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r7s1 (regression, -11.37%): Zero-wait MEM-to-EX forwarding creates a dmem-return-to-load-format-to-operand-mux-to-ALU critical path, so CoreMark's saved load-use bubbles can be outweighed by Fmax loss unless the load response is timing-isolated.\\\"}\\n22:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Speculation-safe loop target predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"CoreMark repeatedly executes a few loop-closing conditional branches, where\\\\nthe EX-stage redirect discards two younger instructions on each taken edge.\\\\nPrior BTBs either harmed the PC feedback path or treated a PC hit as proof\\\\nthat the fetched word was still a branch, which is invalid under symbolic\\\\ninstruction memory and broke RVFI PC sequencing.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"CoreMark repeatedly executes a few loop-closing conditional branches, where\\\\nthe EX-stage redirect discards two younger instructions on each taken edge.\\\\nPrior BTBs either harmed the PC feedback path or treated a PC hit as proof\\\\nthat the fetched word was still a branch, which is invalid under symbolic\\\\ninstruction memory and broke RVFI PC sequencing.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a one-entry last-resolved conditional-branch predictor, but make its\\\\nprediction a transaction carried by every fetched instruction rather than a\\\\nbranch-only promise. The entry stores branch PC, target, and last direction;\\\\nits small registered-PC equality and target mux remain the only logic added\\\\nto fetch. IF/ID and ID/EX carry predicted_next_pc for all accepted fetches.\\\\nIn EX, compare that value against the architectural next PC for every valid\\\\ninstruction: non-control instructions resolve to PC+4, branches and jumps\\\\nresolve normally. Any mismatch redirects and flushes, including a predictor\\\\nhit whose symbolic imem word is no longer a branch. Train the entry only\\\\nwhen a valid resolved conditional branch advances from EX, and bind prediction\\\\nmetadata to its fetch PC across imem/dmem stalls and redirects. This retains\\\\nthe timing advantage of a one-entry PC-only predictor while making all stale\\\\nor aliased hits recoverable under RVFI.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/last_branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a one-entry PC/target/direction predictor with reset state and an EX-advance-qualified conditional-branch training interface.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add fetch-PC and predicted-next-PC fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so prediction remains paired with the instruction that accepted it.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use the one-entry predictor only to choose the fetch successor, and emit the exact predicted-next-PC transaction for every fetched instruction.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Latch prediction metadata atomically with decoded instruction state while preserving existing flush and hold semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compute architectural next PC for every valid instruction, redirect on any predicted-versus-actual mismatch, and expose precisely qualified conditional-branch training signals.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Integrate universal misprediction recovery with redirect, load-use, long-operation, and memory-stall priorities without advancing stale fetch metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire predictor lookup, EX training, transaction metadata, and recovery while retaining the nret=1 external and RVFI contracts.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_predictor.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed tests for loop warm-up and exit, a trained-PC non-branch instruction replacement, redirects, and imem/dmem stall transaction ownership.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/last_branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a one-entry PC/target/direction predictor with reset state and an EX-advance-qualified conditional-branch training interface.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add fetch-PC and predicted-next-PC fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so prediction remains paired with the instruction that accepted it.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use the one-entry predictor only to choose the fetch successor, and emit the exact predicted-next-PC transaction for every fetched instruction.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Latch prediction metadata atomically with decoded instruction state while preserving existing flush and hold semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compute architectural next PC for every valid instruction, redirect on any predicted-versus-actual mismatch, and expose precisely qualified conditional-branch training signals.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Integrate universal misprediction recovery with redirect, load-use, long-operation, and memory-stall priorities without advancing stale fetch metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire predictor lookup, EX training, transaction metadata, and recovery while retaining the nret=1 external and RVFI contracts.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_predictor.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed tests for loop warm-up and exit, a trained-PC non-branch instruction replacement, redirects, and imem/dmem stall transaction ownership.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 167.49, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -59.3, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": -40.78, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 73.5, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4388269, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 5875, \\\"ff\\\": 2286, \\\"seeds\\\": [73.5, 70.26, 73.93], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T02:34:44.881629Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 2, \\\"round_id\\\": 7}\\n23:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r8s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Exact source-aware load interlock\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The load-use interlock currently compares a preceding load destination against\\\\nboth raw IF/ID bit fields, even when the following instruction does not read\\\\none or either field. Those false matches insert avoidable bubbles after loads\\\\nwithout shortening any real data dependency or changing memory timing.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The load-use interlock currently compares a preceding load destination against\\\\nboth raw IF/ID bit fields, even when the following instruction does not read\\\\none or either field. Those false matches insert avoidable bubbles after loads\\\\nwithout shortening any real data dependency or changing memory timing.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Derive explicit uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 signals from the validated decode of\\\\nthe IF/ID instruction, and gate the existing load-use comparisons with those\\\\nsignals and IF/ID validity. Classify every architectural source exactly:\\\\nOP, STORE, and BRANCH use both; OP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR use rs1 only; all\\\\nremaining legal instructions and traps use neither. Keep the existing\\\\none-cycle stall for every true dependency, so the MEM/WB forwarding boundary\\\\nand the dmem-to-EX timing path remain unchanged while false interlocks no\\\\nlonger cost CoreMark issue cycles.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/decoder.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose validated decode-local uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 signals, defaulting both low for illegal or operand-free encodings.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Route the decoded source-use qualifiers alongside the IF/ID decode outputs without changing operand capture or pipeline payload timing.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire source-use qualifiers from decode into the load-use hazard decision.\\\"}, {\\\"