 high-half corrections, because the added subtractor network outweighs any saved multiplier logic on the CoreMark-critical ALU path.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (improvement, +32.31%): Moving DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a blocking iterative unit removes wide divide/remainder cones from the common EX path, and CoreMark's sparse division use lets the Fmax gain outweigh the rare multi-cycle front-end stalls.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (regression, +0.69%): Removing imem_data from branch prediction is insufficient when a combinational PC-indexed BTB tag match, counter read, and next-PC mux remain on the fetch feedback path; CoreMark's saved loop-back bubbles did not amortize that added front-end cost.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r3s0 (regression, -27.02%): Registering a blocking 33x33 multiplier without splitting its arithmetic only moves the full-cycle product into a new register-to-register cone while adding EX ownership and interlock logic, so it cannot deliver the divide unit's Fmax benefit without real pipelining or iteration.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): A sequential fetch FIFO must index its storage procedurally with runtime read/write pointers; generate-block hierarchy and prefixes are elaboration-time constructs and reject dynamic queue indices before synthesis.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r4s0 (broken, n/a): Decode-qualified load-use detection must classify every architectural source in the same valid/timing domain as operand capture, because suppressing a real dependency lets stale register data reach EX and is caught by RVFI register checks.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (regression, -18.56%): A four-entry procedural IF queue can lose CoreMark fitness when its pointer/count, dequeue arbitration, and redirect-flush control cost more than the transient imem stalls that prefetch can cover, so front-end decoupling needs measured slack rather than assumed stall hiding.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r5s2 (broken, n/a): A registered lookahead BTB must treat its response PC and predicted next PC as a fetch-acceptance transaction, invalidating or holding them consistently across redirects and stalls, or stale predictions can misassociate with conditional branches and violate RVFI control-flow checks.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r6s0 (improvement, +1.51%): Encoding BEQ/BNE and signed/unsigned relational branches from one 33-bit subtract's zero, sign, and borrow flags shares a carry-chain-friendly EX cone, modestly improving CoreMark loop-branch timing without changing redirect behavior.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): A write-behind store buffer must make buffer admission, external write acknowledgement, and RVFI retirement one ordered transaction boundary, since retiring a store while its request can outlive or be overwritten by younger MEM traffic violates architectural load/store ordering and register-state checks.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 (broken, n/a): A PC-only branch predictor must validate the fetched instruction's branch identity or rely on immutable instruction memory, because formal's per-cycle symbolic imem can reuse a trained PC for a non-branch and make the predictor skip its required PC+4.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r7s0 (improvement, +4.61%): On an FPGA MEM path, replacing variable 32-bit load shifts and shifted store masks with fixed addr-indexed byte/halfword lane muxes removes a barrel-mux cone after dmem and improves Fmax when alignment trapping already restricts halfword selection.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r7s1 (regression, -11.37%): Zero-wait MEM-to-EX forwarding creates a dmem-return-to-load-format-to-operand-mux-to-ALU critical path, so CoreMark's saved load-use bubbles can be outweighed by Fmax loss unless the load response is timing-isolated.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r8s2 (broken, n/a): A signature-mismatched conditional-branch prediction must redirect to the resolved PC+4 even when the branch is not taken, because treating it as a cold not-taken branch without recovery leaves the already-applied stale taken target on the fetch path and violates RVFI PC-forward progress.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r9s1 (broken, n/a): A decoupled in-order completion queue must make dequeue an atomic retirement event for RVFI payload/order, register-file writeback, and PC-forward state, because separate retire and commit views can misalign architectural instruction state across queue transitions.\\n- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260710-003-r9s2 (regression, -20.10%): An epoch-safe registered loop predictor can still lose badly when every EX instruction computes and 32-bit-compares an architectural successor against carried prediction metadata, because that recovery logic extends the hot EX redirect cone more than CoreMark amortizes the saved loop-back bubble.\\n{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n  \\\"required\\\": [\\\"id\\\",\\\"title\\\",\\\"category\\\",\\\"motivation\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"expected_impact\\\",\\\"changes\\\"],\\n  \\\"properties\\\": {\\n    \\\"id\\\":       {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\\\"},\\n    \\\"title\\\":    {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 5},\\n    \\\"category\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"enum\\\": [\\\"micro_opt\\\",\\\"structural\\\",\\\"extension\\\",\\\"predictor\\\",\\\"memory\\\"]},\\n    \\\"motivation\\\":  {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 20},\\n    \\\"hypothesis\\\":  {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"minLength\\\": 20},\\n    \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"required\\\": [\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\",\\\"confidence\\\"],\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\"},\\n        \\\"confidence\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"enum\\\": [\\\"low\\\",\\\"medium\\\",\\\"high\\\"]}\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"changes\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\", \\\"minItems\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"items\\\": {\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n        \\\"required\\\": [\\\"file\\\",\\\"description\\\"],\\n        \\\"properties\\\": {\\n          \\\"file\\\":        {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n            \\\"description\\\": \\\"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\\\",\\n            \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\\\\\.py)$\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"description\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The viable gap is a registered decode-stage BTFNT predictor: it removes `imemData` from the PC feedback path and only compares/recoveries for instructions actually predicted, avoiding the prior universal EX successor comparator.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'test ! -e cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.yaml && git status --short'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'test ! -e cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.yaml && git status --short'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"file_change\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.yaml\",\"kind\":\"add\"}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"file_change\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.yaml\",\"kind\":\"add\"}],\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git diff --check && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.yaml && git status --short\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git diff --check && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.yaml && git status --short\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"id: hyp-20260711-003-r10s2\\ntitle: \\\"Registered decode BTFNT predictor\\\"\\ncategory: predictor\\nmotivation: |\\n  CoreMark repeatedly executes backward conditional loop branches, but prior\\n  fetch-stage predictors lost Fmax by putting instruction-memory data or BTB\\n  lookup in the PC feedback path. A predictor can still remove a recovery\\n  bubble if it acts after a registered fetch payload, rather than directly\\n  from the instruction-memory response.\\nhypothesis: |\\n  Add a real registered IF/ID payload and apply static backward-taken,\\n  forward-not-taken prediction in decode only for a decoded, valid conditional\\n  branch with a negative B immediate. Decode supplies the predicted target to\\n  the PC register for the next fetch, so instruction-memory data, branch\\n  decode, immediate extraction, and target addition are separated across the\\n  IF/ID register instead of one PC-to-PC timing cone. Carry a small\\n  predicted-branch/predicted-taken bit with the instruction; EX performs its\\n  existing architectural branch resolution and recovers only for that\\n  prediction's direction/target mismatch. Thus non-branch instructions avoid\\n  the universal 32-bit successor comparison that made the epoch predictor\\n  slow, while symbolic instruction memory is safe because prediction is\\n  qualified from the registered instruction itself.\\nexpected_impact:\\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\\n  confidence: low\\nchanges:\\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\\n    description: \\\"Add registered fetch payload and branch-prediction metadata fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\\\"\\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\\n    description: \\\"Turn the combinational fetch output into a stall-aware IF/ID register and accept a decode-stage predicted redirect with defined EX-recovery priority.\\\"\\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\\n    description: \\\"Decode valid conditional branches from the registered fetch payload, form negative B-immediate targets, and emit/latch BTFNT prediction metadata without consulting branch operands.\\\"\\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\\n    description: \\\"Retain architectural branch resolution and issue recovery only for a carried, qualified branch prediction whose resolved successor disagrees.\\\"\\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\n    description: \\\"Arbitrate decode prediction, EX misprediction recovery, load-use, divide, and bus holds so prediction metadata and fetch acceptance stay aligned.\\\"\\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\\n    description: \\\"Wire the registered fetch path, decode predictor, carried metadata, and qualified EX recovery while preserving the nret=1 RVFI interface.\\\"\\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\\n    description: \\\"Add directed backward-loop warm-up, final not-taken exit, forward-taken recovery, imem/dmem stall, and symbolic instruction-change tests with RVFI PC-order assertions.\\\"\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"ruby -e 'require \\\\\\\"yaml\\\\\\\"; h = YAML.load_file(\\\\\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.yaml\\\\\\\"); abort \\\\\\\"bad fields\\\\\\\" unless h[\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\"] == \\\\\\\"predictor\\\\\\\" && h.dig(\\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\").is_a?(Integer) && %w[low medium high].include?(h.dig(\\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\")) && h[\\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\"].all? { |c| c[\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\"].match?(%r{\\\\\\\\A(?:rtl/[\\\"'^.].*|test/test_[''^/]+'\\\"\\\\\\\\.py)\\\\\\\\z}) }; puts \\\\\\\"YAML schema-critical fields valid\\\\\\\"' && git status --short --untracked-files=all\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"ruby -e 'require \\\\\\\"yaml\\\\\\\"; h = YAML.load_file(\\\\\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.yaml\\\\\\\"); abort \\\\\\\"bad fields\\\\\\\" unless h[\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\"] == \\\\\\\"predictor\\\\\\\" && h.dig(\\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\").is_a?(Integer) && %w[low medium high].include?(h.dig(\\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\")) && h[\\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\"].all? { |c| c[\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\"].match?(%r{\\\\\\\\A(?:rtl/[\\\"'^.].*|test/test_[''^/]+'\\\"\\\\\\\\.py)\\\\\\\\z}) }; puts \\\\\\\"YAML schema-critical fields valid\\\\\\\"' && git status --short --untracked-files=all\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"YAML schema-critical fields valid\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Wrote and schema-checked the predictor hypothesis: [hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.yaml](/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.yaml).\\n\\nIt proposes registered decode-stage BTFNT prediction to avoid the prior fetch/EX timing failures.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":416464,\"cached_input_tokens\":362752,\"output_tokens\":3794,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":2052}}\nReading additional input from stdin...\n{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"019f4f29-662e-76c1-80d7-d3ec19631a80\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’ll review the predictor experiment history and the fixture’s current front-end, then write one narrowly scoped predictor hypothesis that avoids the failure modes already observed.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'pwd && rg -n -i \\\"predict|btb|branch|bht|loop\\\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md | tail -n 180 && rg --files cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses | tail -n 20'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'pwd && rg -n -i \\\"predict|btb|branch|bht|loop\\\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md | tail -n 180 && rg --files cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses | tail -n 20'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:2:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, -10.84%): A combinational BTFNT predictor that derives the PC update from imem_data puts instruction fetch, branch decode, immediate extraction, and target addition on the IF-to-PC feedback path, so it must be pipelined or decoupled when its Fmax loss exceeds CoreMark's saved redirect bubbles.\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:5:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (regression, +0.69%): Removing imem_data from branch prediction is insufficient when a combinational PC-indexed BTB tag match, counter read, and next-PC mux remain on the fetch feedback path; CoreMark's saved loop-back bubbles did not amortize that added front-end cost.\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:10:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r5s2 (broken, n/a): A registered lookahead BTB must treat its response PC and predicted next PC as a fetch-acceptance transaction, invalidating or holding them consistently across redirects and stalls, or stale predictions can misassociate with conditional branches and violate RVFI control-flow checks.\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:11:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r6s0 (improvement, +1.51%): Encoding BEQ/BNE and signed/unsigned relational branches from one 33-bit subtract's zero, sign, and borrow flags shares a carry-chain-friendly EX cone, modestly improving CoreMark loop-branch timing without changing redirect behavior.\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:13:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 (broken, n/a): A PC-only branch predictor must validate the fetched instruction's branch identity or rely on immutable instruction memory, because formal's per-cycle symbolic imem can reuse a trained PC for a non-branch and make the predictor skip its required PC+4.\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:16:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r8s2 (broken, n/a): A signature-mismatched conditional-branch prediction must redirect to the resolved PC+4 even when the branch is not taken, because treating it as a cold not-taken branch without recovery leaves the already-applied stale taken target on the fetch path and violates RVFI PC-forward progress.\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:18:- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260710-003-r9s2 (regression, -20.10%): An epoch-safe registered loop predictor can still lose badly when every EX instruction computes and 32-bit-compares an architectural successor against carried prediction metadata, because that recovery logic extends the hot EX redirect cone more than CoreMark amortizes the saved loop-back bubble.\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:21:- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r10s2 (broken, n/a): A decode-stage branch prediction redirect must atomically invalidate or suppress the already-issued sequential fetch payload, because otherwise a fall-through instruction can survive alongside the predicted target and widespread conditional-branch RVFI PC checks fail.\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Share RV32 multiply datapath\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\\\\nevaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\\\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\\\\nevaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\\\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace the unconditional signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and\\\\nsigned-unsigned product expressions with one shared 33x33 unsigned modular\\\\nmultiplier. Select the operands' sign extension from the decoded multiply\\\\noperation, then select bits [31:0] for MUL or [63:32] for MULH, MULHU, and\\\\nMULHSU. The low 64 bits of the 33-bit two's-complement product preserve all\\\\nRV32M result definitions, while removing two large parallel multiplier\\\\ncones. Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expressions unchanged.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"improvement\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 306.38, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 8.33, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 8.33, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 137.61, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 9816, \\\"ff\\\": 1867, \\\"seeds\\\": [136.3, 149.12, 137.61], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T00:55:35.641639Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 1, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +8.33%): RV32M multiply variants should share a sign-selected 33x33 product and select the required 32-bit half, since parallel signed/unsigned multiplier cones waste LUTs even though each instruction consumes only one result.\\\"}\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Decode-stage branch resolution\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Restructure the front end so conditional branches resolve in decode using\\\\nthe register-file read values and explicit bypasses from EX/MEM and WB.\\\\nRedirect the PC and squash only the fetched wrong-path instruction in the\\\\nsame decode cycle; retain EX resolution for JALR and preserve a targeted\\\\nload-to-branch interlock until load data is available. This removes one\\\\nrecovery cycle for the common backward conditional branch while retaining\\\\nsingle-retire RVFI ordering and the existing memory interface.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 7, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provide decode-stage bypass selects so branches compare the architecturally newest operands.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 7, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provide decode-stage bypass selects so branches compare the architecturally newest operands.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"broken\\\", \\\"formal_passed\\\": false, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": false, \\\"error\\\": \\\"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\\\ng trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Status: failed\\\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:18 (18)\\\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:12 (12)\\\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_42_56 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:42.6-42.59 step 20\\\\nSBY 21:54:54 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\\\n\\\\nFormal: 51 passed, 2 failed\\\\nFai