/experiments/log.jsonl:24:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Decode-accepted direct JAL redirect\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Every direct JAL has a PC-relative target encoded in its own instruction, but\\\\nthe current pipeline waits until EX to redirect it and discards younger\\\\nfall-through work. CoreMark uses calls and helper loops often enough that\\\\nthis fixed, non-speculative control penalty is worth removing.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Every direct JAL has a PC-relative target encoded in its own instruction, but\\\\nthe current pipeline waits until EX to redirect it and discards younger\\\\nfall-through work. CoreMark uses calls and helper loops often enough that\\\\nthis fixed, non-speculative control penalty is worth removing.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Resolve only direct JAL in decode when that instruction is accepted into\\\\nID/EX. Form its immediate target from the fetched instruction and update the\\\\nfetch PC at the same edge, while carrying an already-redirected bit so EX\\\\npreserves the JAL RVFI pc_wdata and return-address result without issuing a\\\\nsecond redirect. Leave conditional branches and JALR in EX, avoiding the\\\\ncostly decode-stage comparator and operand-forwarding network that made the\\\\nearlier full branch-resolution attempt fragile. Gate the early redirect on\\\\nID acceptance and give an older EX redirect priority across all stalls.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add ID/EX metadata marking a direct JAL whose fetch redirect was accepted in decode.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Recognize valid direct JAL instructions, form the PC-relative target, and emit an acceptance-qualified early-redirect request while latching its metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Separate PC-update redirect selection from EX wrong-path output squashing so an accepted decode-stage JAL is retained while the PC advances to its target.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Suppress only the duplicate EX redirect for a JAL already redirected in decode; retain JAL result, RVFI pc_wdata, JALR, and branch behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose or qualify the ID acceptance condition so early JAL redirection cannot occur while ID/EX is held or an older EX redirect squashes it.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Arbitrate older EX recovery ahead of an accepted decode-stage JAL redirect and wire the split fetch-control paths without changing the nret=1 interface.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_core.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed JAL call/return, consecutive JAL, load-use hold, dmem-stall, and simultaneous older-redirect cases that check RVFI PC order and return-address writes.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add ID/EX metadata marking a direct JAL whose fetch redirect was accepted in decode.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Recognize valid direct JAL instructions, form the PC-relative target, and emit an acceptance-qualified early-redirect request while latching its metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Separate PC-update redirect selection from EX wrong-path output squashing so an accepted decode-stage JAL is retained while the PC advances to its target.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Suppress only the duplicate EX redirect for a JAL already redirected in decode; retain JAL result, RVFI pc_wdata, JALR, and branch behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose or qualify the ID acceptance condition so early JAL redirection cannot occur while ID/EX is held or an older EX redirect squashes it.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Arbitrate older EX recovery ahead of an accepted decode-stage JAL redirect and wire the split fetch-control paths without changing the nret=1 interface.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_core.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed JAL call/return, consecutive JAL, load-use hold, dmem-stall, and simultaneous older-redirect cases that check RVFI PC order and return-address writes.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 161.77, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -62.42, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": -42.8, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 71.86, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4442158, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 5736, \\\"ff\\\": 2199, \\\"seeds\\\": [70.77, 71.86, 73.86], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T02:44:32.240279Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 8}\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:25:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r8s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Signature-qualified loop predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"CoreMark repeatedly revisits a small number of loop-closing branches, but\\\\nprevious BTB attempts either put a large table on the fetch feedback path or\\\\npaid for a wide universal predicted-next-PC comparison in execute. A tiny\\\\npredictor can retain the temporal-locality benefit if alias recovery is\\\\nexplicit and restricted to the control cases that need it.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"CoreMark repeatedly revisits a small number of loop-closing branches, but\\\\nprevious BTB attempts either put a large table on the fetch feedback path or\\\\npaid for a wide universal predicted-next-PC comparison in execute. A tiny\\\\npredictor can retain the temporal-locality benefit if alias recovery is\\\\nexplicit and restricted to the control cases that need it.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a one-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor that stores branch\\\\nPC, target, direction, and the resolved instruction word as a signature.\\\\nIF uses only registered PC equality, direction, and target muxing to select\\\\nthe speculative successor; the instruction signature is carried as\\\\nsideband validation metadata and is not placed in the PC-select cone. EX\\\\nretains architectural branch resolution and redirects only for a predicted\\\\ncontrol instruction whose resolved successor differs, or for a predicted\\\\nhit that resolves as a non-branch (including a symbolic-imem signature\\\\nmismatch), explicitly restoring PC+4. This avoids assuming PC identity\\\\nproves instruction identity, while replacing the prior universal 32-bit\\\\nnext-PC compare with narrow prediction-valid/control-qualified recovery.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/last_branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a resettable one-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor holding PC, target, direction, and resolved instruction signature, with EX-advance-qualified training.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add fetch prediction-valid, predicted target, and signature-match metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so the prediction remains bound to its fetched instruction.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use only the small registered-PC predictor lookup for the speculative successor and carry its transaction metadata for every accepted fetch without decoding imem data in the PC-select path.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Latch predictor transaction metadata atomically with decoded instruction state across ordinary holds and flushes.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Resolve branches architecturally, recover only control-qualified prediction mismatches, and force PC+4 recovery for a predicted hit that is not the trained conditional branch.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Integrate predictor recovery with redirect, load-use, divide, and memory-stall priorities while ensuring wrong-path payloads cannot advance.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instantiate and wire the predictor, metadata path, qualified recovery, and EX training without changing the nret=1 I/O or RVFI contract.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_predictor.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed warm-up, repeated-loop, final-exit, trained-PC non-branch replacement, signature-mismatch, and imem/dmem-stall RVFI PC-sequencing tests.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/last_branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a resettable one-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor holding PC, target, direction, and resolved instruction signature, with EX-advance-qualified training.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add fetch prediction-valid, predicted target, and signature-match metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so the prediction remains bound to its fetched instruction.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use only the small registered-PC predictor lookup for the speculative successor and carry its transaction metadata for every accepted fetch without decoding imem data in the PC-select path.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Latch predictor transaction metadata atomically with decoded instruction state across ordinary holds and flushes.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Resolve branches architecturally, recover only control-qualified prediction mismatches, and force PC+4 recovery for a predicted hit that is not the trained conditional branch.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Integrate predictor recovery with redirect, load-use, divide, and memory-stall priorities while ensuring wrong-path payloads cannot advance.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instantiate and wire the predictor, metadata path, qualified recovery, and EX training without changing the nret=1 I/O or RVFI contract.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_predictor.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed warm-up, repeated-loop, final-exit, trained-PC non-branch replacement, signature-mismatch, and imem/dmem-stall RVFI PC-sequencing tests.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"broken\\\", \\\"formal_passed\\\": false, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": false, \\\"error\\\": \\\"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\\\nd_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\\\nSBY 23:43:01 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: pc_fwd_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\\\nSBY 23:43:01 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_pc_fwd_check_sv_41_55 at rvfi_pc_fwd_check.sv:41.6-41.69 step 20\\\\nSBY 23:43:01 [pc_fwd_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\\\nSBY 23:43:40 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:01  waiting for solver (1 minute)\\\\nSBY 23:44:21 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:42  Status: passed\\\\nSBY 23:44:21 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\\\nSBY 23:44:21 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\\\nSBY 23:44:21 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:01:42 (102)\\\\nSBY 23:44:21 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:01:33 (93)\\\\nSBY 23:44