eMark uses calls and helper loops often enough that\\\\\\\\nthis fixed, non-speculative control penalty is worth removing.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Every direct JAL has a PC-relative target encoded in its own instruction, but\\\\\\\\nthe current pipeline waits until EX to redirect it and discards younger\\\\\\\\nfall-through work. CoreMark uses calls and helper loops often enough that\\\\\\\\nthis fixed, non-speculative control penalty is worth removing.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Resolve only direct JAL in decode when that instruction is accepted into\\\\\\\\nID/EX. Form its immediate target from the fetched instruction and update the\\\\\\\\nfetch PC at the same edge, while carrying an already-redirected bit so EX\\\\\\\\npreserves the JAL RVFI pc_wdata and return-address result without issuing a\\\\\\\\nsecond redirect. Leave conditional branches and JALR in EX, avoiding the\\\\\\\\ncostly decode-stage comparator and operand-forwarding network that made the\\\\\\\\nearlier full branch-resolution attempt fragile. Gate the early redirect on\\\\\\\\nID acceptance and give an older EX redirect priority across all stalls.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 4, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add ID/EX metadata marking a direct JAL whose fetch redirect was accepted in decode.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recognize valid direct JAL instructions, form the PC-relative target, and emit an acceptance-qualified early-redirect request while latching its metadata.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Separate PC-update redirect selection from EX wrong-path output squashing so an accepted decode-stage JAL is retained while the PC advances to its target.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Suppress only the duplicate EX redirect for a JAL already redirected in decode; retain JAL result, RVFI pc_wdata, JALR, and branch behavior.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Expose or qualify the ID acceptance condition so early JAL redirection cannot occur while ID/EX is held or an older EX redirect squashes it.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Arbitrate older EX recovery ahead of an accepted decode-stage JAL redirect and wire the split fetch-control paths without changing the nret=1 interface.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/test_core.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add directed JAL call/return, consecutive JAL, load-use hold, dmem-stall, and simultaneous older-redirect cases that check RVFI PC order and return-address writes.\\\\\\\"}]}, \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 4, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add ID/EX metadata marking a direct JAL whose fetch redirect was accepted in decode.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recognize valid direct JAL instructions, form the PC-relative target, and emit an acceptance-qualified early-redirect request while latching its metadata.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Separate PC-update redirect selection from EX wrong-path output squashing so an accepted decode-stage JAL is retained while the PC advances to its target.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/