a large table on the fetch feedback path or\\\\\\\\npaid for a wide universal predicted-next-PC comparison in execute. A tiny\\\\\\\\npredictor can retain the temporal-locality benefit if alias recovery is\\\\\\\\nexplicit and restricted to the control cases that need it.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CoreMark repeatedly revisits a small number of loop-closing branches, but\\\\\\\\nprevious BTB attempts either put a large table on the fetch feedback path or\\\\\\\\npaid for a wide universal predicted-next-PC comparison in execute. A tiny\\\\\\\\npredictor can retain the temporal-locality benefit if alias recovery is\\\\\\\\nexplicit and restricted to the control cases that need it.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add a one-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor that stores branch\\\\\\\\nPC, target, direction, and the resolved instruction word as a signature.\\\\\\\\nIF uses only registered PC equality, direction, and target muxing to select\\\\\\\\nthe speculative successor; the instruction signature is carried as\\\\\\\\nsideband validation metadata and is not placed in the PC-select cone. EX\\\\\\\\nretains architectural branch resolution and redirects only for a predicted\\\\\\\\ncontrol instruction whose resolved successor differs, or for a predicted\\\\\\\\nhit that resolves as a non-branch (including a symbolic-imem signature\\\\\\\\nmismatch), explicitly restoring PC+4. This avoids assuming PC identity\\\\\\\\nproves instruction identity, while replacing the prior universal 32-bit\\\\\\\\nnext-PC compare with narrow prediction-valid/control-qualified recovery.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 3, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"low\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/last_branch_predictor.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Implement a resettable one-entry last-taken conditional-branch predictor holding PC, target, direction, and resolved instruction signature, with EX-advance-qualified training.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add fetch prediction-valid, predicted target, and signature-match metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so the prediction remains bound to its fetched instruction.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Use only the small registered-PC predictor lookup for the speculative successor and carry its transaction metadata for every accepted fetch without decoding imem data in the PC-select path.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Latch predictor transaction metadata atomically with decoded instruction state across ordinary holds and flushes.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Resolve branches architecturally, recover only control-qualified prediction mismatches, and force PC+4 recovery for a predicted hit that is not the trained conditional branch.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Integrate predictor recovery with redirect, load-use, divide, and memory-stall priorities while ensuring wrong-path payloads cannot advance.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Instantiate and wire the predictor, metadata path, qualified recovery, and EX training without changing the nret=1 I/O or RVFI contract.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/test_predictor.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add directed warm-up, repeated-loop, final-exit, trained-PC non-branch replacement, signature-mismatch, and imem/dmem-stall RVFI PC-sequencing tests.\\\\\\\"}]}, \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\