s/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.yaml).\\\\n\\\\nIt proposes registered decode-stage BTFNT prediction to avoid the prior fetch/EX timing failures.\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"turn.completed\\\",\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":416464,\\\"cached_input_tokens\\\":362752,\\\"output_tokens\\\":3794,\\\"reasoning_output_tokens\\\":2052}}\\nReading additional input from stdin...\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"thread.started\\\",\\\"thread_id\\\":\\\"019f4f29-662e-76c1-80d7-d3ec19631a80\\\"}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"turn.started\\\"}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_0\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I’ll review the predictor experiment history and the fixture’s current front-end, then write one narrowly scoped predictor hypothesis that avoids the failure modes already observed.\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'pwd && rg -n -i \\\\\\\"predict|btb|branch|bht|loop\\\\\\\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md | tail -n 180 && rg --files cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses | tail -n 20'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'pwd && rg -n -i \\\\\\\"predict|btb|branch|bht|loop\\\\\\\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md | tail -n 180 && rg --files cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses | tail -n 20'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1\\\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:2:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, -10.84%): A combinational BTFNT predictor that derives the PC update from imem_data puts instruction fetch, branch decode, immediate extraction, and target addition on the IF-to-PC feedback path, so it must be pipelined or decoupled when its Fmax loss exceeds CoreMark's saved redirect bubbles.\\\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:5:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (regression, +0.69%): Removing imem_data from branch prediction is insufficient when a combinational PC-indexed BTB tag match, counter read, and next-PC mux remain on the fetch feedback path; CoreMark's saved loop-back bubbles did not amortize that added front-end cost.\\\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:10:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r5s2 (broken, n/a): A registered lookahead BTB must treat its response PC and predicted next PC as a fetch-acceptance transaction, invalidating or holding them consistently across redirects and stalls, or stale predictions can misassociate with conditional branches and violate RVFI control-flow checks.\\\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:11:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r6s0 (improvement, +1.51%): Encoding BEQ/BNE and signed/unsigned relational branches from one 33-bit subtract's zero, sign, and borrow flags shares a carry-chain-friendly EX cone, modestly improving CoreMark loop-branch timing without changing redirect behavior.\\\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:13:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 (broken, n/a): A PC-only branch predictor must validate the fetched instruction's branch identity or rely on immutable instruction memory, because formal's per-cycle symbolic imem can reuse a trained PC for a non-branch and make the predictor skip its required PC+4.\\\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:16:- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r8s2 (broken, n/a): A signature-mismatched conditional-branch prediction must redirect to the resolved PC+4 even when the branch is not taken, because treating it as a cold not-taken branch without recovery leaves the already-applied stale taken target on the fetch path and violates RVFI PC-forward progress.\\\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:18:- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260710-003-r9s2 (regression, -20.10%): An epoch-safe registered loop predictor can still lose badly when every EX instruction computes and 32-bit-compares an architectural successor against carried prediction metadata, because that recovery logic extends the hot EX redirect cone more than CoreMark amortizes the saved loop-back bubble.\\\\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:21:- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r10s2 (broken, n/a): A decode-stage branch prediction redirect must atomically invalidate or suppress the already-issued sequential fetch payload, because otherwise a fall-through instruction can survive alongside the predicted target and widespread conditional-branch RVFI PC checks fail.\\\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Share RV32 multiply datapath\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\\\\\\\\nevaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\\\\\\\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\\\\\\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The current ALU computes three distinct 64-bit products on every ALU\\\\\\\\nevaluation, although an instruction can consume only one result. This is a\\\\\\\\nhigh-LUT combinational cone in a design already near its LUT target and\\\\\\\\nbelow its 135 MHz Fmax target.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Replace the unconditional signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and\\\\\\\\nsigned-unsigned product expressions with one shared 33x33 unsigned modular\\\\\\\\nmultiplier. Select the operands' sign extension from the decoded multiply\\\\\\\\noperation, then select bits [31:0] for MUL or [63:32] for MULH, MULHU, and\\\\\\\\nMULHSU. The low 64 bits of the 33-bit two's-complement product preserve all\\\\\\\\nRV32M result definitions, while removing two large parallel multiplier\\\\\\\\ncones. Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expressions unchanged.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 5, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/test_alu.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\\\\\\\"}]}, \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 5, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Implement one opcode-selected 33x33 multiplier and route all four RV32M multiply variants through it, preserving the ALTOPS branch and division semantics.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/test_alu.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Extend multiply tests with signed/unsigned boundary and randomized vectors that prove the shared product's high and low halves match RV32M semantics.\\\\\\\"}], \\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"improvement\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"fitness\\\\\\\": 306.38, \\\\\\\"delta_pct\\\\\\\": 8.33, \\\\\\\"vs_baseline\\\\\\\": 8.33, \\\\\\\"fmax_mhz\\\\\\\": 137.61, \\\\\\\"ipc_coremark\\\\\\\": 2e-06, \\\\\\\"cycles\\\\\\\": 4491485, \\\\\\\"iterations\\\\\\\": 10, \\\\\\\"lut4\\\\\\\": 9816, \\\\\\\"ff\\\\\\\": 1867, \\\\\\\"seeds\\\\\\\": [136.3, 149.12, 137.61], \\\\\\\"formal_passed\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\"cosim_passed\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\": null, \\\\\\\"implementation_notes\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-07-11T00:55:35.641639Z\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"slot\\\\\\\": 0, \\\\\\\"round_id\\\\\\\": 1, \\\\\\\"lesson\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +8.33%): RV32M multiply variants should share a sign-selected 33x33 product and select the required 32-bit half, since parallel signed/unsigned multiplier cones waste LUTs even though each instruction consumes only one result.\\\\\\\"}\\\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Decode-stage branch resolution\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structural\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\\\\\\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\\\\\\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\\\\\\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The five-stage pipe resolves every conditional branch in EX, so a taken\\\\\\\\nloop branch discards two fetched/decode-path cycles. CoreMark spends much\\\\\\\\nof its time in short counted loops, making this fixed control penalty a\\\\\\\\nmeaningful limit on iterations per cycle under the same bus-stall model.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Restructure the front end so conditional branches resolve in decode using\\\\\\\\nthe register-file read values and explicit bypasses from EX/MEM and WB.\\\\\\\\nRedirect the PC and squash only the fetched wrong-path instruction in the\\\\\\\\nsame decode cycle; retain EX resolution for JALR and preserve a targeted\\\\\\\\nload-to-branch interlock until load data is available. This removes one\\\\\\\\nrecovery cycle for the common backward conditional branch while retaining\\\\\\\\nsingle-retire RVFI ordering and the existing memory interface.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 7, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add load-to-branch and EX-producer branch interlocks plus the reduced wrong-path flush policy.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Provide decode-stage bypass selects so branches compare the architecturally newest operands.\\\\\\\"}]}, \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 7, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Rewire redirect and hazard control so decoded conditional branches redirect before entering EX.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add decode-stage branch comparator, target adder, operand bypass selection, and branch redirect outputs.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Keep jump resolution in EX while removing duplicate conditional-branch redirect ownership.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\