\\\"Wire the atomic fetch transaction, prediction metadata, and EX recovery while preserving the existing single-retire RVFI interface.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\"=>\\\\\\\"test/test_predictor.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\"=>\\\\\\\"Add directed loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem/dmem-stall, and divide-hold tests that verify no sequential payload retires after a predicted redirect.\\\\\\\"}]}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Wrote and YAML-validated the predictor hypothesis:\\\\n\\\\n[hyp-20260711-003-r11s2.yaml](/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r11s2.yaml)\\\\n\\\\nIt proposes an atomic registered decode-stage BTFNT front end, explicitly invalidating the sequential fetch payload on predicted redirects.\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"turn.completed\\\",\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":270547,\\\"cached_input_tokens\\\":181504,\\\"output_tokens\\\":3272,\\\"reasoning_output_tokens\\\":1793}}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n\n--- target file state ---\nls: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r12s2.yaml: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
