, and issue the recorded backward target next;\n  thus the target reaches decode as the branch reaches EX without a decode or\n  target-adder cone on the PC feedback path. Carry prediction metadata only\n  with predicted branches and make EX redirect only for that branch's\n  direction/target mismatch. Give EX recovery priority over predictor\n  refill, and gate every fill/consume transition with imem readiness and the\n  existing downstream hold conditions, preserving a one-to-one PC,\n  instruction, and prediction transaction under stalls.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add fetch-payload validity, PC, and branch-only predicted-successor fields to keep each prediction bound to its decoded instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement the single-ahead registered payload, sequential lookahead fetch, atomic predicted-branch discard, and priority-ordered EX recovery.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize valid backward conditional branches from the registered payload and emit a prediction only on an actual ID/EX acceptance.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Carry branch-only prediction metadata and compare resolved direction and target only for a predicted branch before requesting recovery.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Define acceptance, hold, and flush precedence for imem/dmem stalls, load-use stalls, divider ownership, predicted discard, and EX recovery.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire fetch acceptance, branch prediction metadata, and qualified recovery without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add directed taken-loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem-stall, dmem-stall, and divider-hold tests for atomic sequential-payload discard and RVFI PC order.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
