closing branches still discard two younger instructions because\\nresolution occurs in EX. Earlier predictors recovered some cycles but lost\\nFmax when lookup logic entered the PC feedback loop; the registered\\nlookahead version instead failed because its prediction state was not\\nrigorously aligned across redirects and stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Taken loop-closing branches still discard two younger instructions because\\nresolution occurs in EX. Earlier predictors recovered some cycles but lost\\nFmax when lookup logic entered the PC feedback loop; the registered\\nlookahead version instead failed because its prediction state was not\\nrigorously aligned across redirects and stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement a small direct-mapped conditional-branch BTB whose lookup is made\\nfor sequential PC+4 and registered before it can influence fetch. A response\\nmay redirect only when its recorded query PC exactly equals the current fetch\\nPC; otherwise fetch deterministically falls through and invalidates the\\nstale response. EX trains only resolved valid branches and carries the exact\\npredicted next PC for mismatch recovery. Redirects, instruction stalls, and\\ndownstream holds invalidate or preserve the response according to whether\\nthe matching fetched instruction was actually accepted. This removes hot\\nloop recovery bubbles while keeping tag comparison, counter read, and target\\nselection out of the PC-to-PC feedback path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact direct-mapped BTB with registered PC+4 lookup responses, query-PC tags, valid bits, and resolved-branch-only target/direction training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend fetch and pipeline payloads with predicted-next-PC, prediction-valid, and fetch-PC metadata needed to prove response alignment.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a registered prediction only on an exact current-PC match, issue the next sequential lookahead query, and invalidate stale responses on redirect or non-sequential flow.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch prediction metadata only with an accepted IF instruction so ID/EX cannot pair a branch with a different lookup response.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved architectural next PC with the carried prediction, redirect only on mismatch, and expose precisely qualified conditional-branch BTB training events.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define predictor-response hold and invalidation priority for load-use, bus, divider, and EX redirect events without changing their existing retirement behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire predictor lookup, response-valid alignment, EX training, and misprediction recovery while retaining the nret=1 external contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add checks for sequential lookahead hits, taken-loop and final-exit recovery, redirect-stale-response suppression, imem stalls, and RVFI PC-order correctness.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact direct-mapped BTB with registered PC+4 lookup responses, query-PC tags, valid bits, and resolved-branch-only target/direction training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend fetch and pipeline payloads with predicted-next-PC, prediction-valid, and fetch-PC metadata needed to prove response alignment.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume a registered prediction only on an exact current-PC match, issue the next sequential lookahead query, and invalidate stale responses on redirect or non-sequential flow.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch prediction metadata only with an accepted IF instruction so ID/EX cannot pair a branch with a different lookup response.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved architectural next PC with the carried prediction, redirect only on mismatch, and expose precisely qualified conditional-branch BTB training events.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define predictor-response hold and invalidation priority for load-use, bus, divider, and EX redirect events without changing their existing retirement behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire predictor lookup, response-valid alignment, EX training, and misprediction recovery while retaining the nret=1 external contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add checks for sequential lookahead hits, taken-loop and final-exit recovery, redirect-stale-response suppression, imem stalls, and RVFI PC-order correctness.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: insn_beq_ch0\\ngeu_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:09:01  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\nSBY 23:07:25 [insn_bgeu_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:09:01  Status: failed\\nSBY 23:07:25 [insn_bgeu_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 23:07:25 [insn_bgeu_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 23:07:25 [insn_bgeu_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:09:02 (542)\\nSBY 23:07:25 [insn_bgeu_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:08:26 (506)\\nSBY 23:07:25 [insn_bgeu_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 23:07:25 [insn_bgeu_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: insn_bgeu_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 23:07:25 [insn_bgeu_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_insn_check_sv_198_153 at rvfi_insn_check.sv:198.6-198.31 step 20\\nSBY 23:07:25 [insn_bge