covers on a direction or target mismatch, while unpredicted\\ninstructions retain normal PC+4 behavior without a universal successor\\ncomparator. This removes hot loop-back recovery work while keeping\\ninstruction decode and target formation behind the fetch register.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add IF/ID registered-payload and branch-only prediction metadata fields, including the predicted successor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-entry stall-aware IF/ID register whose fill, dequeue, predicted redirect, EX recovery, and invalidation follow one atomic acceptance protocol.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect valid backward conditional branches from the registered payload, form their target, and emit prediction only when the payload advances into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry qualified branch prediction metadata and recover only a resolved predicted branch whose direction or target disagrees.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define ready/hold and redirect precedence so load-use, bus stalls, divider ownership, prediction, and EX recovery cannot consume or retain a wrong-path fetch entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the atomic fetch transaction, prediction metadata, and EX recovery while preserving the existing single-retire RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem/dmem-stall, and divide-hold tests that verify no sequential payload retires after a predicted redirect.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add IF/ID registered-payload and branch-only prediction metadata fields, including the predicted successor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-entry stall-aware IF/ID register whose fill, dequeue, predicted redirect, EX recovery, and invalidation follow one atomic acceptance protocol.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect valid backward conditional branches from the registered payload, form their target, and emit prediction only when the payload advances into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry qualified branch prediction metadata and recover only a resolved predicted branch whose direction or target disagrees.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define ready/hold and redirect precedence so load-use, bus stalls, divider ownership, prediction, and EX recovery cannot consume or retain a wrong-path fetch entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the atomic fetch transaction, prediction metadata, and EX recovery while preserving the existing single-retire RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem/dmem-stall, and divide-hold tests that verify no sequential payload retires after a predicted redirect.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:36:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r12s1\", \"title\": \"Decode-resolved direct JAL path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Direct JAL has a fully encoded PC-relative target and no register operands,\\nyet the current pipeline waits until EX to redirect it. Calls, returns from\\ncompiler veneers, and unconditional loop transfers therefore pay the same\\ntwo-younger-instruction recovery cost as a data-dependent control transfer.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Direct JAL has a fully encoded PC-relative target and no register operands,\\nyet the current pipeline waits until EX to redirect it. Calls, returns from\\ncompiler veneers, and unconditional loop transfers therefore pay the same\\ntwo-younger-instruction recovery cost as a data-dependent control transfer.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a decode-stage redirect path for validated JAL only. Form pc+J-immediate\\nfrom the current IF/ID payload and update the fetch PC when that payload\\nadvances into ID/EX, while preserving the JAL payload for normal EX/MEM/WB\\nretirement and PC+4 writeback. Give an older EX redirect priority, keep\\nconditional branches and JALR entirely EX-resolved, and distinguish the\\ndecode redirect from an EX flush so the issuing JAL is never suppressed.\\nThis removes one control-recovery cycle for direct jumps without a branch\\ncomparator, register bypass network, prediction table, or imem-to-PC path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Arbitrate decode-stage JAL and older EX redirects, and preserve the single-retire RVFI boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode validated JAL, form its PC-relative target, and emit a ready-qualified direct-redirect request.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept a distinct decode redirect without bubbling the currently issued JAL; continue to flush only EX-resolved wrong-path fetches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress duplicate EX redirect generation for JAL while retaining its PC+4 result and RVFI pc_next payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define load, bus, long-operation, decode-redirect, and older EX-redirect precedence so a JAL advances exactly once.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed JAL, consecutive JAL, JAL-after-stall, and older-EX-redirect collision tests checking PC order, link values, and RVFI retirement.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\