ce-free. Illegal or unrecognized encodings remain conservatively\\ntwo-source so the interlock cannot weaken trap-path operand capture. This\\nremoves only false bubbles while retaining the current pipeline, forwarding,\\nmemory timing, RVFI payload, and all true load dependencies.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Export exact uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 signals only from positively validated instruction arms, with conservative two-source defaults for illegal encodings.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the decoder-owned source-use metadata alongside the decoded IF/ID instruction for hazard detection without changing operand or control capture.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the source-use bits from decode to the load-use interlock while preserving existing imem, dmem, divide, and redirect arbitration.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each raw register-number comparison with its corresponding decoder-owned source-use bit and retain the exact one-cycle stall for every live source match.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed load-followed-by tests for each source-free, rs1-only, and two-source encoding, including illegal instructions and genuine dependent branches, stores, and RV32M operations.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Export exact uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 signals only from positively validated instruction arms, with conservative two-source defaults for illegal encodings.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the decoder-owned source-use metadata alongside the decoded IF/ID instruction for hazard detection without changing operand or control capture.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Conne