payload to survive a redirect.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly executes backward conditional loop branches, yet the\\ncurrent EX-stage redirect admits two sequential wrong-path instructions.\\nEarlier predictors either placed decode and target addition on the fetch\\nfeedback path or allowed a sequential fetch payload to survive a redirect.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-ahead registered fetch payload and use static\\nbackward-taken/forward-not-taken prediction only when that payload is\\naccepted by decode as a valid conditional branch. The fetch address always\\nrequests the sequential successor of the registered payload, so normal\\ninstructions retain one-instruction-per-cycle delivery. On an accepted\\npredicted branch, atomically discard that already-fetched sequential word,\\ninstall an invalid payload, and issue the recorded backward target next;\\nthus the target reaches decode as the branch reaches EX without a decode or\\ntarget-adder cone on the PC feedback path. Carry prediction metadata only\\nwith predicted branches and make EX redirect only for that branch's\\ndirection/target mismatch. Give EX recovery priority over predictor\\nrefill, and gate every fill/consume transition with imem readiness and the\\nexisting downstream hold conditions, preserving a one-to-one PC,\\ninstruction, and prediction transaction under stalls.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add fetch-payload validity, PC, and branch-only predicted-successor fields to keep each prediction bound to its decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement the single-ahead registered payload, sequential lookahead fetch, atomic predicted-branch discard, and priority-ordered EX recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize valid backward conditional branches from the registered payload and emit a prediction only on an actual ID/EX acceptance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry branch-only prediction metadata and compare resolved direction and target only for a predicted branch before requesting recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define acceptance, hold, and flush precedence for imem/dmem stalls, load-use stalls, divider ownership, predicted discard, and EX recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire fetch acceptance, branch prediction metadata, and qualified recovery without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed taken-loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem-stall, dmem-stall, and divider-hold tests for atomic sequential-payload discard and RVFI PC order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add fetch-payload validity, PC, and branch-only predicted-successor fields to keep each prediction bound to its decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement the single-ahead registered payload, sequential lookahead fetch, atomic predicted-branch discard, and priority-ordered EX recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize valid backward conditional branches from the registered payload and emit a prediction only on an actual ID/EX acceptance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry branch-only prediction metadata and compare resolved direction and target only for a predicted branch before requesting recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define acceptance, hold, and flush precedence for imem/dmem stalls, load-use stalls, divider ownership, predicted discard, and EX recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire fetch acceptance, branch prediction metadata, and qualified recovery without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed taken-loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem-stall, dmem-stall, and divider-hold tests for atomic sequential-payload discard and RVFI PC order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 358.51, \"delta_pct\": -16.71, \"vs_baseline\": 26.76, \"fmax_mhz\": 167.56, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4673734, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5976, \"ff\": 2334, \"seeds\": [172.83, 167.56, 166.94], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T03:34:09.779966Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12}\n38:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r13s0\", \"title\": \"Share PC-relative target adder\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX control logic forms pc + immediate for branch_target and\\nseparately expresses the same addition as the direct-JAL arm of\\njump_target. This leaves two equivalent wide arithmetic expressions in the\\nhot control cone, despite both consumers requiring the identical result.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX control logic forms pc + immediate for branch_target and\\nseparately expresses the same addition as the direct-JAL arm of\\njump_target. This leaves two equivalent wide arithmetic expressions in the\\nhot control cone, despite both consumers requiring the identical result.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Materialize one pc-relative target wire in EX and use it for both conditional\\nbranch targets and non-JALR jump targets, including the EX/MEM branch-target\\nmetadata. Keep JALR on its independent forwarded rs1 + immediate path and\\nretain the existing misalignment and redirect semantics. Making this common\\nsubexpression explicit should force one carry-chain-friendly adder rather\\nthan duplicate arithmetic and routing, improving Fmax without changing IPC\\nor moving any control decision earlier in the pipeline.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Introduce one explicit pc-relative target adder and route branch, JAL, redirect, EX/MEM metadata, and alignment checks through that shared result; preserve the separate JALR adder and all trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed branch and JAL target cases, including positive and negative offsets plus misaligned targets, to verify shared-target control flow and RVFI PC results.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Introduce one explicit pc-relative target adder and route branch, JAL, redirect, EX/MEM metadata, and alignment checks through that shared result; preserve the separate JALR adder and all trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed branch and JAL target cases, including positive and negative offsets plus misaligned targets, to verify shared-target control flow and RVFI PC results.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 380.36, \"delta_pct\": -11.64, \"vs_baseline\": 34.49, \"fmax_mhz\": 170.85, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5791, \"ff\": 2221, \"seeds\": [170.85, 177.4, 170.39], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T03:45:51.301622Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r13s0 (regression, -11.64%): Explicitly sharing the PC-relative branch/JAL adder can reduce Fmax when the single result must fan out through EX redirect, alignment, and EX/MEM metadata logic, since local duplicated adders may route more cheaply than a high-fanout shared control-cone signal.\"}\n39:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r13s1\", \"title\": \"DSP-backed one-cycle multiplier unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current shared signed 33x33 multiply is the remaining large arithmetic\\nstructure in EX after divide/remainder was moved out of the fast path.\\nBlocking and fabric-partial-product multiplier experiments regressed because\\nthey added issue interlocks and wide LUT reductions. Tang Nano 20K instead\\nprovides dedicated arithmetic resources that can isolate this operation\\nwithout adding architectural latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current shared signed 33x33 multiply is the remaining large arithmetic\\nstructure in EX after divide/remainder was moved out of the fast path.\\nBlocking and fabric-partial-product multiplier experiments regressed because\\nthey added issue interlocks and wide LUT reductions. Tang Nano 20K instead\\nprovides dedicated arithmetic resources that can isolate this operation\\nwithout adding architectural latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the inferred fabric multiply inside the general ALU with a dedicated,\\none-cycle RV32M multiply execution unit explicitly structured for Gowin DSP\\ninference or primitive mapping. The unit will sign-extend operands once,\\ncompose the full product from DSP-sized terms, and select MUL or the required\\nhigh half before the existing EX/MEM register. It remains combinational at\\nthe architectural interface, so dependent instructions, retirement timing,\\nand RVFI payloads are unchanged; only the implementation topology moves the\\nmultiplier off LUT/carry fabric and out of the normal ALU cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the generic 33x33 product from the fast ALU while preserving all non-multiply operations and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mul_dsp.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-cycle RV32M multiplier unit with sign-selected DSP-sized products, full-width reconstruction, MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU selection, and synthesis attributes or supported Gowin primitive mapping.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate the dedicated multiplier beside the fast ALU and select its result only for legal multiply operations without adding a busy state or changing EX/MEM timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed and randomized exact-result tests for all four multiply variants, including signed-boundary and dependent-consumer cases.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the generic 33x33 product from the fast ALU while preserving all non-multiply operations and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mul_dsp.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-cycle RV32M multiplier unit with sign-selected DSP-sized products, full-width reconstruction, MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU selection, and synthesis attributes or supported Gowin primitive mapping.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate the dedicated multiplier beside the fast ALU and select its result only for legal multiply operations without adding a busy state or changing EX/MEM timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed and randomized exact-result tests for all four multiply variants, including signed-boundary and dependent-consumer cases.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 337.88, \"delta_pct\": -21.51, \"vs_baseline\": 19.47, \"fmax_mhz\": 151.77, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5898, \"ff\": 2217, \"seeds\": [166.58, 131.6, 151.77], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T03:50:20.642980Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r13s1 (regression, -21.51%): Moving RV32M multiplication into a separate combinational `mul_dsp` module does not shorten the EX-to-EX/MEM path by itself; without verified DSP mapping, the full product plus result-selection routing can cost more than the original shared ALU cone.\"}\n40:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r13s2\", \"title\": \"Partial-tag backward loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends much of its time on repeatedly taken backward loop branches,\\nbut full BTBs and BTFNT decode have reduced Fmax by making the fetch feedback\\ncone too wide. A much smaller predictor can retain the useful loop behavior\\nwithout placing instruction decode or a full PC tag comparison on that path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends much of its time on repeatedly taken backward loop branches,\\nbut full BTBs and BTFNT decode have reduced Fmax by making the fetch feedback\\ncone too wide. A much smaller predictor can retain the useful loop behavior\\nwithout placing instruction decode or a full PC tag comparison on that path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a four-entry, direct-mapped backward-loop target cache trained only by\\nresolved, valid, taken conditional branches whose target is below their PC.\\nEach entry holds a valid bit, a short PC fragment tag, and its target; fetch\\npredicts taken only on the narrow index-plus-fragment match, selecting the\\nregistered target rather than PC+4. Carry a prediction-valid bit and the\\nselected successor with the fetched instruction. EX remains the sole\\narchitectural resolver and recovers to PC+4 for a predicted alias that is\\nnot a branch, or to the resolved successor for a branch direction/target\\nmismatch. This deliberately permits harmless partial-tag aliases but makes\\ntheir recovery explicit, preserving correctness under symbolic imem while\\navoiding a full tag, counter RAM, or imem-data-to-PC path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a four-entry direct-mapped cache of resolved backward taken branch targets using a narrow PC-fragment tag and EX-only training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry prediction-valid and predicted-successor metadata from IF through ID/EX for branch-qualified recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select the target-cache successor from registered-PC predictor outputs without inspecting io_imemData in the PC feedback path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch fetch prediction metadata atomically with the instruction payload and preserve it across downstream holds.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve every control instruction architecturally, train valid backward taken branches, and redirect predicted non-branches or direction/target mismatches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat predictor recovery as an EX redirect with existing bus-stall, load-use, and divider-hold precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire predictor lookup, EX training, metadata, and recovery while retaining the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Test loop warm-up, final exit, fragment-tag alias to a non-branch, branch-target collision, and imem/dmem stall recovery with RVFI PC order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a four-entry direct-mapped cache of resolved backward taken branch targets using a narrow PC-fragment tag and EX-only training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry prediction-valid and predicted-successor metadata from IF through ID/EX for branch-qualified recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select the target-cache successor from registered-PC predictor outputs without inspecting io_imemData in the PC feedback path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch fetch prediction metadata atomically with the instruction payload and preserve it across downstream holds.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve every control instruction architecturally, train valid backward taken branches, and redirect predicted non-branches or direction/target mismatches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat predictor recovery as an EX redirect with existing bus-stall, load-use, and divider-hold precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire predictor lookup, EX training, metadata, and recovery while retaining the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Test loop warm-up, final exit, fragment-tag alias to a non-branch, branch-target collision, and imem/dmem stall recovery with RVFI PC order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 404.91, \"delta_pct\": -5.93, \"vs_baseline\": 43.17, \"fmax_mhz\": 179.12, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4423715, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6264, \"ff\": 2399, \"seeds\": [179.12, 176.68, 188.64], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T03:48:36.935256Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13}\n41:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r14s0\", \"title\": \"RVFI-safe source-masked load interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock compares both raw register-field positions of every\\nIF/ID word, so immediate fields and source-free instructions can create\\nbubbles after a load. Earlier source-aware attempts failed formal because\\nsuppressing a stall while retaining a pseudo-source let stale data reach\\nthe RVFI source payload.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock compares both raw register-field positions of every\\nIF/ID word, so immediate fields and source-free instructions can create\\nbubbles after a load. Earlier source-aware attempts failed formal because\\nsuppressing a stall while retaining a pseudo-source let stale data reach\\nthe RVFI source payload.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Define validated uses-rs1 and uses-rs2 metadata once for each legal RV32IM\\nopcode/funct combination, then use it in both the load-use interlock and\\nID/EX operand capture. OP, STORE, and BRANCH keep two live sources;\\nOP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR keep rs1 only; JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, EBREAK, and\\ntraps have no live sources. Mask an unused source address and value to x0\\nbefore ID/EX so forwarding and RVFI cannot observe a stale pseudo-source.\\nThis removes only provably false load-use bubbles while preserving every\\ntrue dependency, the existing MEM-to-EX timing boundary, and trap safety.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/source_use.sv\", \"description\": \"Add one validated RV32IM source-use classifier shared by decode capture and hazard logic, with conservative source use for any encoding not explicitly accepted.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use source-use metadata to mask unused rs addresses and data to x0 as ID/EX is captured, keeping forwarding and RVFI source payloads architecturally safe.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each raw-field load-use comparison with the shared source-use result and IF/ID validity, retaining the existing one-cycle interlock for every real consumer.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the IF/ID instruction and source-use qualification into the hazard path without changing the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add load-followed-by-immediate, load-followed-by-source-free, and true rs1/rs2 dependency tests that check retirement and RVFI source fields.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/source_use.sv\", \"description\": \"Add one validated RV32IM source-use classifier shared by decode capture and hazard logic, with conservative source use for any encoding not explicitly accepted.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use source-use metadata to mask unused rs addresses and data to x0 as ID/EX is captured, keeping forwarding and RVFI source payloads architecturally safe.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each raw-field load-use comparison with the shared source-use result and IF/ID validity, retaining the existing one-cycle interlock for every real consumer.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the IF/ID instruction and source-use qualification into the hazard path without changing the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add load-followed-by-immediate, load-followed-by-source-free, and true rs1/rs2 dependency tests that check retirement and RVFI source fields.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 14}\n42:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r14s1\", \"title\": \"Ordered memory-wait retirement queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Random dmem backpressure currently holds EX/MEM, ID/EX, IF, and the\\nretirement boundary whenever a load or store is pending. That turns a\\nshort external memory wait into a whole-pipeline bubble even though later\\nindependent integer operations have already been decoded and can execute.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Random dmem backpressure currently holds EX/MEM, ID/EX, IF, and the\\nretirement boundary whenever a load or store is pending. That turns a\\nshort external memory wait into a whole-pipeline bubble even though later\\nindependent integer operations have already been decoded and can execute.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the coupled EX/MEM-to-MEM/WB handoff with a small in-order\\nretirement queue whose head owns the sole dmem request. A pending load or\\nstore keeps its address, data, and masks stable until io_dmemReady, while\\nyounger non-memory results may enter later queue entries but cannot write\\nthe register file, retire, or bypass an older entry. Commit exactly one\\nready head entry per cycle and generate its RVFI record, register write,\\nand store visibility as one atomic event. Scoreboard dependencies on an\\nunresolved queued producer so only independent work passes a memory wait.\\nThis retains precise RVFI order and prevents early store retirement while\\nconverting common random dmem stalls from full-pipeline freezes into\\nbounded queue backpressure.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define an in-order completion packet and queue state fields, including unresolved memory and ready-to-commit status.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct MEM/WB retirement wiring with ordered queue enqueue, head commit, and RVFI/writeback connections.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Turn memory access into a head-owned request/response producer that holds each request stable until acknowledgement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit non-memory completion packets into the queue and interlock only when the queue or dependency scoreboard requires it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add queue-capacity and unresolved-producer interlocks while preserving redirect, load-use, divide, and bus-stall precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Select only committed or ready older queue results for forwarding, and force consumers of unresolved queued results to wait.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add randomized dmem-stall tests for queued independent ALU work, load/store ordering, store acknowledgement, dependencies, and RVFI order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define an in-order completion packet and queue state fields, including unresolved memory and ready-to-commit status.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct MEM/WB retirement wiring with ordered queue enqueue, head commit, and RVFI/writeback connections.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Turn memory access into a head-owned request/response producer that holds each request stable until acknowledgement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit non-memory completion packets into the queue and interlock only when the queue or dependency scoreboard requires it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add queue-capacity and unresolved-producer interlocks while preserving redirect, load-use, divide, and bus-stall precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Select only committed or ready older queue results for forwarding, and force consumers of unresolved queued results to wait.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add randomized dmem-stall tests for queued independent ALU work, load/store ordering, store acknowledgement, dependencies, and RVFI order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"build_failed: yosys synth: cores/bench/rtl/core.sv:143: ERROR: Index in generate block prefix syntax is not constant!\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 14}\n43:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r14s2\", \"title\": \"Atomic direct JAL target prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The EX-resolved direct JAL path always has a known PC-relative target, yet\\nit currently admits two sequential instructions before recovery. Prior BTB,\\nloop, and RAS predictors lost Fmax to lookup and validation logic; direct\\nJAL needs neither a direction predictor nor register operands.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX-resolved direct JAL path always has a known PC-relative target, yet\\nit currently admits two sequential instructions before recovery. Prior BTB,\\nloop, and RAS predictors lost Fmax to lookup and validation logic; direct\\nJAL needs neither a direction predictor nor register operands.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Predict only validated JAL instructions as they are accepted from the\\nfetch/decode payload. Compute their PC-relative target in decode and make\\nthe PC update an atomic transaction: the JAL itself must advance once into\\nID/EX, while the already-visible sequential payload is invalidated before\\nit can enter ID/EX. An older EX redirect always wins and cancels the decode\\nprediction; JAL is then marked already redirected so EX retains its PC+4\\nwriteback and RVFI pc_wdata but cannot issue a duplicate redirect. This\\ntargets frequent direct calls without putting a BTB, tag match, counter,\\nRAS, or generic predicted-successor comparison on the fetch feedback path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a JAL-only accepted-redirect marker to the fetch and ID/EX transaction payloads, keeping the redirect bound to its issuing instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only legal JAL, form its PC-relative target, and emit a prediction request only when the current fetch payload will advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply an accepted decode JAL redirect atomically after retaining the issuing payload, invalidate the sequential payload, and give older EX recovery priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Preserve JAL link-register and RVFI pc_next behavior while suppressing only the duplicate EX redirect for a decode-predicted JAL.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define precise precedence among EX redirect, dmem and divider holds, imem readiness, load-use bubbles, and accepted JAL prediction so no payload is replayed or leaked.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the JAL prediction request, target, acceptance qualification, and EX-priority recovery without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed direct-JAL, consecutive-JAL, JAL-after-imem-or-dmem-stall, and collision-with-older-EX-redirect tests checking link data and RVFI PC/order continuity.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a JAL-only accepted-redirect marker to the fetch and ID/EX transaction payloads, keeping the redirect bound to its issuing instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only legal JAL, form its PC-relative target, and emit a prediction request only when the current fetch payload will advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply an accepted decode JAL redirect atomically after retaining the issuing payload, invalidate the sequential payload, and give older EX recovery priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Preserve JAL link-register and RVFI pc_next behavior while suppressing only the duplicate EX redirect for a decode-predicted JAL.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define precise precedence among EX redirect, dmem and divider holds, imem readiness, load-use bubbles, and accepted JAL prediction so no payload is replayed or leaked.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the JAL prediction request, target, acceptance qualification, and EX-priority recovery without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed direct-JAL, consecutive-JAL, JAL-after-imem-or-dmem-stall, and collision-with-older-EX-redirect tests checking link data and RVFI PC/order continuity.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 347.24, \"delta_pct\": -19.33, \"vs_baseline\": 22.78, \"fmax_mhz\": 154.25, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4442158, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5749, \"ff\": 2233, \"seeds\": [154.25, 153.75, 170.39], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T04:02:19.447107Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
