r branch-target calculation on the fetch feedback path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a shallow committed return-address stack and predict only canonical\\nreturns (`jalr x0, x1/x5, 0`) in IF. The prediction is just an instruction\\nfield match and a mux of the registered RAS top, avoiding branch-immediate\\nextraction, target addition, tags, and counter RAM on the PC path. Train\\npushes and pops only when the corresponding JAL/JALR has resolved in EX;\\ncarry the predicted next PC to EX and retain existing redirect recovery for\\nany mismatch. Correct returns therefore avoid the existing two younger\\nwrong-path instructions without changing conditional-branch behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/return_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small registered RAS with resolved-call push and resolved-return pop inputs, plus a combinational valid/top-address query interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend fetch and ID/EX payloads with the predicted next-PC metadata needed to validate a return prediction at EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only canonical ra/t0 JALR returns and select the registered RAS top as their predicted next PC; all other instructions keep PC+4.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fetch packet's predicted next PC beside the decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved control-flow next PC with the carried prediction, redirect only on mismatch, and emit ordered call/return RAS update events after validation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat a control-flow prediction mismatch as the flush condition while retaining existing bus, load-use, and divide interlock priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the RAS predictor, fetch metadata, EX validation, and update events without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed nested-call/return, empty-stack, noncanonical-JALR, misprediction-recovery, and imem-stall tests with RVFI PC-order checks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/return_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small registered RAS with resolved-call push and resolved-return pop inputs, plus a combinational valid/top-address query interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend fetch and ID/EX payloads with the predicted next-PC metadata needed to validate a return prediction at EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only canonical ra/t0 JALR returns and select the registered RAS top as their predicted next PC; all other instructions keep PC+4.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fetch packet's predicted next PC beside the decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved control-flow next PC with the carried prediction, redirect only on mismatch, and emit ordered call/return RAS update events after validation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat a control-flow prediction mismatch as the flush condition while retaining existing bus, load-use, and divide interlock priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the RAS predictor, fetch metadata, EX validation, and update events without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed nested-call/return, empty-stack, noncanonical-JALR, misprediction-recovery, and imem-stall tests with RVFI PC-order checks.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 364.95, \"delta_pct\": -9.97, \"vs_baseline\": 29.04, \"fmax_mhz\": 163.43, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4478102, \"iterations