with a negative B\\nimmediate. Treat prediction as an atomic valid-ready transaction: when\\ndecode advances the predicted branch into ID/EX, replace the concurrently\\nissued sequential fetch payload with an invalid entry and redirect the PC\\nto the predicted target. Carry branch-only prediction metadata to EX;\\nEX recovers on a direction or target mismatch, while unpredicted\\ninstructions retain normal PC+4 behavior without a universal successor\\ncomparator. This removes hot loop-back recovery work while keeping\\ninstruction decode and target formation behind the fetch register.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add IF/ID registered-payload and branch-only prediction metadata fields, including the predicted successor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-entry stall-aware IF/ID register whose fill, dequeue, predicted redirect, EX recovery, and invalidation follow one atomic acceptance protocol.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect valid backward conditional branches from the registered payload, form their target, and emit prediction only when the payload advances into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry qualified branch prediction metadata and recover only a resolved predicted branch whose direction or target disagrees.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define ready/hold and redirect precedence so load-use, bus stalls, divider ownership, prediction, and EX recovery cannot consume or retain a wrong-path fetch entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the atomic fetch transaction, prediction metadata, and EX recovery while preserving the existing single-retire RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem/dmem-stall, and divide-hold tests that verify no sequential payload retires after a predicted redirect.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add IF/ID registered-payload and branch-only prediction metadata fields, including the predicted successor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-entry stall-aware IF/ID register whose fill, dequeue, predicted redirect, EX recovery, and invalidation follow one atomic acceptance protocol.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect valid backward conditional branches from the registered payload, form their target, and emit prediction only when the payload advances into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry qualified branch prediction metadata and recover only a resolved predicted branch whose direction or target disagrees.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define ready/hold and redirect precedence so load-use, bus stalls, divider ownership, prediction, and EX recovery cannot consume or retain a wrong-path fetch entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the atomic fetch transaction, prediction metadata, and EX recovery while preserving the existing single-retire RVFI interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem/dmem-stall, and divide-hold tests that verify no sequential payload retires after a predicted redirect.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11}\n37:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r12s2\", \"title\": \"Atomic single-ahead BTFNT predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly executes backward conditional loop branches, yet the\\ncurrent EX-stage redirect admits two sequential wrong-path instructions.\\nEarlier predictors either placed decode and target addition on the fetch\\nfeedback path or allowed a sequential fetch payload to survive a redirect.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark repeatedly executes backward conditional loop branches, yet the\\ncurrent EX-stage redirect admits two sequential wrong-path instructions.\\nEarlier predictors either placed decode and target addition on the fetch\\nfeedback path or allowed a sequential fetch payload to survive a redirect.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-ahead registered fetch payload and use static\\nbackward-taken/forward-not-taken prediction only when that payload is\\naccepted by decode as a valid conditional branch. The fetch address always\\nrequests the sequential successor of the registered payload, so normal\\ninstructions retain one-instruction-per-cycle delivery. On an accepted\\npredicted branch, atomically discard that already-fetched sequential word,\\ninstall an invalid payload, and issue the recorded backward target next;\\nthus the target reaches decode as the branch reaches EX without a decode or\\ntarget-adder cone on the PC feedback path. Carry prediction metadata only\\nwith predicted branches and make EX redirect only for that branch's\\ndirection/target mismatch. Give EX recovery priority over predictor\\nrefill, and gate every fill/consume transition with imem readiness and the\\nexisting downstream hold conditions, preserving a one-to-one PC,\\ninstruction, and prediction transaction under stalls.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add fetch-payload validity, PC, and branch-only predicted-successor fields to keep each prediction bound to its decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement the single-ahead registered payload, sequential lookahead fetch, atomic predicted-branch discard, and priority-ordered EX recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize valid backward conditional branches from the registered payload and emit a prediction only on an actual ID/EX acceptance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry branch-only prediction metadata and compare resolved direction and target only for a predicted branch before requesting recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define acceptance, hold, and flush precedence for imem/dmem stalls, load-use stalls, divider ownership, predicted discard, and EX recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire fetch acceptance, branch prediction metadata, and qualified recovery without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed taken-loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem-stall, dmem-stall, and divider-hold tests for atomic sequential-payload discard and RVFI PC order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add fetch-payload validity, PC, and branch-only predicted-successor fields to keep each prediction bound to its decoded instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement the single-ahead registered payload, sequential lookahead fetch, atomic predicted-branch discard, and priority-ordered EX recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize valid backward conditional branches from the registered payload and emit a prediction only on an actual ID/EX acceptance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry branch-only prediction metadata and compare resolved direction and target only for a predicted branch before requesting recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define acceptance, hold, and flush precedence for imem/dmem stalls, load-use stalls, divider ownership, predicted discard, and EX recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire fetch acceptance, branch prediction metadata, and qualified recovery without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed taken-loop, final-exit, forward-branch, imem-stall, dmem-stall, and divider-hold tests for atomic sequential-payload discard and RVFI PC order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 358.51, \"delta_pct\": -16.71, \"vs_baseline\": 26.76, \"fmax_mhz\": 167.56, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4673734, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5976, \"ff\": 2334, \"seeds\": [172.83, 167.56, 166.94], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T03:34:09.779966Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12}\n40:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r13s2\", \"title\": \"Partial-tag backward loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends much of its time on repeatedly taken backward loop branches,\\nbut full BTBs and BTFNT decode have reduced Fmax by making the fetch feedback\\ncone too wide. A much smaller predictor can retain the useful loop behavior\\nwithout placing instruction decode or a full PC tag comparison on that path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends much of its time on repeatedly taken backward loop branches,\\nbut full BTBs and BTFNT decode have reduced Fmax by making the fetch feedback\\ncone too wide. A much smaller predictor can retain the useful loop behavior\\nwithout placing instruction decode or a full PC tag comparison on that path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a four-entry, direct-mapped backward-loop target cache trained only by\\nresolved, valid, taken conditional branches whose target is below their PC.\\nEach entry holds a valid bit, a short PC fragment tag, and its target; fetch\\npredicts taken only on the narrow index-plus-fragment match, selecting the\\nregistered target rather than PC+4. Carry a prediction-valid bit and the\\nselected successor with the fetched instruction. EX remains the sole\\narchitectural resolver and recovers to PC+4 for a predicted alias that is\\nnot a branch, or to the resolved successor for a branch direction/target\\nmismatch. This deliberately permits harmless partial-tag aliases but makes\\ntheir recovery explicit, preserving correctness under symbolic imem while\\navoiding a full tag, counter RAM, or imem-data-to-PC path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a four-entry direct-mapped cache of resolved backward taken branch targets using a narrow PC-fragment tag and EX-only training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry prediction-valid and predicted-successor metadata from IF through ID/EX for branch-qualified recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select the target-cache successor from registered-PC predictor outputs without inspecting io_imemData in the PC feedback path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch fetch prediction metadata atomically with the instruction payload and preserve it across downstream holds.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve every control instruction architecturally, train valid backward taken branches, and redirect predicted non-branches or direction/target mismatches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat predictor recovery as an EX redirect with existing bus-stall, load-use, and divider-hold precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire predictor lookup, EX training, metadata, and recovery while retaining the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Test loop warm-up, final exit, fragment-tag alias to a non-branch, branch-target collision, and imem/dmem stall recovery with RVFI PC order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a four-entry direct-mapped cache of resolved backward taken branch targets using a narrow PC-fragment tag and EX-only training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry prediction-valid and predicted-successor metadata from IF through ID/EX for branch-qualified recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select the target-cache successor from registered-PC predictor outputs without inspecting io_imemData in the PC feedback path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch fetch prediction metadata atomically with the instruction payload and preserve it across downstream holds.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve every control instruction architecturally, train valid backward taken branches, and redirect predicted non-branches or direction/target mismatches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat predictor recovery as an EX redirect with existing bus-stall, load-use, and divider-hold precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire predictor lookup, EX training, metadata, and recovery while retaining the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Test loop warm-up, final exit, fragment-tag alias to a non-branch, branch-target collision, and imem/dmem stall recovery with RVFI PC order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 404.91, \"delta_pct\": -5.93, \"vs_baseline\": 43.17, \"fmax_mhz\": 179.12, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4423715, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6264, \"ff\": 2399, \"seeds\": [179.12, 176.68, 188.64], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T03:48:36.935256Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13}\n43:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r14s2\", \"title\": \"Atomic direct JAL target prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The EX-resolved direct JAL path always has a known PC-relative target, yet\\nit currently admits two sequential instructions before recovery. Prior BTB,\\nloop, and RAS predictors lost Fmax to lookup and validation logic; direct\\nJAL needs neither a direction predictor nor register operands.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX-resolved direct JAL path always has a known PC-relative target, yet\\nit currently admits two sequential instructions before recovery. Prior BTB,\\nloop, and RAS predictors lost Fmax to lookup and validation logic; direct\\nJAL needs neither a direction predictor nor register operands.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Predict only validated JAL instructions as they are accepted from the\\nfetch/decode payload. Compute their PC-relative target in decode and make\\nthe PC update an atomic transaction: the JAL itself must advance once into\\nID/EX, while the already-visible sequential payload is invalidated before\\nit can enter ID/EX. An older EX redirect always wins and cancels the decode\\nprediction; JAL is then marked already redirected so EX retains its PC+4\\nwriteback and RVFI pc_wdata but cannot issue a duplicate redirect. This\\ntargets frequent direct calls without putting a BTB, tag match, counter,\\nRAS, or generic predicted-successor comparison on the fetch feedback path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a JAL-only accepted-redirect marker to the fetch and ID/EX transaction payloads, keeping the redirect bound to its issuing instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only legal JAL, form its PC-relative target, and emit a prediction request only when the current fetch payload will advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply an accepted decode JAL redirect atomically after retaining the issuing payload, invalidate the sequential payload, and give older EX recovery priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Preserve JAL link-register and RVFI pc_next behavior while suppressing only the duplicate EX redirect for a decode-predicted JAL.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define precise precedence among EX redirect, dmem and divider holds, imem readiness, load-use bubbles, and accepted JAL prediction so no payload is replayed or leaked.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the JAL prediction request, target, acceptance qualification, and EX-priority recovery without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed direct-JAL, consecutive-JAL, JAL-after-imem-or-dmem-stall, and collision-with-older-EX-redirect tests checking link data and RVFI PC/order continuity.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a JAL-only accepted-redirect marker to the fetch and ID/EX transaction payloads, keeping the redirect bound to its issuing instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only legal JAL, form its PC-relative target, and emit a prediction request only when the current fetch payload will advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply an accepted decode JAL redirect atomically after retaining the issuing payload, invalidate the sequential payload, and give older EX recovery priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Preserve JAL link-register and RVFI pc_next behavior while suppressing only the duplicate EX redirect for a decode-predicted JAL.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Define precise precedence among EX redirect, dmem and divider holds, imem readiness, load-use bubbles, and accepted JAL prediction so no payload is replayed or leaked.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the JAL prediction request, target, acceptance qualification, and EX-priority recovery without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed direct-JAL, consecutive-JAL, JAL-after-imem-or-dmem-stall, and collision-with-older-EX-redirect tests checking link data and RVFI PC/order continuity.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 347.24, \"delta_pct\": -19.33, \"vs_baseline\": 22.78, \"fmax_mhz\": 154.25, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4442158, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5749, \"ff\": 2233, \"seeds\": [154.25, 153.75, 170.39], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T04:02:19.447107Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
